04:17:25','黄茶 / 车前草黄茶 / 红参黄茶 / 地黄黄茶 / 普洱茶 / 五味子茶等','可以','全年无休','2025-10-29 15:22:40'),(705,796,'zh','花郎之丘(화랑의언덕)','◎ 邂逅韩流魅力的旅游信息 - 《坏妈妈》 强豪和邻居孩子们玩耍的草原在社交媒体上被选为热门拍照地点。爬上悬崖尽头的一块名为&ldquo;冥想岩&rdquo;的岩石，脚下是雅致的村庄和梯田。山坡上宽阔的草坪和平静的水库相映成趣，可以尽情享受平静的风景。这里可以散步和野餐，但不允许野营和汽车露营。','庆尚北道庆州市山内面守义街601号','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:29','2026-09-14 15:23:29',NULL,'可以','全年无休','2025-10-28 16:19:31'),(706,813,'zh','道里村银杏树林(도리마을은행나무숲)','这片深林遍布银杏树，十分茂密。每至秋天，银杏叶就会染黄树林，景色蔚为壮观，成为婚纱摄影的圣地。这里是剧中强豪找到双胞胎弹力球的场所，让我们漫步在村庄，读一读路墙上的精彩语句，在银杏树林中留下人生照吧。','庆尚北道庆州市西面道里35-102号','00:00~24:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:29','2026-09-14 15:23:29',NULL,'可以','全年无休','2025-10-28 10:24:32'),(707,883,'zh','庆州皇理团路(경주 황리단길)','皇理团路是指皇南洞鲍石路一带被叫做&ldquo;皇南大路&rdquo;的胡同。作为皇南洞与首尔梨泰院经理团路合二为一的新名词，具有&ldquo;皇南洞经理团路&rdquo;之意。由传统韩屋改建而成的美食店、咖啡馆、照相馆、商店等汇聚此处，备受MZ世代年轻人的欢迎。街道和建筑物等到处充满复古风，皇理团路保存着的20世纪六七十年代的老建筑，更是令人原封不动地感受到当时的氛围，十分有魅力。附近有瞻星台、大陵苑等庆州代表性景点，交通便利，是庆州旅游的必访路线。作为新兴景点，备受瞩目。','庆尚北道庆州市鲍石路1080 (황남동)','各商店各异',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:30','2026-09-14 15:23:30',NULL,'有','全年无休(各商店各异)','2025-10-27 13:45:24'),(708,160,'zh','瑶石宫1779요석궁1779','建于新罗武烈王女儿瑶石公主旧居的瑶石宫餐厅是朝鲜时代庆州崔富者买地后建造的一家传统韩定食餐厅。目前由其子孙经营，历经十二代传承的手艺，让这里的菜品味道堪称一流。&ldquo;坚持使用有机食品作为食材，不过多加入化学调味品&rdquo;是这家饭店的经营哲学。','庆尚北道庆州市校村内路19-4(校洞)','12:00 ~ 21:00 (休息时间 16:00~17:30 / 最后点餐 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:30','2026-09-16 04:17:23','参甲鱼 / 天美等','可以停车','每周二，节日当天','2025-09-02 09:27:56'),(709,859,'zh','庆州乡校(경주향교)','庆州乡校位于庆州校村与崔富者宅附近，附近之所以被称为校村、校里、校洞，都是因乡校的缘故。这里千年来都是学习之处，最早可追溯到新罗神文王2年(682)在此首度兴建的国学。如今这里已不具备教育功能，作为祭祀之处，每年春秋两季举办传统的儒教祭礼仪式释奠大祭。此外，在庆州乡校也提供国弓、捣年糕、茶道等传统文化体验和每年4~10月期间明伦堂的传统婚礼免费体验的示范婚礼活动。','庆尚北道庆州市校村內街27-20 (校洞)','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:30','2026-09-14 15:23:30',NULL,'无(月精桥公营停车场)','全年无休','2025-06-23 15:10:14'),(710,80,'zh','奉吉大王岩海边(봉길대왕암해변)','位于庆州市东32km大钟河口的 奉吉大王岩海水浴场，沙滩长500m、宽40m，海水浴场开放时平均水温为22℃。与东海岸其他海水浴场相比，这里避暑客稀少，适合享受静逸悠闲的假期。 周边有感恩寺址、感恩寺塔、祇林寺、禅武道之本山骨窟寺、龙渊等古迹。','庆尚北道庆州市阳北面奉吉海岸街','全天开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:31','2026-09-16 04:17:23',NULL,'有','全年无休','2025-06-19 16:41:58'),(711,816,'zh','佛理团路(불리단길)','庆州佛理团路，其名称来源于佛国寺+首尔经理团路，是庆州新兴热门旅游景区。范围主要指庆州进岘路一带的胡同内，布满着佛国寺商街市场，一直连接到吐含山下村的店家。 这里综合文化空间Road22户外活动，艺术集市、工坊、艺廊等各种体验活动不断，与美食店、咖啡厅等一起，丰富访客的脚步。佛国寺邮局旁的壁画街，还会给人以没有屋顶的美术馆之错觉，美不胜收。','庆尚北道庆州市佛国新宅地5街11 (进岘洞)','各店铺不同',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:31','2026-09-16 04:17:25',NULL,'有','各店铺不同','2025-06-19 16:39:46'),(712,1011,'zh','庆州世界文化EXPO纪念馆(경주세계문화엑스포 기념관)','庆州世界文化EXPO纪念馆由世界建筑巨匠设计而成，其设计灵感源于庆州大陵苑与柱状节理。这里收藏了韩国、中国知名艺术家的珍贵作品，食客共享并体验艺术乐趣的综合性文化空间。整个纪念馆由精彩的展览空间和各种主题空间构成，期待访客的到访和探索。','庆尚北道庆州市镜鑑路614 (千军洞)','10:00~18:00 ※ 夏季延长运营(具体事项请参考主页)','成人 12,000韩元','2026-09-14 15:23:31','2026-09-14 15:23:31',NULL,'可以','全年无休','2025-05-22 11:13:15'),(713,993,'zh','国立庆州博物馆新罗千年书库(국립경주박물관 신라천년서고)','开馆于2022年12月15日的新罗千年书库， 是可阅览博物馆收藏图书的博物馆内附属图书馆设施。图书馆的前身&mdash;博物馆库房，在维持其仿韩屋形态的外观基础上，以现代化的方式对内部进行装潢整修。这里不仅有国立庆州博物馆至今为止发行的图书，还典藏了国内外展览图录、新罗及庆州学相关图书等。还设有图书策展室，陈列各种主题图书并举办相关活动。','庆尚北道庆州市仁旺洞 76','10:00~18:00','免费','2026-09-14 15:23:31','2026-09-14 15:23:31',NULL,'可以 (国立庆州博物馆停车场)','每周六，日 /公休日','2025-05-22 11:08:53'),(714,172,'zh','皇南饼(황남빵)','庆州皇南饼之名始于1939年。来买面包的人们被告知，在庆州皇南洞制成的这种面包叫皇南饼。该名称流传至今，并成为正式名称。皇南饼创始人已故崔荣华先生作为庆州崔氏子孙，21岁那年在经历千辛万苦之后，终于制做出了皇南饼。他发展代代相传利用豆沙制做年糕和饼的传统，采用特别秘方制做皇南饼，80多年来至今仅采用豆沙来打造美味。皇南饼的另一大特点是拥有秀丽的窗户斜格子图案，能令人感受到新罗的氛围。','경상북도 경주시 태종로 783 (황오동)','08:00 ~ 22:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:32','2026-09-14 15:23:32','皇南饼 / 皇南饼','有','年中无休','2025-03-27 13:19:34'),(715,100,'zh','庆州蔬菜包饭一条街（경주 쌈밥거리）','在庆州大陵苑周边形成的饮食街。蔬菜包饭是将鲜美的鱼、肉、用家制大酱煮的大酱汤等丰盛的配菜，拿新鲜的包肉蔬菜包着享用的美食。在蔬菜包饭一条街，还可以品尝到皇南饼（在面团中放入红豆的面包）、辣条（用玉米粉和糖做的零食）等多种多样的零食。周边景点有瞻星台、东宫与月池、月精桥和国立庆州博物馆。','庆尚北道庆州市鸡林路9','依餐厅而异',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:32','2026-09-14 15:23:32',NULL,'有（大陵苑停车场、餐厅停车场）','依餐厅而异','2025-03-27 11:33:35'),(716,882,'zh','庆州普门旅游区(경주 보문관광단지)','&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 庆州普门旅游区占地面积约1033公顷(总面积323万坪)，距离庆州室内约10公里左右，以湖为中心，是一处综合性的温泉区及观光特区，各种设施健全，是具有国际标准的修养、旅游风景区。 普门旅游区内有国际会议场即观光中心、高尔夫球场、综合性商店、旅游饭店等设施，都按韩国传统的形式建造。还有游船停泊处、六府村、Sonje美术馆、普门露天舞台、汽车剧院、庆州世界等娱乐设施。普门景区沿路樱花树茂密，4月时樱花绽开，园内成为粉红色的一片雪地。微风袭来时，粉红色的花朵似乎是充满了魔力，让游客们的脸上不由自主地浮现出微笑。','庆尚北道庆州市新坪洞','随时开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:32','2026-09-14 15:23:32',NULL,'可以停车','年中无休','2025-03-27 11:31:29'),(717,155,'zh','庆州中央市场(경주 중앙시장)','1983年建立的庆州中央市场位于庆尚北道庆州市金城路295号(城乾洞)，庆州人都喜欢将其称为下面市场。整个市场面积11.053㎡，拥有11栋建筑、700多家店铺和100多个路边摊，是一处规模较大的传统市场。','庆尚北道庆州市金城路295','05:00 ~ 22:30',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:32','2026-09-14 15:23:32',NULL,'可以停车','每月1日, 15日定期休息','2025-03-27 11:27:59'),(718,803,'zh','庆州石窟庵[联合国教科文组织世界遗产](경주 석굴암 [유네스코 세계유산])','※ 2019_2020 韩国观光100选 ※ 石窟庵作为韩国第24号国宝，始建于新罗景德王10年，由当时的宰相金大城主持修建。从佛国寺沿山路走3Km，再沿公路走9km便可到达。石窟庵由方形和圆形、直线和曲线、平面和球面等造型各异的岩壁佛像雕塑34尊组成，每尊佛像都堪称是一部杰作，融汇了哲学与科学两种思想。其中，位于正中央，由白色花岗岩打造而成的如来本尊坐像俯视着东海。 石窟庵1995年被联合国教科文组织指定为世界文化遗产。主室呈圆形，内有本尊像等菩萨及其弟子雕像。石窟庵正是为了供奉本尊像而建造的。本尊像坐在莲花宝座之上，姿态文雅，表情慈祥。石窟庵的屋顶呈半月形或弓形，上有莲花纹的圆盘为盖。这里日出的景色十分美丽，因此有许多游客都在清晨前往石窟庵。','庆尚北道庆州市石窟路238石窟庵','09:00 ~18:00 (退场时间 19:00)',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:33','2026-09-14 15:23:33',NULL,'可以停车','年中无休','2025-03-27 11:14:13'),(719,806,'zh','庆州良洞村(世界教科文组织指定世界遗产)경주 양동마을 [유네스코 세계유산]','良洞民俗村是朝鲜时代传统文化与自然相结合的典范，是韩国规模最大的村落，由月城孙氏和骊江李氏建立。村庄内的国宝、宝物、民俗资料丰富，整个村落被指定为重要民俗材料第189号。由于村庄规模宏大，保存状态良好，文化财数量多，传统色彩浓重，自然环境优秀等特点，在1993年，英国的查尔斯王子曾来访于此。 作为良洞天然背景雪仓山的文章峰，其山脊向四方延伸的部分与山谷形成了一个&ldquo;勿&rdquo;字的形态，每个山脊与山谷上，若连无人居住的房子也算上，拥有500余年历史的传统韵味十足的古宅和草房共有160多处，间或隐藏在密林之中。其中年头在200年以上的古街54号，保存完整，在这里可以将朝鲜中期韩国丰富多彩的特色屋舍一览无余。 建议游客在去这里旅游之前，事先对行程路线进行安排，了解下关于这里文化财的背景知识，以便更好地进行实地考察。但请尽量在参观村庄时，不要对当地的村民进行过多的打扰。 2010年7月31日，安东河回村和庆州的良洞村，作为韩国历史村落被世界教科文组织指定为世界遗产。韩国目前拥有的世界遗产除此之外，还有石窟庵ㆍ佛国寺、海印寺藏经板殿、宗庙、昌德宫、水原华城、庆州历史遗迹地区、高敞ㆍ和顺ㆍ江华古人墓遗迹、济州火山岛和熔岩石窟、朝鲜王陵等共10处。 * 良洞村的国家遗产 1) 国宝1件 - 通鉴续编 283号 2) 宝物4件 &ndash; 无添堂 411号、香坛 412号、观稼亭，442号、孙昭影帧 1216号 3) 重要民俗资料12件 &ndash; 书百堂 23号、乐善堂 73号、沙湖堂 74号、赏春轩 75号、谨庵古宅 76号、杜谷古宅 77号、守拙堂 78号、二香亭 79号、水云亭 80号、心水亭 81号、安乐亭 82号、讲学堂 83号 4)庆尚北道指定文化财7件 ▶有形文化遗产 &ndash; 敌忾功臣论赏录券 13号、孙昭先生分财记 14号 ▶纪念物 &ndash; 良洞的桧柏 8号 ▶ 民俗资料 &ndash; 对圣轩 34号 ▶ 文化遗产资料 &ndash; 孙宗老旌忠碑阁 261号 ▶ 乡土文化遗产 &ndash; 景山书堂、杜谷影堂','庆尚北道庆州市江东面良洞村路134 (江东面)','夏季（4~9月）：09:00~19:00 冬季（10~3月）：09:00~18:00 ※虽没有指定的观览时间，但为了保护附近居民的生活观览时有限制',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:33','2026-09-14 15:23:33',NULL,'临时停车场','年中无休','2025-03-27 11:10:34'),(720,69,'zh','庆州历史遗迹地区[联合国教科文组织世界遗产]경주역사유적지구[유네스코 세계유산]','于2000年11月被载入联合国教科文组织世界文化遗产录的庆州历史遗址地区是完整保存新罗(57-935)古都“庆州”历史与文化的地区。 这里按照遗迹的类型共分为5大区域，第一个区域是新罗佛教美术的宝库-南山地区。庆州南山被称为户外博物馆，在这里可以看到鉴证新罗王朝建立及没落的历史遗迹，其中主要有鲍石亭(史迹第1号)、塔谷磨崖雕像群(宝物第201号)、天龙寺址三层石塔(宝物第188号)、七佛庵磨崖石佛(宝物第200号) 、佛谷石佛坐像(宝物第198号)等37个佛教遗址。 第二个区域是新罗千年王朝的宫阙-月城地区。其中包含鸡林(史迹第19号)、新罗王宫的别宫东宫和月池(史迹第18号)、以及东洋首屈一指的观星设施瞻星台(国宝第31号)。第三个地区则是新罗王与王妃贵族的古坟群分布地区-大陵苑地区。这里按区域划分分为路东里古坟群(史迹第38号)、路西里古坟群(史迹第39号)、皇南里古坟群(史迹第40号)、五陵(史迹第172号)、财买井(史迹第162号)等， 挖掘古坟时所发现的珍贵文物有金冠、天马图、各种土器等，通过这些遗物可以让游客更加充分地了解当时的文化。 第四个区域是浓缩了新罗佛教文化精髓的皇龙寺地区，这里保存了皇龙寺(史迹第6号)与芬皇寺石塔。第五一区域是王京防御设施的核心山城地区，据推测它属于400年前堆砌的明活山城(史迹第47号)。 庆州历史遗址地区共有52个地方文化财入选为世界文化遗产。 * 南山地区(史迹第311号) 菩提寺磨崖石佛(地方有形文化财第193号) 弥勒谷石佛坐像(宝物第136号) 茸长寺谷三层石塔(宝物第186号) 石佛坐像(宝物第187号) 茸长寺址磨崖如来坐像(宝物第91号) 天龙寺址三层石塔(宝物第1188号) 南涧寺址幢竿支柱(宝物第909号) 南涧寺址石井(地方文化财资料第13号) 庆州南山里三层石塔(宝物第124号) 庆州拜里石佛立像(宝物第63号) 润乙谷磨崖佛坐像(地方有形文化财第195号) 三陵(史迹第219号) 佛谷石佛坐像(宝物第198号) 神仙庵磨崖菩萨半跏像(宝物第199号) 七佛庵磨崖石佛(宝物第200号) 塔谷磨崖雕像群(宝物第201号) 三陵溪石佛坐像(宝物第666号) 三陵溪谷磨崖观音菩萨像(地方有形文化财第19号) 三陵溪谷磨崖石迦如来坐像/线刻如来坐像(地方有形文化财第158号/159号) 三陵溪谷线刻六尊佛(地方有形文化财第21号) 笠谷石佛头(地方有形文化财第94号) 寝息谷石佛坐像(地方有形文化财第112号) 列岩谷石佛坐像(地方有形文化财第113号) 药水溪谷磨崖立佛像(地方有形文化财第114号) 白云台磨崖石佛立像(地方有形文化财第206号) 鲍石亭址(史迹第1号) 庆州南山城(史迹第22号) 书出池(史迹第138号) 新罗逸圣王陵(史迹第173号) 新罗定康王陵(史迹第186号) 新罗宪康王陵(史迹第187号) 新罗奈勿王陵(史迹第188号) 袛摩王陵(史迹第221号) 景哀王陵(史迹第222号) 庆州萝井(史迹第245号) 庆州南山洞石造龛室(地方有形文化财第6号) * 月城地区 鸡林(史迹第19号) 庆州月城(史迹第16号) 临海殿址(史迹第8号) 瞻星台(国宝第31号) 奈勿王陵鸡林月城地带(史迹与名胜第2号) * 大陵苑地区 味邹王陵(史迹第175号) 皇南里古坟群(史迹第40号) 路东里古坟群(史迹第38号) 路西里古坟群(史迹第39号) 五陵(史迹第172号) 东部史迹地带(史迹第161号) 财买井(史迹第246号) * 皇龙寺地区 皇龙寺址(史迹第6号) 芬皇寺石塔(国宝第30号) * 山城地区 明活山城(史迹第47号)','庆尚北道庆州市太宗路757(路东洞)一带 (路东洞)一带','各设施不同',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:33','2026-09-16 04:17:26',NULL,'可用','各设施不同','2025-03-27 11:03:18'),(721,832,'zh','皇龙院(황룡원)','皇龙院寺将历史上新罗时代皇龙寺九层塔样式的中道塔，以现代科学技术与建筑工法重新诠释并建成的特色建筑。这里如今是远近有名的庆州普门园区的新地标，也是针对个人及企业推出各种冥想与修行活动的修炼院，还设有住宿设施。在庆州世界文化EXPO公园内的玫瑰花园望到的皇龙院全景尤为美丽。','庆尚北道庆州市EXPO路40 (신평동)','[住宿] 入住 - 15:00 退房 -次日 10:00 [餐厅] 早餐 - 07:30~09:00 中餐 - 11:30~13:30 晚餐 - 17:30~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:33','2026-09-14 15:23:33',NULL,'可以','全年无休','2025-03-21 15:44:13'),(722,802,'zh','庆州月城(半月城) （경주 월성(반월성)）','&nbsp;&nbsp; 半月城是从西元101年婆娑王22年建造的新罗王城，在西元935年遭到毁灭。其地形貌似弦月，故而又被称为新月城。因为它是王居住的城，又被称为在城。而从朝鲜时代至今人们将其称为半月城。 &nbsp;&nbsp; 月城是由石头和泥土筑成的，长1841米，面积为193,585平方米。东部有东宫临海殿和雁鸭池相连，北有瞻星台，南有护城小溪。据记载，这里的门分为南门、归正门、北门、仁和门、玄德门、武平门、临海门，阁楼则有月上楼、忘德楼、鸣鹤楼、鼓楼；殿有朝元殿、崇礼殿、平议殿、南堂、月正堂、右司禄馆、左司禄馆、玲阁省等，宫有宫东宫、月池宫、永昌宫、内黄殿等。目前的月城地下铺有青铜器时代的无文土器、统一新罗时代的土器、瓦片和建筑物基石等。 &nbsp;&nbsp; 据说在建城之前，名为瓠公的人，在昔脱解王年幼时，企图占领此地。南解王闻听此事之后，便将昔脱解王招为女婿，使之成为新罗第四代王。此后在婆娑王22年(西元101年)将城移至此地后，历代王室便都住在月城。','庆尚北道庆州市蚊川路47(仁王洞)附近','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:34','2026-09-16 04:17:23',NULL,'请使用国立中央博物馆或雁鸭池停车场','年中无休','2025-01-03 11:45:18'),(723,810,'zh','统一殿银杏路（통일전 은행나무길）','位于统一殿（为纪念新罗三国统一业绩而建的建筑）前长约2公里的林荫道，作为庆州市的代表性秋季名胜，其道路两侧是伸展开的一排排银杏树，一到秋天，成片的金黄十分耀眼。可以享受兜风路线或散步的乐趣，也可以在统一殿楼阁上欣赏银杏路全貌。','庆尚北道庆州市七佛庵街6','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:34','2026-09-16 04:17:25',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-12-20 17:01:51'),(724,834,'zh','庆州感恩寺址(경주 감은사지)','感恩寺是新罗第30代王文武大王完成三国统一大业后，为了借助佛祖的庇佑赶走海盗的侵袭而开始修建，但文武王在寺庙还没建成时就已驾崩。他的儿子神文王依据遗言，在即位的第二年将该寺庙修建而成。文武王临死前留有遗言，希望自己死后化为海中之龙，继续保卫祖国，神文王依其父亲所言，将文武王葬于大王陵，并将为其父而建的寺庙称为感恩寺。 目前的寺庙是在1792年通过两年考察研究，依据当时建筑物的风格模仿而建的。并且还在金堂之下发现了象征文武王成为海龙的特殊构造及东侧通路的痕迹。寺中高耸的两座三层石塔建于统一新罗时代，为可分割成数十个部分的组装式结构，高13.4米，是新罗三层石塔中规模最大的一处。','庆尚北道庆州市阳北面龙堂里55-1','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:34','2026-09-16 04:17:23',NULL,'可以停车','年中无休','2024-12-17 17:11:16'),(725,890,'zh','罗亭沙滩海边나정고운모래해변','宽广的细沙和东海的蔚蓝海域，充裕的周边设施和宽广的空间，还有利用东海海水制作的温泉池，让您感受到全新的体验。温泉旁还有开放的停车场和松林。另外，还可以搭乘电动小艇，香蕉船等水上娱乐设施。 * 白沙滩 – 长 0.5㎞, 宽 40∼90ｍ','庆尚北道庆州市甘浦邑东海岸路1915','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:35','2026-09-16 04:17:23',NULL,'有(100辆)','全年无休','2024-12-09 11:12:21'),(726,833,'zh','庆州阳南柱状节理展望台（경주 양남 주상절리 전망대）','被指定为国家地质公园的阳南柱状节理群建于2017年10月，是可将海洋四周景色尽收眼帘的展望台。阳南柱状节理是顺着阳南面邑川里海岸而发达起来的柱状节理群，可以观察到冲向天空的柱状节理、扇子形状的柱状节理、倾斜状、卧状等多种形态的柱状节理。其中最惹眼的是扇子模样圆圆展开的柱状节理。在世界范畴内属于罕见、珍贵的形态，于2012年9月被指定为天然纪念物。柱状节理展望台内还会进行地质资源相关的展示活动，还有常驻地质解说员为游客提供讲解服务。','庆尚北道庆州市阳南面东海岸路498-13','09:00~18:00 (入场截止17:00)',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:35','2026-09-16 04:17:24',NULL,'可用','每周一','2024-12-02 13:24:30'),(727,868,'zh','芬皇寺（분황사）','这是一座位于庆州皇龙寺遗址旁的新罗时代寺庙，始建于634年。可以见到被指定为国宝的模砖石塔、被登记为有形文化遗产的和诤国师碑趺等文化遗产。这是一座历史悠久的大型寺庙，但蒙古的侵略和壬辰倭乱等战争导致大部分寺庙被毁，只剩下普光殿等少量建筑物和寺庙遗址。附近坐落着皇龙寺历史文化馆。','庆尚北道庆州市芬皇路94-11','08:00~18:00（冬季 17:00为止）',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:35','2026-09-14 15:23:35',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-02-29 10:34:35'),(728,64,'zh','庆州鸟园（경주 버드파크）','这是一座位于普门旅游区的鸟类观赏公园，被建成鸟巢状的流线形。拥有250种900只鸟类和花草等各种动植物，是一个可以亲手触摸鸟类并一起玩耍的体验教育场。一楼是生态体验馆，有鸟类、爬行动物、鱼类和小动物等，二楼是展览馆和露天体验场。','庆尚北道庆州市普门路74-14','10:00~19:00（入场截止时间：营业结束1小时前）',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:35','2026-09-14 15:23:35',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-02-28 10:25:38'),(729,835,'zh','庆州国立公园（경주국립공원）','作为韩国唯一一座史迹型公园，1968年被指定为国立公园。占地136.55平方公里，共有8个区，包括佛教文化的翘楚&ldquo;佛国寺&rdquo;、怀抱着石窟庵的吐含山和被称为&ldquo;佛教博物馆&rdquo;的南山等，拥有新罗遗址和美丽的自然风光。1979年被联合国教科文组织指定为世界十大遗址之一，是世界公认的遗址。','庆尚北道庆州市川北南路12','石窟庵 09:00~17:00 / 佛国寺 09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:36','2026-09-14 15:23:36',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-02-27 17:49:44'),(730,889,'zh','庆州民俗工艺村（경주민속공예촌）','这座民俗工艺村位于庆州吐含山山麓，由40多间草房和瓦房组成，均为韩国传统房屋。身怀传统艺术和工艺技术的工匠们聚集在一起，生产和销售陶瓷、木材、珠宝、韩服和石工艺品等，还运营体验项目。在村子里的新罗历史科学馆里可以看到新罗时代的文物，附近有普门旅游区、佛国寺和石窟庵等景点。','庆尚北道庆州市普佛路230','11月~2月 09:00~17:00 / 3月~10月 09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:37','2026-09-14 15:23:37',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-02-27 16:51:53'),(731,147,'zh','花郎教育院（화랑교육원）','作为韩国最初的人性教育机构，旨在继承新罗花郎（青少年武士组织）之魂，培养正确的品性与人格，设施包括花郎馆、操场、礼堂、安全体验馆等。安全体验馆由地震体验室、生命尊重室、4D影像室等构成，可接受到有关保健、犯罪、自然灾难等有效的预防性安全教育。周边景点有国立庆州博物馆、定康王陵、庆北千年林庭园和景哀王陵。','庆尚北道庆州市新南山街62','09:00~17:00','免费','2026-09-14 15:23:37','2026-09-14 15:23:37',NULL,'有','周六、周日、公休日','2024-02-23 10:47:05'),(732,792,'zh','隍城公园（황성공원）','位于庆州市立图书馆和庆州室内体育馆附近的公园，威风凛凛的松树和拥有数百年树龄的古木郁郁葱葱。每逢夏日，会形成麦门冬群落；到了秋天，榉树和橡树古木便会披上美丽的秋衣，景色美不胜收。公园内有金庾信将军骑马像、国弓场和摔跤场。周边景点有庆州邑城、天马冢、大陵苑和皇理团路。','庆尚北道庆州市源花路431-12','常年开放',NULL,'2026-09-14 15:23:37','2026-09-14 15:23:37',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-02-23 10:43:08'),(733,808,'en','Gyeongju Daereungwon Ancient Tomb Complex (경주 대릉원 일원)','Gyeongju Daereungwon Tomb Complex consists of five tombs, Ancient Tombs of Gyeongju Nodong-ri, Noseo-ri, Hwangnam-ri, Hwango-ri, and Inwang-ri. The tombs are distributed in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju-si, and are located in the Daereungwon area. Within Daereungwon Tomb Complex is Cheonmachong Tomb, which was excavated in 1973. Furthermore, Hwangnamdaechong Tomb was excavated between 1973 and 1975, and is a set of twin tombs belonging to a presumed married couple. ◎ Hallyu Travel Information - Drama This park, where Bora spent free time during her school trip in , is densely filled with ancient tombs. About 20 large tombs create a dreamy atmosphere as if drawing a ridgeline. The spot with a magnolia tree standing between the tombs is famous as a photo zone. We recommend visiting Cheonmachong, the only tomb with its interior open to the public.','9 Gyerim-ro, Gyeonju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00-22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:45','2026-09-16 03:17:45',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2026-06-10 11:06:30'),(734,46,'en','Gyeongju EXPO Grand Park (경주엑스포대공원)','Located in the Bomun Tourist Complex, Gyeongju EXPO Grand Park is where the Gyeongju World Expo, the world\'s first cultural fair themed around culture and arts, was held in 1998. Over the following 20 years, it served as the venue for ten Gyeongju World Expos, boosting Korean cultural pride and contributing to the development of human culture. Today, it is a popular attraction featuring diverse cultural content such as exhibitions, videos, performances, and hands-on experiences. Major facilities include Gyeongju Tower, Gyeongju Expo Solgeo Art Museum, and more.','614 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Expo Park] 10:00-22:00 [Exhibition Hall] 10:00-18:00 * Operating hours vary by month; check the website for details',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:45','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available (Free)','Open year-round','2026-05-19 09:27:08'),(735,1096,'en','Homeplus Mega Food Market Gyeongju Branch [Tax Refund Shop](홈플러스 메가푸드마켓 경주점)','Homeplus is a major Korean retail brand known for affordable prices and a wide product range. From fresh food and household essentials to home appliances, it offers a convenient, value-focused shopping experience—especially through its online ordering and delivery services.','97, Gongdan-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:45','2026-09-16 03:17:45',NULL,'Available','Seollal (Lunar New Year\'s Day) & Chuseok (Korean Thanksgiving Day) holidays','2026-03-18 10:10:06'),(736,812,'en','Woljeonggyo Bridge (월정교)','Woljeonggyo Bridge, located in Gyo-dong, Gyeongju, was built during the Unified Silla period (AD 676-935), but was burnt down during the Joseon dynasty. Through historical research, the bridge was rebuilt in April 2018 to become the largest wooden bridge in Korea. According to Samguk Sagi (History of the Three Kingdoms), the bridge was built during the 19th year of King Gyeongdeok&rsquo;s reign (AD 760), connecting Wolseong and Namsan together. The historical research to rebuild the bridge lasted from November 26, 1984 to September 8, 1986, finding that the bridge was made with wood for the first time. The first rebuilding of the bridge was from 2008 to 2013 and the finishing touches were added from April 2016 to April 2018. Through this research and rebuilding process, future restoration of historical buildings have a better reference to use.','274 Gyo-dong, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00-22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:45','2026-09-16 03:17:45',NULL,'Available (Woljeonggyo Bridge public parking lot)','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-06-13 13:09:12'),(737,824,'en','Gyeongju Five Royal Tombs (경주 오릉)','The Five Royal Tombs (called Oreung in Korean) have been officially designated Historic Site No. 172 and are the final resting places of four kings of the Park clan—King Park Hyeokgeose (founder of the Silla Kingdom), King Namhae, King Yuri, and King Jabi—and one queen (Queen Aryeong, wife of King Park Hyeokgeose). To the east of the royal tombs lies Sungdeokjeon Shrine, which holds the ancestral tablet of King Park Hyeokgeose. Behind the shrine is the Aryeongjeong Well, said to be the birthplace of Queen Aryeong.','38-9 Geumseong-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','March-October 09:00-18:00 November-February 09:00-17:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:45','2026-09-16 03:17:45',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-06-13 11:10:23'),(738,63,'en','Tomb of King Munmu (경주 문무대왕릉)','A little rocky islet approximately 200 meters from the shore at Bonggil-ri is the Tomb of King Munmu (AD 661-681), who unified the three kingdoms and became the 30th ruler of the Silla Kingdom. The king gave specific instructions to be buried in the East Sea after his death so that he would become a dragon and protect Silla from foreign invaders. The rocky island, about 200 meters in circumference, is divided by a cross-shaped waterway, forming a pool at the center, at the bottom of which is a granite stone 3.6 meters long, 2.9 meters wide and 0.9 meters thick. Legend has it that the remains of King Munmu’s cremated body are buried under this rock. Historians still debate whether the ashes of the King Munmu were scattered or stored in an urn and placed under the rock.','1366-9, Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:46','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-06-12 17:50:08'),(739,803,'en','Gyeongju Seokguram Grotto [UNESCO World Heritage] (경주 석굴암 [유네스코 세계유산])','Seokguram Grotto was constructed by Kim Dae-Seong during the reign of King Gyeongdeok (742-765) of the Silla Kingdom. Located 3 kilometers away by hiking trail and 9 kilometers by car from Bulguksa Temple, the grotto was designed very harmoniously with the seated Buddha facing the East Sea. It is a valuable cultural heritage that is preserved and registered as a UNESCO World Heritage on December 6, 1995.','238 Seokgul-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00-18:00 * Viewing time until 19:00 * Operating hours subject to change',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:46','2026-09-16 03:17:46',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-06-12 17:13:23'),(740,870,'en','Padosori Trail (파도소리길)','The Padosori (Sound of the Waves) Trail stretches for 1.7 kilometers along the shoreline of Eupcheon-ri in Gyeongju, offering stunning views of the Gyeongju Yangnam Columnar Joint. The coastal road is well-maintained and features a decked pathway, benches, viewing platforms, and a suspension bridge. The Columnar Joint has diverse shapes; in particular, the fan-shaped columnar joint is a rare sight not only in Korea but also worldwide, and thus has been designated as a Natural Monument in 2012.','405-7 Eupcheon-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:46','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round','2025-05-28 17:58:10'),(741,996,'en','Salon Heritage (살롱헤리티지)','Salon Heritage is a world cultural heritage media promotion hall, located inside the Gyeongju World Expo Memorial, which was designed by renowned architect Kengo Kuma, drawing inspiration from Daereungwon Ancient Tombs and columnar joints of Gyeongju. It features dynamic media walls, a media tunnel and a world heritage study, offering visitors an immersive digital experience to explore the rich heritage of Gyeongju.','614 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00-18:00 (Operating hours extended in summer)','[Gyeongju Expo Park ticket] Individuals: Adults 12,000 won / Children 10,000 won Groups: Adults 10,000 won / Children 8,000 won Senior citizens 4,000 won * Group: 10 people or more * Adults (age 19-64) / Children (age 3-18) / Senior citizens (ages 65 and older)','2026-09-16 03:17:46','2026-09-16 03:17:46',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-05-26 15:47:01'),(742,804,'en','Bomunho Lake (보문호)','Bomunho Lake is a man-made lake 1,652,900 m&sup2; in size. It was built on the site of an old fortress in Myeonghwalsan Mountain in the east of Gyeongju in accordance with the Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Resort development plan. There are many leisure facilities and parks around the lake, including an international hotel and Gyeongju World. Bomunho Lake is very popular among bikers and walkers. Unlike other cities or towns where cherry trees are only found in certain areas, Gyeongju is packed with cherry blossoms. In spring, the whole cityscape turns pink with the beautiful blossoms. The combination of the stunning trees reflected in the waters of Bomunho Lake and the trees of Bulguksa Park gracefully adorning the nearby temple make for particularly stunning sights. When a light breeze blows, cherry blossoms gently flutter down like satin snow flakes. The Gyeongju Cherry Blossom Marathon is held in April when the cherry blossoms are in full bloom.','424-33 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open 24 hr',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:47','2026-09-16 03:17:47',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-05-21 17:46:30'),(743,805,'en','Gyeongju Golgulsa Temple (골굴사(경주))','Golgulsa Temple is a temple located within the Hamwolsan Mountain, situated between Gyeongju City and the East Sea. With a history of over 1,500 years, it houses many Buddha statues preserved within its twelve grottoes. Maintaining the tradition of Korean Buddhism\'s practice of Seonmudo, visitors can witness Seonmudo performances. Additionally, there are templestay programs available, offering opportunities to experience Korean temple culture.','101-5 Girim-ro, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open 24 hr',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:47','2026-09-16 03:17:47',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-05-21 15:04:38'),(744,1005,'en','Gyeongju Expo Solgeo Art Museum (경주솔거미술관(솔거미술관))','Gyeongju Expo Solgeo Art Museum is Gyeongju&rsquo;s first public art museum, opened in 2015 with the donation of 830 works by the Korean painter Park Dae-sung. Designed by the renowned architect Seung H-Sang, the museum&rsquo;s architecture blends people, space, and nature. It features a permanent exhibition of works by Park Dae-sung, along with special rotational exhibitions by invited artists. For visitors seeking deeper insight into the artwork, the museum offers a docent program. The window in the permanent exhibition hall has become a popular SNS spot and is often referred to as a moving painting.','614 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','January-April, October-December: 10:00-18:00 May-July, September: 10:00-19:00 August: 10:00-20:00','Individuals: Adults 12,000 won / Children 10,000 won Groups: Adults 10,000 won / Children 8,000 won * Group: 10 or more people * Adults (ages 19-64) / Children (ages 3-18)','2026-09-16 03:17:47','2026-09-16 03:17:47',NULL,'Available','Open all year round','2025-05-19 17:12:40'),(745,811,'en','Gyeongju-si Special Tourist Zone (경주시 관광특구)','Gyeongju was the capital city of the ancient kingdom of Silla. The city is often referred to as a &ldquo;museum without walls&rdquo; because of the many cultural relics scattered throughout the city. Almost everything in this city, from the streets to the mountains, is rich in history. Gyeongju has roughly 300 sites that have been designated as a cultural heritage, with some of them being UNESCO-recognized World Heritage Sites. The Gyeongju Special Tourist Zone includes the districts of Namsan, Wolseong, Daereungwon, Hwangryongsa, and Sanseong. This area has a total of 52 cultural assets registered on the World Heritage list. Many of the hills are actually royal tombs and fields of grass used to be sites of ancient temples. The entire Namsan Mountain can almost be considered a cultural asset because of the many stone pagodas and Buddha statues that can be found here. The Bulguk district is home to many of Gyeongju&rsquo;s most well-known attractions such as Bulguksa Temple, Seokguram Grotto, Gyeongju Folk Village, Silla Arts and Science Museum, and Goereung. In the Bomun district, there are plenty of recreation facilities surrounding Bomunho Lake. Other attractions in the area include Gyeongju World Culture Expo Park, Gyeongju World, and Silla Millennium Park. [Gyeongju Special Tourist Zone] Areas included: Downtown area, Bomun Lake Resort, and Bulguksa Temple in Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangnam-do Area size: 32,650,000㎡ Tourist Attractions: Bulguksa Temple, Seokguram Grotto, Daereungwon Tomb Complex, Namsan Mountain, Bomunho Lake, Shilla Millennium Park, Gyeongju World Culture Expo Park, etc.','614 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Varies by facility',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:47','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'26 public parking lots are available at tourist sites, Bomun Tourism Complex and Bulguksa Temple','Varies by facility','2025-03-25 16:23:13'),(746,807,'en','Gyeongju Bulguksa Temple [UNESCO World Heritage] (경주 불국사 [유네스코 세계유산])','Bulguksa Temple is a representative relic of Buddhist culture from the Silla kingdom. The temple was built during the 15th year of King Beopheung\'s reign (514-540) to wish for peace and prosperity for all. It was later rebuilt in 751 by Kim Dae-seong. Unfortunately, the temple caught fire during the Imjin War (1592-1598). After the war, the temple suffered serious damage and was often the target of theft. Starting in 1920, the temple has undergone continual restoration work. The temple now holds seven national treasures and a number of additional important heritages and was designated a World Cultural Heritage Site along with the nearby Seokguram Grotto by UNESCO in December 1995.','385 Bulguk-ro, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00-18:00 (Exit time 19:00) * No pets allowed',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:47','2026-09-16 03:17:47',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2025-03-24 13:45:06'),(747,858,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Mountain (경주 남산)','Namsan Mountain of Gyeongju is a 466-meter mountain located south of the Gyeongju city center. Gyeongju was the capital of the Silla dynasty (BC 57-AD 935) from its inception to its end. The Silla people revered this mountain, considering it sacred, and left many traces of their presence, resulting in numerous cultural relics that still exist today. Therefore, visitors can enjoy both hiking and cultural heritage sightseeing on this mountain.','Namsan Mountain of Gyeongju (경주 남산)','06:00-18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:48','2026-09-16 03:17:48',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round)','2024-02-27 17:17:35'),(748,65,'en','Oryu Goarahaebyeon Beach (오류고아라해변)','Oryu Goarahaebyeon Beach, located near Gampo Port, is known for its soft sand and is famous for sand baths. It\'s an ideal spot for camping, boasting a 1km stretch of white sandy beach, shallow waters, and a lush pine forest. Within the pine forest, there\'s a campsite where visitors can enjoy caravan or tent camping. During the summer, marine leisure facilities like banana boats and motor boats are available. Nearby tourist attractions include Songdaemal Lighthouse and Gampo Marine Park.','277-8 Oryu-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju-si, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Sea bathing] 09:00-19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:48','2026-09-16 03:17:48',NULL,'Available','N/A (Open all year round) * Sea bathing may be restricted due to bad weather or the appearance of harmful creatures.','2024-02-23 10:00:11'),(749,1096,'ja','[事後免税店]ホームプラスメガフードマーケット・キョンジュ（慶州）店(홈플러스 메가푸드마켓 경주점)','ホームプラスは品揃えが豊富で値段もお手頃な韓国の大型スーパーです。生鮮食品から日用品、家電まで1か所で購入でき、オンライン配送サービスを利用すれば便利でお得なお買い物体験ができます。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市コンダンロ97','10:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:56','2026-09-16 03:17:56',NULL,'あり','ソルナル（旧暦1月1日）・秋夕（旧暦8月15日）','2026-03-18 10:10:07'),(750,1005,'ja','率居美術館（솔거미술관）','率居（ソルゴ）美術館は慶州初の公立美術館です。韓国画の巨匠、小山（ソサン）・朴大成（パク・テソン）画伯が作品約830点を寄贈する意思を示し、美術館建設の構想がスタートし、「シルクロード慶州 2015」開幕に合わせてオープンしました。美術館の建物は韓国を代表する建築家である承孝尚（スン・ヒョサン）氏が設計し、人と空間、自然の境界を取り払うように建てられました。朴大成画伯の作品を展示する常設展示室と、時期にごとに新しいアーティストを招待して作品を展示する企画展示室が用意されています。常設展示室のひとつに、「動く絵」の窓という自然光が入る大きな窓があり、SNSで率居美術館最高のフォトポイントとして人気を集めています。窓から差し込む日差しが展示室内の作品をより輝かせ、窓の外の風景はそれ自体が作品になります。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市キョンガムロ614','1～4月・10～12月10:00～18:00、5～9月 10:00～19:00','普通券：大人（19歳以上～64歳）12,000ウォン','2026-09-16 03:17:56','2026-09-16 03:17:56',NULL,NULL,'年中無休','2026-03-09 11:16:46'),(751,63,'ja','慶州 文武大王陵（경주 문무대왕릉）','新羅30代文武王の墓。東海岸から200m離れた海にある水中陵で、世界的に類例がなく、新羅人の独創的な考えを垣間見ることができるスポットです。文武王は父親の太宗武烈王の業績を受け継ぎ、高句麗を滅亡させ、唐の侵略を防ぎ三国統一を成し遂げました。『三国史記』によると、文武王が亡くなり仏式の葬儀に従って火葬し、東海に葬れば龍になって東海に侵入する倭寇を防ぐという遺言を残したとされます。大王岩は自然岩を利用したもので、その中は東西南北に人工水路が造られ、海水が東から入ってきて西に出るようになっているため常に穏やかな環境が保たれています。水面下には長さ3.7m、幅2.06mの南北に長く置かれた平たい亀の形の石で覆われており、この中に文武王の遺骨が埋葬されていると推測されています。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ヤンブク面トンヘアンロ1366-9','常時開放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:57','2026-09-16 04:01:08',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-06-04 14:03:32'),(752,824,'ja','慶州 五陵（경주 오릉）','史跡に指定されている五陵（オルン）は、新羅初代王の「赫居世（パクヒョッコセ）王」と王妃「閼英（アリョル）夫人」、2代目王の「南解（ナムへ）王」、3代目王の「儒理（ユリ）王」、5代目王の「婆娑（パサ）王」など、新羅初期の王族5人の陵墓が集まっていることから名づけられました。 五陵の東方には、今でも初代王の位牌を祀る崇徳殿があり、その後ろには、閼英夫人が誕生したとされる閼英亭が残されています。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市クムソンロ38-9','夏季（3～10月）9:00～18:00 冬季（11～2月）9:00～17:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:57','2026-09-16 03:17:57',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-05-27 11:20:46'),(753,803,'ja','慶州石窟庵［ユネスコ世界遺産］（경주 석굴암 [유네스코 세계유산]）','国宝・石窟庵（ソックラム）は新羅・景徳王10（751）年、当時の宰相であった金大城（キム・デソン）が創建したと伝えられています。 仏国寺から稜線伝いに約3km、迂回路の一般道・仏国路経由で約9kmのところにある石窟庵。 その構造は方形と円形、直線と曲線、平面と球面が調和をなし、特に菩薩像や弟子像など周囲の壁に彫刻された現存する38の仏像はいずれも傑作です。石窟庵はこのような全体の調和を通じ高度な哲学を持ちつつ、同時に科学的な構造をも持ち合わせています。 石窟庵の中央には白色の花崗岩でできた如来坐像本尊仏が鎮座しており、本尊仏の視線は東海の海の方へと向いています。 その訳は、如来坐像が臨む視線の先に慶州市陽北面（ヤンブクミョン）奉吉里（ポンギルリ）にある文武王（ムンムワン）水中王陵、別名・大王岩（テワンアム）があるからなのです。大王岩の近くには文武王ゆかりの感恩寺（カムンサ）址や利見台（イギョンデ）などの史跡があります。 仏国寺・石窟庵は1995年12月6日、海印寺の八万大蔵経や宗廟とともにユネスコ世界文化遺産に正式に登録され、大切に保護されている史跡です。 *吐含山（トハムサン・標高745m）は新羅の人々の魂が宿る霊山で、別名・東岳とも呼ばれています。新羅五名山のひとつとして数えられ、古の時代より仏教の聖地として知られているこの山は、山全体がひとつの遺跡のようになっており、無数の遺跡が点在しています。また山は松やクヌギの森に覆われ、森深い山となっています。 仏国寺から東の方へ山道を歩いていくと、石窟庵が目の前に現れます。この仏国寺から石窟庵につづく山道は、山の中腹を縫うように走る車道ができるまでは唯一の道だったところで、多くの観光客が登っていった山道でした。1960年代以前には修学旅行でやってきた児童・生徒らの姿がこの山道でよく見受けられました。吐含山という名称はこの山が海の近くにあることから霧がよく立ちこめる場所で、山が海側から移流する霧を飲み込み吐き出す姿を表現し付けられたものと言われています。 *石窟庵の日の出* 石窟庵から臨む東海（トンへ）の水平線に昇る日の出。はるか向こうの水平線に真っ赤な太陽が昇り、赤く染まる空と海が絶景です。 石窟庵で日の出を拝んだ後は、吐含山から東海方面へ向う1998年開通した石獐路（ソクチャンノ）を経由して、海辺の町・甘浦（カムポ）や陽北の海岸方面へ向かってみましょう。ここでは韓国でも指折りの綺麗な海で獲れる海の幸を楽しむことができ、また感恩寺址や文武王陵などの史跡地も数多くあり、観光スポットとしてもおすすめです。 慶州中心部へのお戻りの際には民俗工芸村でショッピングもかねて観光したり、普門（ポムン）観光団地に立ち寄るのもおすすめです。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ソックルロ238','9:00～18:00（退場時間19:00） ※季節によって変更されることがありますのでお確かめの上おでかけください',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:57','2026-09-16 03:17:57',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-05-27 09:37:31'),(754,996,'ja','サロンヘリテージ（살롱헤리티지）','慶州（キョンジュ）エキスポ大公園内に位置するサロンヘリテージは、有名建築家・隈研吾が慶州大陵苑と柱状節理からインスピレーションを得てデザインした建築物にある世界文化遺産メディア広報館です。内部ではメディアスクリーン、メディアトンネル、世界遺産の書斎など最先端デジタル技術を利用し、世界文化遺産の起源や世界文化遺産都市を見ることができます。 1. メディアウォール：韓国最高仕様のLEDディスプレイ利用 ・ヘリテージユニバース：世界遺産制度の起源 ・世界遺産都市：慶州の美しい世界遺産 2. メディアトンネル：韓国最長のメディアトンネル ・光の遺産：光で表現された世界遺産 ・千年の森南山：慶州歴史遺跡地区のひとつである南山地区の日の出と日没の映像を含む実写映像 3. 世界遺産旅行：透明OLEDタッチスクリーンを使用し、世界遺産関連の興味深いクイズを解きながら世界遺産について知ることができる体験型コンテンツ 4. 世界文化遺産の書斎：18世紀のヨーロッパ、対話と交流の場だったサロンをモチーフにした書斎','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市キョンガムロ614','10:00～18:00（夏季は延長）','普通券（大人：満19歳以上～64歳）12,000ウォン','2026-09-16 03:17:57','2026-09-16 03:17:57',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-05-23 17:59:39'),(755,870,'ja','パドソリ道（파도소리길）','パドソリ道は邑川港から下西港までの1.7km区間のことをいい、ボードウォーク、東屋、ベンチ、吊橋などが整備された海岸道で、慶州陽南柱状節理を見ながら歩くことができます。慶州陽南柱状節理は2012年、軍部隊が撤収したことで世に知られるようになりました。陽南柱状節理群では上へとそびえる柱状節理だけでなく、扇形柱状節理、傾いた柱状節理、横になっている柱状節理など多様な形態の柱状節理を観察することができます。なかでも圧巻なのは扇のように丸く広がった扇形柱状節理です。陽南柱状節理群は世界的にも類を見ない非常に珍しい形で、2012年9月に天然記念物に指定されました。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ヤンナム面ウプチョン里405-5','常時開放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:57','2026-09-16 04:01:09',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-05-23 17:30:22'),(756,807,'ja','慶州仏国寺[ユネスコ世界遺産]（경주 불국사 [유네스코 세계유산]）','「雲を飲み込み、そして吐き出す」という名称のついた山・吐含山（トハムサン・標高745メートル）の中腹に位置する仏国寺（プルグクサ）と石窟庵（ソックラム）は、きらびやかな新羅の仏教文化の中心をなす史跡です。新羅・法興王15（528）年に、新羅の法興王が母・迎帝夫人の意に従い、国や人々の安寧を願い建立しました。その後も重建を重ね、新羅・景徳王10（751）年には、金大城（キム・デソン）の手により大幅な改修を行い塔や石橋などを造ったといわれています。しかしながらが壬辰倭乱（日本で言う「文禄・慶長の役」）により建物のみならず、貴重な宝物などほとんどが焼失、あるいは略奪されてしまいました。1920年までは一部の建物と塔だけが荒れ果てた状態で放置されていましたが、元来の姿に戻すべくたゆまない復旧作業の甲斐もあり、国宝7点を所蔵する今日のような韓国を代表する名刹の姿となりました。 仏国寺から尾根伝いに約3キロメートル（舗装道路である石窟路経由ではおよそ9キロメートル）ほど進むと、東海（トンへ）の海原の方に向いて鎮座している如来坐像の本尊仏がある石窟庵（ソックラム）にたどり着きます。仏国寺と石窟庵は1995年12月6日に海印寺（ヘインサ）の八万大蔵経や宗廟（チョンミョ）とともに、世界文化遺産に正式に登録され、国際的にもよく知られる史跡になりました。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市プルグクロ385','9:00～18:00（退場時間19:00） ※変更されることがありますのでお確かめの上おでかけください ※ペットの入場不可',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:58','2026-09-16 03:17:58',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-05-07 16:11:31'),(757,804,'ja','普門湖（보문호）','普門湖（ポムンホ）は慶州普門観光団地内にある1,652,900m&sup2;（50万坪）規模の人工湖。春のお花見スポットとして人気で、周辺には国際的規模のホテル、リゾート、慶州ワールド、公園などがあります。また普門湖には散策路と自転車道が整備されており、湖周辺の柳の道に沿って歩く普門湖トゥルレ道（普門湖循環探訪路）が有名です。湖を眺めながら歩く約8kmの散策路が設けられており、全体を一周するのに2時間ほどかかります。桜が満開になる4月には普門観光団地で慶州桜マラソン大会が開催され、秋には紅葉が美しさを演出する湖を見ることができます。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ポムンロ424-33','常時',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:58','2026-09-16 03:17:58',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-05-07 15:34:25'),(758,805,'ja','骨窟寺（慶州）（골굴사（경주））','骨窟寺（コルグルサ）は、慶州市街と東海の間にそびえ立つ含月山（ハムォルサン）に位置している仏教寺院です。1,500年以上の歴史をもち、12の石窟に多くの仏像が保存されています。韓国仏教の 修行方法である「禅武道」の伝統を継承し、禅武道公演を観賞することができます。テンプルステイプログラムもあるので韓国のお寺文化が体験できます。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ヤンブク面キリムロ101-5','常時開放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:58','2026-09-16 03:17:58',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-04-29 11:09:04'),(759,1077,'ja','慶州城東市場（경주 성동시장）','店舗数約300店、露天約30店の規模を誇る慶州（キョンジュ）城東市場（ソンドンシジャン）。 1971年の市場開設以来、地元・慶州を代表する在来市場としてその地位を確固たるものとしています。 衰退化する在来市場の環境改善事業として競争力を高め地域経済活性化を目的で、地元・慶州市が2005年、総事業費16億ウォンあまりをかけ、城東市場現代化事業を開始、市場入口のオブジェ設置、市場及びグルメ通り・全長284mのアーケード設置、およそ600m区間の下水道整備、電気消防設備、市場路面整備、250点におよぶワイドカラー写真設置などを行い、新たな市場として生まれ変わりました。 特に、この城東市場環境改善事業を通じて慶州市は、新羅の悠久の古都であり、国際的な文化・観光都市にふさわしい在来市場を作り上げるべく、地元に点在する貴重な文化遺産およそ250点をテーマにしたワイドカラー写真をアーケードの屋根と店舗の看板との間に設置、慶州を訪れる観光客の方々に城東市場の新たな見どころをご提供するなど、これまでにないアイデアで在来市場活性化を図っています。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ウォンファロ281ボンギル11','7:00～20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:59','2026-09-16 04:01:10',NULL,'可能','店舗ごとに異なる','2025-03-13 15:47:38'),(760,811,'ja','慶州市観光特区（경주시 관광특구）','慶州（キョンジュ）は韓国最大級の観光都市で、街自体が巨大な野外博物館といわれるほど随所に文化遺産が散在しています。歩くすべての道が遺跡であり、見えるすべての景色が生きた歴史であり、出会うすべてが文化遺産と言っても過言ではない韓国を代表する歴史文化都市です。そのため1994年慶州市一帯の市内、普門地区、仏国地区などが観光特区に指定されました。観光特区内には文化遺産に指定された名所が約300ヶ所もあり、そのうちユネスコ世界遺産に登録されているものもあります。観光特区内の主な名所には仏国寺、石窟庵、大陵苑などがあり、慶州エキスポ大公園、慶州ワールド、新羅ミレニアムパークといったレジャー施設も備えています。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市キョンガムロ614 (천군동)','施設ごとに異なる',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:59','2026-09-16 04:01:08',NULL,'あり','施設ごとに異なる','2025-03-12 11:37:28'),(761,46,'ja','慶州エキスポ大公園（경주엑스포대공원）','慶州（キョンジュ）エキスポ大公園は慶州普門（ポムン）観光団地に位置している公園で、新羅の文化と芸術を展示や公演、体験により韓国文化を1カ所で経験できるテーマ公園です。慶州タワー、輝かしい光の新羅、率居（ソルゴ）美術館、新羅を収めた星（ルミナイト）、瞻星台（チョムソンデ）映像館、アサダル彫刻公園などがあります。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市キョンガムロ614','公園： 1月～4月 10:00～18:00 5月～6月 10:00～19:00 7月～8月 10:00～20:00 10月～12月 10:00～18:00 展示館：10:00～18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:59','2026-09-16 04:01:08',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-03-12 10:11:33'),(762,858,'ja','慶州南山（경주 남산）','慶州（キョンジュ）南山（ナムサン）は、慶州市街地の南にそびえ立つ標高466メートルの山です。慶州は新羅王朝（起源前57～起源後935）が最初から最後まで都にしていた年です。新羅人たちは都に立つこの山を神聖化して多くの痕跡を残し、今でも数多くの文化財が残されています。そのため、この山では登山と共に国家遺産を観賞することができます。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ナムサン洞','6:00～18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:17:59','2026-09-16 03:17:59',NULL,'あり','年中無休','2025-01-06 11:11:49'),(763,76,'ja','慶州 皇龍寺址（경주 황룡사지）','「皇龍寺址（ファンリョンサジ）」は慶州市九黄（クファン）洞に位置しており、芬皇寺の前に広がる広大な敷地に残されている遺跡です。 ここは新羅最大の寺院であり、護国の大寺刹として古新羅の仏教文化の精髄が見られる由緒深い寺刹址です。善徳女王がこの地に塔を建ててから23年後、新羅は三国統一し、このことから多くの人々が「新羅の三国統一はこの塔の霊験である」と歴史書に記録しています。かつて新羅三宝と呼ばれる宝物のうちの2つである金堂三尊丈六像、九層木塔が皇龍寺に所蔵されており、また新羅最大の鐘も置かれていましたが、蒙古軍の侵攻によって失ってしまいました。皇龍寺は慈蔵や元曉などの新羅時代の最高の高僧たちが説法を説いた場所で、真興、真平、善徳、憲康、真聖女王などの帝王たちが自ら彼らの説法を聞くために訪れました。1969年7月にこの地を発掘調査した際、金堂、講堂、塔地が発掘されたことをはじめとし、1976年3月から8年間に渡る発掘作業により独特の配置を持つ一塔三金堂式だったことが明らかになり、4万点余りの遺物が出土しました。この際、建物の基礎となる土台をはじめとする下部構造は確認されましたが、建物の上部家具材は正確に考証することができないため、建物全体の復元には至っておらず、土台部分だけが復元されました。発掘された遺跡地から現れた寺院の総面積は8,800坪に至り、これは仏国寺の約8倍の広さに相当します。現在、皇龍寺址は史跡に指定されています。','慶尚北道 慶州市 臨海路64-19','常時開放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:00','2026-09-16 04:01:08',NULL,'可能','年中無休','2024-09-24 16:17:49'),(764,65,'ja','五柳ゴアラ海辺（오류고아라해변）','五柳（オリュ）ゴアラ海辺は、甘浦（カンポ）港の近くにある海水浴場です。砂が柔らかく、砂風呂で広く知られています。約1キロメートルにわたって白い砂浜が広がり、遠浅で松林が生い茂っているためキャンプに最適です。松林にはキャンプ場があり、キャンピングトレーラーやテントでキャンプを楽しむことができます。夏は、バナナボート、モーターボートなどマリンレジャー施設が運営されます。周辺の観光スポットとして、松台末（ソンデマル）灯台、甘浦海上公園があります。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市カンポ邑オリュ里277-8','海水浴場9:00～19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:00','2026-09-16 03:18:00',NULL,'あり','年中無休（悪天候時や有害生物が出現した時は遊泳禁止となります）','2024-02-23 10:00:53'),(765,125,'ja','普門ゴルフクラブ（보문골프클럽）','古都・慶州（キョンジュ）にある普門（ポムン）ゴルフクラブは、普門湖畔に造成されました。国際レベルの普門観光団地を観光しながら楽しむことができます。','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市ポムンロ182-14','日の出～日没後1時間',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:00','2026-09-16 03:18:00',NULL,'あり','ソルナル（旧暦1月1日）・秋夕（旧暦8月15日）','2022-12-26 17:47:48'),(766,11,'ja','慶州 奈勿王陵（경주 내물왕릉）','「慶州奈勿王陵（キョンジュネムルワンヌン）」は慶州郷校の北側に位置する丘の上にある大型の丸い土墳です。墓の底面や周りに自然石の稜がありますが、これは武烈王陵の場合と同じでその中に別の護石が設置されていると推測されています。三国史記には奈勿王の葬地に関する記録はありませんが、三国遺事に瞻星台の南西にあると記録されており現在の位置と一致します。また初期の王陵としては比較的綺麗な形で現存しています。 保護区域1万2,818平方メートル、底径22メートル、高さ5.3メートル','キョンサンブク道キョンジュ市キョ洞','常時開放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:01','2026-09-16 04:01:08',NULL,'可能','年中無休','2022-08-29 14:36:59'),(767,808,'zh','庆州大陵苑一带(경주 대릉원 일원)','大陵苑一带主要是分布于庆尚北道庆州市的新罗时代古坟群, 于2011年7月28日被指定为史迹。庆州市大陵苑一带的新罗古坟群，原来分别被指定为庆州路东里古坟群、 庆州路西里古坟群、庆州皇南里古坟群、 庆州皇吾里古坟群、 庆州仁旺里古坟群。2011年7月28日，国家遗产厅考虑到历史性等特征，将位于庆州平原中央地区且相互临近的新罗古坟群进行了统合，一并指定为古迹。 ◎ 体验韩流魅力的旅行信息 - 电视剧《那年，我们初遇》 《那年，我们初遇》中主人公沃拉修学旅行自由时间去过的地方，是一个密集古坟的公园。约20多座大型古坟如同绘制山脊般布列，营造出梦幻般的氛围。古坟之间站着一棵木兰树的地方是著名的拍照点。推荐一同参观唯一对外开放内部的天马冢。','庆尚北道庆州市皇南洞 (황남동)','09:00~22:00(入场截至 21:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:09','2026-09-16 04:17:24',NULL,'有','全年无休','2026-06-10 11:06:29'),(768,1096,'zh','[事后免税店]Homeplus Mega Food Market庆州店(홈플러스 메가푸드마켓 경주점)','Homeplus是一个韩国零售品牌，价格合理，商品多元化。从生鲜食品、生活用品到家电产品，实现一站式购物，通过线上配送服务提供便捷、实惠的购物体验。','庆尚北道庆州市工团路97','10:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:09','2026-09-16 03:18:09',NULL,'可','传统节日','2026-03-18 10:10:06'),(769,1005,'zh','率居美术馆(솔거미술관）','庆州Solgeo美术馆是公立美术馆。韩国画的巨匠苏山朴大成画家的作品830余件的捐赠意向表明，美术馆建设的构想开始了，并于2015年与丝绸之路庆州博览会的开幕同时开馆。美术馆由韩国建筑师胜효相设计，是一座打破人与空间、自然之间界限的美术馆。考虑到观众的动线，展览空间被布置，并像迷宫一样分隔开。设有展出朴大成画家作品的常设展览室和每个时期邀请新作家的作品展出的策划展览室。如果想更深入地接触作品，可以利用Solgeo美术馆运营的讲解员项目。常设展览室中有一个自然光透入的大窗户。','庆尚北道庆州市镜鉴路614（千军洞）','10:00~18:00※ 因季节不同，请电话咨询','庆州世界文化博览会综合门票- 成人 12,000韩元- 儿童 10,000韩元※ 详细信息请致电咨询','2026-09-16 03:18:09','2026-09-16 03:18:09',NULL,NULL,'全年无休','2026-03-12 11:24:53'),(770,996,'zh','Salon Heritage(살롱헤리티지)','位于庆州EXPO大公园内的Salon Heritage，是世界文化遗产媒体宣传馆，坐落于世界级建筑大师隈研吾从庆州大陵苑柱状节理获得灵感而设计的著名建筑物内。内部通过媒体屏幕、媒体隧道、世界遗产书房等尖端树木装备及媒体，展示世界文化遗产的起源和世界文化遗产城市之风采。','庆尚北道庆州市镜鑑路614','10:00~18:00 (夏季延长运营)','※ 庆州世界文化EXPO公园使用券 [普通券] - 成人 : 12,000韩元(满19岁以上~ 64岁)','2026-09-16 03:18:10','2026-09-16 03:18:10',NULL,'有','全年无休','2025-06-23 10:34:15'),(771,870,'zh','涛声路(파도소리길)','涛声路从邑川港到下西港，长约1.7公里的的路线。整条海岸道路有木栈道、凉亭、长椅、天空步道等休闲便民设施。可以在此一边散步，边欣赏庆州阳南柱状节理景观。因发达规模及形态的多样性受到认定的庆州阳南柱状节理，于2012年9月被指定为天然纪念物。其中最为观赏点的要属扇形柱状节理，形态珍稀，在世界上很难找到类似的例子。','庆尚北道庆州市阳南面邑川里405-5','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:10','2026-09-16 04:17:24',NULL,'有','全年无休','2025-06-19 16:43:53'),(772,1077,'zh','庆州城洞市场경주 성동시장','位于庆尚北道庆州市城东洞的城东市场开业于1971年，现拥有300多家商铺及30多个摊贩，其东侧对面就是庆州站。','庆尚北道庆州市源花路281号街11','各店铺不同',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:10','2026-09-16 04:17:26',NULL,'可能','各店铺不同','2025-03-27 11:26:15'),(773,812,'zh','月精桥(월정교)','月精桥是位于庆尚北道庆州市校洞的统一新罗时代所建的桥梁。朝鲜时代流失后于2018年4月复原为韩国内最大规模的木制桥梁。 据《三国史记》的记载，月精桥由统一新罗时代景德王19年(760年)所建，发挥着连接庆州月城和南山的作用。 1984年11月26日起至1986年9月8日期间，为了复原设计进行的2次资料收集和发掘调查结果，最初确认了建设当时的月精桥为木制桥梁的事实。2008年起至2013年期间的作业过程中完成了长66.15m, 宽13m, 高6m的复原工程。2016年4月起开始的桥梁两侧的2栋门楼建设，也于2018年4月竣工。 门楼2层设置了展示出土文物和桥梁建筑历史的数码展示馆，播放月精桥的历史和复原过程影像。庆州市新罗王京8大核心遗址复原、整修事业中，作为第一环完成的月精桥复原工程为日后进行的皇龙寺、新罗王宫、历史遗址地区、新罗坊等复原整修事业提供了重要的参考价值。','庆尚北道庆州市校洞 274','09:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:11','2026-09-16 04:17:24',NULL,'可用','全年无休','2025-03-27 11:21:35'),(774,807,'zh','庆州佛国寺[联合国教科文组织世界遗产]경주 불국사 [유네스코 세계유산])','佛国寺和石窟庵坐落于&ldquo;吞云吐雾&rdquo;吐含山的山腰处，是灿烂的新罗佛教文化的核心。1440年前，新罗法兴王22年为维护国家安定和百姓平安而建造了佛国寺。此后，在新罗景徳王时期由宰相金大城主导对其进行了修建，使得寺庙焕然一新。壬辰倭乱时期，佛国寺的大部分建筑被烧毁，在1920年之前，仅剩下部分寺庙建筑和佛塔，后经不断地复原和修缮才拥有了如今的规模。在佛国寺里沿山脊上行约3km，便可看到著名的石窟庵，庵内筑有面朝东海的东方最大的如来坐像。佛国寺和石窟庵于1995年12月6日与海印寺八万大藏经及宗庙一同入选世界文化遗产，在世界上享有很高的盛名。 * 主要文物古迹 多宝塔(国宝第20号) 佛国寺三层石塔(国宝第21号) 青云桥、白云桥(国宝第23号) 石窟庵(国宝第24号) 金铜毗卢遮那佛坐像(国宝26号) 金铜阿弥陀如来坐像(国宝第27号) 莲花桥、七宝桥(国宝第22号)','庆尚北道庆州市佛国路385号 (进岘洞)','09:00~18:00 (退场时间 19:00) ※ 宠物入场不可',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:11','2026-09-16 03:18:11',NULL,'可以停车','全年无休','2025-03-27 10:41:23'),(775,811,'zh','庆州市旅游特区(경주시 관광특구)','庆州是韩国内最大的旅游城市，整个城市就是巨大的户外博物馆，文化古迹随处可见。同时还是韩国代表性的历史文化之都，所走的每条路都是遗迹，所见的每处风景都是活生生的历史，游览庆州时的每一处都称为文化古迹也不为过。因此，于1994年将庆州市一带的市区、普门地区、佛国地区等地指定为旅游特区。庆州观光特区内有超过300处景点被指定为国家遗产，其中被列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产的景点也喝多。旅游特区内主要景点有佛国寺、石窟庵、大陵园等，还兼备庆州世界文化EXPO公园、庆州乐园、新罗千年公园等休闲娱乐设施。','庆尚北道庆州市镜鑑路614 (천군동)','各设施不同',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:11','2026-09-16 04:17:24',NULL,'各旅游景点和普门旅游区内，佛国寺一带等有26个公用停车场','各设施不同','2025-03-21 15:34:11'),(776,994,'zh','国立庆州博物馆 （국립경주박물관）','位于新罗千年古都——庆州的国立庆州博物馆是一座收藏者新罗文化遗产的韩国代表型博物馆。 国立庆州博物馆拥有60多年的历史传统，同时还运营着庆州儿童博物馆学校等各种教育活动，另设有儿童博物馆。 最近经过知名设计师的重新设计及改造，新罗历史馆及新罗美术馆以全新华丽的面貌重新迎接访客。 国立庆州博物馆的常设展厅有5个，可以细分为展示馆及展示场，访客们可以在此尽赏千年王国——新罗的灿烂文化艺术、国宝以及其他历史文物等。 [国立庆州博物馆特别展] 特别展示 : 古代韩国的外来文物 - 不同之美 展示时间 : 2021.11.24 ~ 2022.03.20 展示古代韩国与外界交流而留存下来的外来文物，通过这些文物可以看到古代与多种文化的碰撞及交流，神思今日的文化交流及国际化。 查看详情&nbsp; https://gyeongju.museum.go.kr/kor/html/sub02/0202.html?mode=VD&d_mng_no=179','庆尚北道庆州市日精路186号(仁旺洞)','观览时间: 10:00~18:00 (周日及公休日延长1个小时) ※ 截止入场时间 : 关门30分钟以前 夜间延长开馆 ~21:00 (每月最后一周周三, 3-12月每周六)','免费 ※ 但, 付费特别展示除外 ※ 为保护访客安全，维持观览秩序，访客需持免费观览券入场','2026-09-16 03:18:11','2026-09-16 03:18:11',NULL,'可以停车','元旦，春节及中秋节的当天','2025-01-03 11:38:54'),(777,804,'zh','普门湖보문호','根据庆州普门观光团地的开发规划，规模达1,652,900m²（50万坪）的人工湖——普门湖在庆州市东部明活山旧城址下修建了起来。随后周边国际水准的酒店和庆州乐园如雨后春笋般纷纷树立起来。环绕着普门湖的散步路和自行车路也成为了徒步旅行的热门路线，由于整个庆州到处都是樱花树，所以这里也毫不例外地成为了樱花树的海洋。在百花盛开的春天，普门湖周边和佛国寺公园的樱花盛放，微风拂过，一场“樱花雪”把这里点缀的异常美丽壮观。并且每年樱花最盛的4月，这里都会举行“庆州樱花马拉松大赛”。','庆尚北道庆州市普门路424-33新坪洞','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:12','2026-09-16 04:17:23',NULL,'可以停车','年中无休','2024-11-12 14:50:49'),(778,63,'zh','庆州文武大王陵 (경주 문무대왕릉)','新罗第30代文武王（在位661&sim;681）的水下王陵是新罗人创造性思维的体现。它位于东海奉吉里前海，距离海岸约200米，海平面以上的尺寸约为东西35米，南北36米，高度为5.3米。文武王继承了父亲太宗武烈王的业绩，灭亡高句丽，抵挡唐朝的侵略，实现了三国统一。此外，他还创立了兵部、长部等中央机构，为地方治理设立了五小经济道和九西堂十定义的军事制度，为国家体制的完善奠定了基础。实现三国统一的文武王，在临终前遗愿表示希望自己化身为龙，保护国家，抵御侵入的倭贼，因此他要求以佛教方式火化遗体，并将骨灰埋入东海。这块岩石被称为大王岩或大王石，而水下的王陵在全球范围内都是独一无二的。大王岩是利用自然岩石构建的，在岩石岛上东西南北方向开凿了十字形的人造水道，然后在中间挖出一个小池塘，形成一个港口。推测在水下2米深的地方放置了一块长3.7米、宽2.06米、厚0.9米的扁平龟形石头，下面安放着他的骨灰。文武王的儿子神文王在东海附近建立了感恩寺，并在法堂下设计了一个通向东海的排水道，以便化身为龙的文武王能够出入。','庆尚北道庆州市阳北面东海岸路1366-9','常时开放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:12','2026-09-16 04:17:23',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-10-11 09:09:28'),(779,805,'zh','骨窟寺（庆州）（골굴사(경주)）','这座寺庙位于矗立在庆州市区和东海之间的含月山上。拥有1500多年历史，12个石窟中保存着众多佛像。保持着韩国佛教的修行法&ldquo;禅武道&rdquo;传统，因此可以观看禅武道演出。还有寺庙寄宿项目，可以体验韩国寺庙文化。','庆尚北道庆州市阳北面祇林路101-5','常年开放',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:12','2026-09-16 03:18:12',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-10-07 16:59:02'),(780,858,'zh','庆州南山（경주 남산）','这座山矗立于庆州市区南部，海拔466米。庆州自始至终都是新罗王朝（BC57~AD935）的首都。新罗人认为这座矗立在首都的山十分神圣，留下了很多痕迹，至今还保留着许多文化遗产。因此，在这座山上，可以一边登山一边观赏文化遗产。','庆尚北道庆州市南山洞、拜洞','06:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:12','2026-09-16 03:18:12',NULL,'有','全年无休','2024-02-27 17:22:40'),(781,65,'zh','五柳细沙海边（오류고아라해변）','位于甘浦港附近的海水浴场，沙子柔软，可享受沙子桑拿，十分有名。绵延1公里的沙滩、较浅的水深和郁郁葱葱的松林，适合在此露营。松林内有露营场，可以体验房车及帐篷露营。夏季运营香蕉船和汽艇等海洋休闲设施，周边景点有松台末灯塔和甘浦海上公园。','庆尚北道庆州市甘浦邑五柳里277-8','海水浴场 09:00~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:18:12','2026-09-16 03:18:12',NULL,'有','全年无休（天气恶劣或出现有害生物时，将限制入海）','2024-02-23 10:01:34'),(782,5,'en','Oksan Sesim Village','Gyeongju Oksan Sesim Village is where the scholar Lee Eon-jeok dedicated himself to the study of Confucianism, boasting excellent cultural heritage, beautiful natural scenery, and generous hospitality. It is home to UNESCO World Heritage site Oksan Seowon, the Dokrakdang selected by KBS, and the 13-story stone pagoda of Jeonghyesaji, among others, holding over 200 national treasures, making it the most Korean village. The surrounding scenery of the village is so beautiful that it resembles a tranquil Eastern painting. Oksan Sesim Village features six themes: farm stay village, traditional theme village, rural leisure village, farm school village, food education specialized farm, and rural-20. Experience programs include traditional games (archery, making and kicking a jegi, ring toss), food experiences (making and eating kalguksu, making rice cakes, frying jeon, making tofu), cultural experiences (looking into the past, making kimchi), ecological experiences (handkerchief leaf dyeing), and harvest experiences (potatoes, sweet potatoes).','301-3 Oksanseowon-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round ※ For experience program inquiries, please call',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:19:53','2026-09-16 03:19:53',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(783,3,'en','Hanwha Resort Gyeongju','Hanwha Resort Gyeongju is a representative accommodation facility in the Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Complex, a UNESCO World Heritage site. The rooms are composed of Eton and Damton, and the resort features various amenities including a swimming pool, hot spring sauna, banquet hall, and seminar rooms. The rooms boast cleanliness and comfort, decorated in a modern and simple style to match contemporary sensibilities. The spacious rooms are equipped with various modern facilities, providing all conveniences for a comfortable stay through customer-oriented services.','182-27 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:19:53','2026-09-16 03:19:53',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(785,5,'ja','オクサンセシムマウル','慶州オクサンセシムマウルは、会齋イ・オンジョク先生が性理学の研究に専念していた場所で、優れた文化遺産と美しい自然景観、そして豊かな人情を誇る村です。ユネスコ世界文化遺産に指定されたオクサン書院やKBSが選定した独楽堂、正慧寺の13層石塔などがあり、国家指定の宝物が200点以上も保有されている、最も韓国らしい村です。村の周辺の景観は、一幅の静かな東洋画を思わせるほど美しいです。オクサンセシムマウルが持つテーマは、ファームステイ村、伝統テーマ村、農村休養村、ファームスクール村、食教育専門農場、ルーラル-20までの6つのテーマで構成されています。体験プログラムには、伝統遊び体験（弓矢、けん玉作り、輪投げ）、食体験（カルグクス作り、餅つき、チヂミ作り、豆腐作り）、文化体験（過去を見る、キムジャン）、生態体験（ハンカチの葉染め）、収穫体験（ジャガイモ、サツマイモ）があります。','慶尚北道慶州市安康邑オクサン書院路301-3','常時開放 ※ 体験プログラム利用は電話問い合わせ',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:19:59','2026-09-16 03:19:59',NULL,'可能','年中無休',NULL),(787,3,'ja','ハンファリゾート慶州','ハンファリゾート慶州は、世界的な文化遺産である慶州ボムンダンジの代表的な宿泊施設です。客室はエトンとダムトンで構成されており、プール、温泉サウナ、宴会場、セミナールームなど多様な付帯施設を備えています。客室は清潔さと快適さを誇り、現代的な感覚に合わせてモダンでシンプルに装飾されています。ゆったりとした余裕を感じられる客室には、さまざまな最新設備が整っており、顧客を一層考えたサービスを通じて快適に滞在できるよう、すべての便宜を提供しています。','慶尚北道慶州市ボムン路182-27 (北軍洞)',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:19:59','2026-09-16 03:19:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(790,5,'zh','玉山细心村','庆州玉山细心村是会齋李彦迪先生专注于理学研究的地方，是一个拥有优秀文化遗产和美丽自然景观，以及宽厚人情的村庄。村内有被联合国教科文组织列为世界文化遗产的玉山书院，以及KBS选定的独乐堂、正惠寺13层石塔等，拥有国家指定的宝物200余件，是最具韩国特色的村庄。村庄周围的景观如同一幅宁静的东方画，十分美丽。玉山细心村的主题包括农场住宿村、传统主题村、农村休闲村、农场学校村、食育专业农场、乡村-20等6个主题。体验项目包括传统游戏体验（射箭、制作并踢毽子、投环）、食物体验（制作并品尝刀削面、捶年糕、煎饼、制作豆腐）、文化体验（回顾过去、腌制泡菜）、生态体验（手帕叶子染色）、收获体验（马铃薯、红薯）。','庆尚北道庆州市安康邑玉山书院路301-3','常年开放 ※ 体验项目需电话咨询',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:20:06','2026-09-16 03:20:06',NULL,'可用','全年无休',NULL),(793,3,'zh','汉华度假村庆州','汉华度假村庆州是世界文化遗产庆州博文观光区的代表性住宿设施。客房分为艾顿和丹顿，配备游泳池、温泉桑拿、宴会厅、会议室等多种附属设施。客房以干净和舒适为特点，现代感十足，装饰简约时尚。宽敞的客房配备了多种最新设施，通过考虑客户的服务，提供所有便利，让客人能够舒适地入住。','庆尚北道庆州市博文路182-27 (北军洞)',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:20:06','2026-09-16 03:20:06',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(794,881,'en','Tohamsan Natural Recreation Forest','Tohamsan Natural Recreation Forest is located at the eastern foot of Tohamsan, which houses Bulguksa Temple and Seokguram Grotto, and is operated by the Gyeongju Facility Management Corporation. The facility includes forest houses, Hwarang Hall, camping sites, sports facilities (futsal field, foot volleyball court, basketball court), forest trails (hiking paths), and forest bathing areas. Various coniferous and broadleaf trees grow naturally, and a variety of wildlife such as squirrels and woodpeckers create an ecosystem, making it a popular destination for nature experience learning and recreation. It is centrally located between Gampo Beach, Yangnam Jusangjeolli, Yangbuk King Munmu\'s Tomb to the east, and Bulguksa Temple, Seokguram Grotto, and Bomun Tourist Complex to the west, making it a highly regarded accommodation facility for enjoying both historical and cultural experiences and relaxation.','1208-45 Bulguk-ro, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(795,99,'en','Tohamsan','Tohamsan is the second highest mountain after Dansuksan in Gyeongju and is one of the five sacred mountains revered by the Silla people. Being close to the sea, the mountain is often shrouded in mist, which is said to resemble the mountain drinking and exhaling the fog, hence the name Tohamsan. It is a mountain where one can see the splendid heritage of Silla Buddhist art, such as Bulguksa and Seokguram. Additionally, Tohamsan is a gentle mountain, making it suitable for light hiking, and the sunrise view from the summit is spectacular.','238 Seokgul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Gyeongju National Park parking lot (Seokguram parking lot, Girimsa parking lot / Paid)',NULL,NULL),(796,35,'en','Baekryulsa Temple (Gyeongju)','Baekryulsa Temple, located on the slopes of Sogeumgangsan in northern Gyeongju, is a temple dedicated to the martyrdom of Lee Chadon, who died for the recognition of Buddhism in the 14th year of King Beopheung\'s reign (527). According to records from the time of King Heondeok, Lee Chadon was martyred while fulfilling the king\'s command to establish Buddhism and build temples. After being beheaded, strange occurrences such as white blood gushing from his neck and flower rain were reported. Even the ministers who opposed the recognition of Buddhism changed their minds after witnessing this. It is said that Lee Chadon\'s wife built a shrine at the spot where his head fell to pray for his soul. Baekryulsa is presumed to be this shrine. The temple was rebuilt after being burned during the Imjin War, and some parts of its foundation retain the style of the Silla period. The gilt-bronze statue of the Medicine Buddha that was once enshrined in the main hall was created around the same time as the gilt-bronze Amitabha and Vairocana statues at Bulguksa Temple, and these three statues are known as the three great gilt-bronze Buddhas of the Unified Silla period. The gilt-bronze Medicine Buddha statue and Lee Chadon\'s stone altar are housed in the National Gyeongju Museum.','4214-110, Sanjeong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(797,59,'en','Gyeongju Seokbinggo','Seokbinggo is a storage facility for ice, located on the northern wall of the Banwolseong in Gyeongju, stretching north-south. Upon entering through the entrance on the south, visitors descend via stairs. The floor slopes inward to allow for drainage. The roof is semi-circular with three ventilation ducts to allow outside air in. According to the stone monument and the entrance stone, it is recorded that in the 14th year of King Yeongjo (1738), Jo Myeong-gyeom constructed a stone ice storage facility from a wooden one, and four years later, it was moved to its current location from the west, indicating that it dates back to that time. It is also regarded as an outstanding masterpiece in terms of scale and technique.','449-1 Inwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(798,34,'en','Gyeongju Poseokjeong Site','Poseokjeong, located on the west side of Namsan in Gyeongju, was one of the palaces prepared for the king to enjoy drinking, but currently, there is no pavilion, only the waterway where the pleasure was enjoyed remains. It is believed to have been constructed during the reign of Heongangwang, the 49th king of Silla (875–886). The dimensions are approximately 35cm wide, an average depth of 26cm, and a total length of about 10m. Poseokjeong originated from the ancient Chinese custom of holding a ceremony to drive away evil spirits by floating wine cups in a winding stream. In 353, Wang Hee-ji wrote in the \'Nanjeongseomun\' that clear stream water flowed in nine bends, and wine cups were floated in the flowing water, and if a poem was not composed before the wine cup passed through all nine bends, three cups of punishment wine had to be drunk. The surroundings of the place where the ceremony was enjoyed were high and rugged mountains, with forests and bamboo groves, and a clear stream flowed beside it. Thus, Silla created Poseokjeong in a valley with dense bamboo and pine groves, backed by the rugged peaks of Namsan. Originally, there was a large stone shaped like a turtle at the entrance of the Namsan valley, from which water was made to flow, but it has now disappeared, and its exact shape is unknown. According to the \'Samguk Yusa\', Heongangwang came here and created the dance of the Namsan deity, called Eomusangsimmu. This place was also a beautiful location where people cultivated their minds, the Hwarang trained their spirits, composed poetry, and felt the emotions of the world. In 927, King Gyeongae of Silla held a feast here and was captured by the attack of Gyeon Hwon of Later Baekje, leading to his suicide, marking a disgrace in the thousand-year history of Silla. The Hwarangsegi manuscript refers to Poseokjeong as Poseoksa, and in 1998, many artifacts were excavated 50m south, revealing that there was a large building here. It is also suggested that Poseokjeong was a sacred place where rituals for the country\'s peace were conducted, rather than just a place for enjoying banquets. The entrance Poseokjeong Visitor Center screens models and videos to help understand Poseokjeong.','454-3 Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Summer season (March–October): 09:00–18:00. Winter season (November–February): 09:00–17:00.',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(799,94,'en','Geumgwan Tomb','This name comes from the gold crown excavated from the site. It was accidentally discovered in September 1921 during house construction, but since the tomb had already been destroyed and not formally excavated, the structure of the tomb and the exact situation of the artifacts have not been clarified. The excavated items include a gold crown, jewelry, weapons, and vessels, with over 30,000 beads found in total. The original form of Geumgwan Tomb is about 50m in diameter and 13m in height, known as a stone mound tomb that existed only during the Silla period, and it is speculated that there was a wooden coffin inside. Based on this structure and the influence of Buddhism, it is presumed to be a royal tomb created in the 6th century, around the time of King Jijeung (智證王).','15 Bonghwang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00 (Last admission 17:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(800,809,'en','Oksan Seowon (Gyeongju)','Oksan Seowon in Gyeongju is dedicated to the Confucian scholar Hoijae Lee Eon-jeok from the Joseon Dynasty, whose teachings were passed down to Toegye Lee Hwang, making him a pioneer of the Yeongnam School of Confucianism. To honor this teacher, the Gyeongju governor Lee Je-min established it in the 5th year of King Seonjo (1572), and the following year it received the name \'Oksan\' from the king, becoming a government-designated seowon. The layout follows the traditional style of \'jeonghakhu-myo\' with the study hall Guindang in front and the ritual hall Cheinmyo behind. Guindang is a gabled roof building that was destroyed by fire in the 5th year of King Heonjong (1839) and was rebuilt. Other buildings include the main gate Yeoknakmun, the two-story building Mubyunru, the dormitory for students Dongjae Min-gujae, and the study room Amsujae. Oksan Seowon is one of the 47 government-designated seowons that survived the seowon abolition decree of Heungseon Daewongun in the late Joseon period, allowing the preservation of the teacher\'s writings as well as valuable books from renowned scholars throughout history.','Gyeongsangbuk-do, Gyeongju-si, Angang-eup, Oksan Seowon-gil 216-27','Summer season (April–September): 09:00–18:00. Winter season (October–March): 09:00–17:00.',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(801,861,'en','Danseoksan Mountain','Danseoksan Mountain (827.2m) is the highest mountain in Gyeongju and was a strategic defense point for Silla against Baekje. It is loved by mountain enthusiasts in spring for its azalea colonies and is a popular hiking course along with the nearby Joraebong Peak. Additionally, there is a natural cave surrounded by four rocks at about 70-80% of the mountain\'s slope, which was once called Sangin Rock. The Hwarang carved a Buddha statue inside this rock cave and covered it with a roof to create a stone temple. This temple is called Sinseonsa (神仙寺) or Danseoksa (斷石寺). The stone Buddha statue inside is designated as a national treasure.','Bangnae-ri, Geoncheon-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Gyeongju National Park entry hours: summer season (April–October) 04:00–16:00; winter season (November–March) 05:00–15:00.',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(802,76,'en','Gyeongju Hwangnyongsa','Hwangnyongsa was built in the 6th century during the Silla period and was destroyed by the Mongol invasion in the 13th century, leaving only the site to imagine its scale. It is estimated to have been a large temple covering an area of 8,800 pyeong, eight times larger than Bulguksa. Construction began in 553 (14th year of King Jinheung) by royal decree, and the main halls were completed in 566, with the main hall finished in 584 (6th year of King Jinpyeong). By the 14th year of Queen Seondeok (645), Hwangnyongsa was completed, becoming the center of Silla\'s national faith. Within Hwangnyongsa, there was the Hwangnyongsa Seven-Story Wooden Pagoda, one of the treasures of Silla, which was completed in three years by the monk Jajang, who returned from studying in Tang China, at the suggestion of the Baekje king Abiji. Currently, the central pillar base stone, which supported the pagoda, remains at the site where the pagoda once stood. This temple was located east of the Silla royal palace, Wolseong, and according to its founding record, King Jinheung intended to build a new palace in the low area east of Wolseong but stopped upon seeing a dragon ascending from that place, leading him to establish a temple instead, naming it Hwangnyongsa. As a national temple, it frequently hosted the movements of successive kings and held the top position among Silla\'s national temples. Even after the fall of Silla, it continued to receive deep reverence and protection from the Goryeo dynasty, with timber provided for the repair of the pagoda. However, in 1238 (25th year of Gojong), the pagoda and all buildings were burned down due to the invasion of the Mongol army. In 1969, excavations revealed the foundation stones of the main hall, lecture hall, and pagoda site, and from March 1976, an eight-year excavation project revealed a unique layout of a single pagoda and three main halls, with over 40,000 artifacts unearthed. While the lower structure of the buildings, including the base, has been confirmed, the upper structure has not been accurately verified, so a complete restoration has not been achieved, and only the base with 64 foundation stones has been restored. Next to the Hwangnyongsa site, there is the Hwangnyongsa History and Culture Center, which consists of a 3D audiovisual room depicting the process from the establishment to the destruction of Hwangnyongsa and an exhibition hall displaying artifacts unearthed during the excavation, with a model pagoda of Hwangnyongsa at one-tenth scale on the first floor.','772, GuHwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(803,865,'en','Mauna Ocean Resort Blue Water','Blue Water Spa, located within Mauna Ocean Resort, is the first high-end spa facility in the Yeongnam region. It features an indoor water pool, outdoor swimming pool, sauna, and more, making it a popular destination for families to enjoy relaxation and leisure together. With both indoor and outdoor water play facilities, it attracts many visitors looking to unwind with their children.','982 Dongnam-ro, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Varies by season, please refer to the website',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Varies by season, please refer to the website',NULL),(804,801,'en','Gyeongju Gyerim','Gyeongju Gyerim is located between Cheomseongdae and Wolseong, and is a historic site where the legendary founder of the Gyeongju Kim clan, Alji, was said to have been born. During the reign of King Talhae of Silla, a man named Hoegong heard a rooster crowing in this forest, and upon approaching, he found a golden chest shining on a branch. He reported this to the king, who personally visited the forest and retrieved the chest. When he opened the lid, a baby boy emerged, and he was given the surname Kim and the name Alji, leading to the forest, originally called Shirim and Gurim, being referred to as Gyerim. Gyerim also became associated with the national name of Silla. The king made Alji the crown prince, but later the throne was succeeded by the Park clan\'s King Pasa, and Alji did not become king. From the reign of King Naemul onwards, the Kim clan of Silla inherited the throne. The stele in the area was erected in the 3rd year of King Sunjo of Joseon (1803) and records the birth of Kim Alji. Located near the royal palace of Silla, Gyerim is considered a sacred site as the birthplace of the Silla Kim royal family. Even today, the royal zelkova and elm trees grow thickly, shading the sky, and a small stream flows gently from the north to the west. In spring, yellow canola flowers bloom along the walking path that connects Daereungwon, Gyerim, and Banwolsong, enhancing the charm of the historical site.','Gyeongsangbuk-do, Gyeongju-si, Gyodong','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(808,45,'en','Seochulji, Gyeongju','In the 10th year of King Soji of Silla, in the year 488, during a full moon procession, a crow and a rat appeared and the rat said, \'Watch where this crow goes.\' The king sent a general to follow it. Upon reaching the pond near Dongnam Mountain, the general lost sight of the crow. Suddenly, an old man dressed in grass appeared in the middle of the pond, holding an envelope. \'You must deliver this message to the king,\' he said, handing over the envelope before disappearing into the water. When the king opened the envelope, it read, \'If you open it, two people will die; if you do not, one person will die.\' A minister suggested, \'The two refer to commoners, and the one refers to the king; perhaps it would be wise to open it.\' Following the minister\'s advice, the king opened the envelope, which instructed him to \'shoot the guqin box.\' The king then drew his bow towards the guqin box placed in the queen\'s chamber. Inside the box was a monk who had conspired with the queen to harm King Soji. The queen was executed, and the king was spared thanks to the envelope given by the old man. This pond is called Seochulji because it is where the envelope with the message emerged. The 10th year of King Soji was 40 years before Buddhism was recognized in Silla. During the reign of King Nulji, the monk Mukhoja came to spread Buddhism but was unsuccessful. Similarly, during King Soji\'s reign, Monk Ado also failed to propagate Buddhism. It was only after the martyrdom of Lee Chadon in the 15th year of King Beopheung that Buddhism was officially recognized in Silla. At that time, the Silla aristocracy strongly adhered to folk beliefs, especially ancestor worship, making it difficult to accept Buddhism. The legend of Seochulji illustrates a facet of the conflict arising from the introduction of new Buddhist culture within traditional folk beliefs.','974-1, Namsan-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(809,24,'en','Gyeongju Baedong Samneung','Gyeongju Baedong Samneung consists of three royal tombs lined up east-west on the western foothills of Gyeongju Namsan. It is said to be the tombs of three kings of the Park clan: King Adalla (8th king of Silla), King Sinduk (53rd king), and King Gyeongmyeong (54th king). All the tombs are in the form of round mounds made of piled earth. The middle tomb, said to be that of King Sinduk, was looted in 1953 and 1963, and upon investigation, it was confirmed to be a stone chamber tomb (horizontal stone chamber tomb). The walls of the tomb have some color painted on the east and west walls, resembling folding screens, which is noteworthy as it is the first discovery of such coloring in Silla tombs in Gyeongju that do not have murals. The colors are red, yellow, white, blue, and dark blue, and there are 12 panels. Although it is said that the protagonists of Gyeongju Baedong Samneung are the three kings of the Park clan, there are no definitive records, and there is a gap of over 700 years between the early Silla kings Adalla, Sinduk, and Gyeongmyeong, making it difficult to accept that their tombs are gathered in one place. Additionally, such large tombs did not exist in early Silla. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','73-1 Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(810,93,'en','Gyeongju Najung','This is a well that holds the legend of the birth of Park Hyeokgeose, the founder of Silla. Remnants include a monument honoring Park Hyeokgeose, an octagonal building site presumed to be a shrine, well site, wall site, auxiliary building site, and drainage system. In particular, the octagonal building site, which has a side length of 8m and is surrounded by a square wall, is presumed to be a shrine of Silla, and it can be inferred that Najung was a temple where offerings were made to Park Hyeokgeose. There is a record about Najung: The village chiefs of the six clans, who were the main figures in the founding of Silla, gathered to elect a ruler and decide on the capital. They ascended to a high place, and near the well called Najung, a strange aura was present, and a white horse was kneeling. When they approached, the horse ascended to the sky, leaving behind a large red egg, and when they broke the egg, a young boy emerged. It is said that when they bathed him in the Dongcheon River, he radiated light, and birds and beasts danced around him, causing the heavens and earth to tremble and the sun and moon to become clear. Because he was born from an egg resembling a gourd, his surname was Park (朴), and he was named Hyeokgeose (赫居世) meaning \'to brighten the world.\' When he turned 13, in 57 BC, he ascended to the throne and named the kingdom Searabal.','700-1 Tapdong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(811,872,'en','Unification Hall (Gyeongju)','Unification Hall is a national hall that inherits the spirit of the unification of the Three Kingdoms and wishes for the upcoming unification of North and South Korea. Inside, portraits of King Taejong Muyeol, King Munmu, and General Kim Yushin are enshrined, and records depicting fierce battles for unification are displayed along a long corridor. Built to honor the spirits of the fallen soldiers, it serves as an ideological education center for elementary and middle school students and has become a must-visit on school trips. The battle scenes from the unification of the Three Kingdoms are impressively depicted in various frames, and it is also nice to pay respects to the spirits of the fallen soldiers and rest on the wide lawn during a visit to Namsan.','6 Chilbulam-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00 (Last admission 17:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','Closed every Monday, January 1, and on the days of Lunar New Year and Chuseok.',NULL),(812,74,'en','Gyeongju Wonseong Wangneung','Wonseong Wangneung is located in a low hill south of a pine forest and is presumed to be the tomb of Wonseong Wang, the 38th king of Silla (reigned 785-798). Wonseong Wang\'s name was Gyeongsin, and he was a descendant of King Naemul. He established the new examination system and expanded the Byeokgolje. Before the royal tomb was built, there was originally a small pond, and according to a legend that the king\'s body was hung above the water surface for burial without changing the pond\'s appearance, it was named Gwaereung. This mound is a round earthen mound with a diameter of about 23m and a height of about 6m. Surrounding the mound is a protective stone with 12 zodiac figures carved on it. In front of the mound, there are four square stone statues, and about 80m away from them, pairs of stone lions, civil officials, and military officials, as well as a pair of stone markers indicating the tomb, are facing each other. The carving techniques of these stone structures are considered among the best in Silla sculptures, particularly the powerful-looking military stone figures, which some claim resemble Persian faces. The burial system of Wonseong Wangneung was influenced by the Tang Dynasty, but the detailed techniques, such as the arrangement of the 12 zodiac figures on the surrounding stones, are unique to Silla. Additionally, the outstanding carving techniques seen in various stone artifacts well represent the artistic level of the Silla people. (Source: Gyeongju City Hall Cultural Tourism Website)','139, Singyeipshil-gil, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(813,77,'en','Gyeongju Gujeong-dong Square Tomb','The Gyeongju Gujeong-dong Square Tomb is a tomb from the Unified Silla period located on the northern hillside along the road to Bulguksa. This square tomb has a side length of 9.5m and a height of 2m. The tomb is square-shaped, and beneath the earthen mound, there is a protective stone with 12 zodiac figures carved on it. The arrangement of the surrounding stones is a tradition that has been passed down since the Three Kingdoms period, and it is common to see surrounding stones with 12 zodiac figures carved in the royal tombs of the Gyeongju region during the Unified Silla period. Inside the tomb, there is a rectangular stone chamber tomb (horizontal stone chamber tomb) slightly offset to the south of the mound. On the eastern wall of the burial chamber, there is a passageway (entrance). Artifacts such as gold crown ornaments, silver belt buckles, and silver leaf were unearthed. Based on the arrangement of the surrounding stones, the use of stone coffins, and the carving techniques of the 12 zodiac figures, it is believed to be a tomb of the highest aristocracy from the late Unified Silla period. It is the only square tomb among Silla tombs, and while its lineage is unknown, it is evaluated as a pioneering form of square tombs with surrounding stones that appeared in the early Goryeo period.','15-5, Bulguk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(814,73,'en','Gyeongju Igyundae','There are two significant places to observe Daewangam. One is Igyundae located in front of Daebon Elementary School, and the other is the site of the monument \'My Unforgettable Sea\' under the Donghae-gu sign. Igyundae is where King Munmu, who rejected the splendid royal tombs to become a dragon of the East Sea to protect the country, is said to have transformed into a dragon, and his son, King Sinmun, obtained the invaluable treasure Manpasikjeok. The name Igyundae is derived from the \'Yijing\' phrase \'Feilong Zaitian Lijian Daren\' (飛龍在天 利見大人), and the current building was recently constructed based on the foundation revealed during excavations in 1970. If you go down under the Donghae-gu sign, you will see the monument \'My Unforgettable Sea\', erected by the students of the late U Hyun-goo in 1985 to honor his anti-Japanese spirit. Reflecting on King Munmu\'s will to defend the country against the invasions of the Japanese pirates during the Unified Silla period, the poem \'Daewangam\' written by U Hyun-goo and the monument \'My Unforgettable Sea\' are placed side by side, facing Daewangam, adding deeper meaning.','12-14, Daebit-gil, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(815,56,'en','Yeongji Stone Buddha Statue','The Yeongji Stone Buddha Statue is located in Gwaenung-ri, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a seated stone Buddha with a halo carved on the pedestal and the back of the body, although some parts of the halo and head are severely worn, making it difficult to recognize its shape. The robust body, waist, and voluminous knee expressions well represent the style of Unified Silla. The right hand is positioned with the fingertips pointing to the ground, while the left hand rests on the left knee with the palm facing outward. The delicate and beautiful octagonal lotus pedestal and the halo carved from a single stone with the Buddha depict a small Buddha intricately carved within a chaotic flame pattern, showcasing the appearance of that time well. There is a story that a woman named Asan-nyo, who waited for Asadal, the creator of the Seokgatap at Bulguksa, threw herself to death, and Asadal made this statue for her, but the exact details are unknown.','1297-7 Gwaenung-ri, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(816,43,'en','Gampo Port','Gampo Port is the largest port in Gyeongju, celebrating its 100th anniversary in 2025. The port area is always bustling with fishing boats, and fresh fish are auctioned daily at the live fish market. Gampo Maritime Park, established in 2018 at the breakwater of Gampo Port, features a coastal deck, a pinwheel hill, and sculptures of Gampo Port. Additionally, a beautiful lighthouse, designed to resemble the three-story stone pagoda of Gamunsaji, stands tall at the breakwater, making it a famous spot for sea fishing. Nearby attractions include Jeonchon Yonggul, Oryu Goara Beach, and Jeonchon Port, which can be visited together.','Gampo-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(817,890,'en','Najung Beautiful Sand Beach','Najung Beautiful Sand Beach boasts a wide sandy beach with calm sand and the pristine waters of the East Sea. It offers ample surrounding space and various nearby amenities, as well as a seawater bath where visitors can enjoy hot springs using the sea water. Next to the seawater bath, there is parking space and a pine forest, and water sports such as motor boating and banana boating can be enjoyed, making it a great summer getaway for families and friends. There is also a well-developed walking path along the beach, perfect for strolling while enjoying the view of the sea.','1915 Donghaean-ro, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open all year round',NULL),(818,862,'en','Jeonchon Solbat Beach','Jeonchon Solbat Beach is a small pine forest beach located between Jeonchon Port and Najung Fine Sand Beach. The white sandy beach, 0.8 km long and 30 to 60 m wide, is not very large, so it is not famous as a swimming beach, but it connects to the adjacent Najung Fine Sand Beach, creating a long stretch of sand. It is equipped with facilities such as restaurants, cafes, and showers, attracting tourists looking for a quiet beach experience. On the opposite side, Jeonpo Port is popular among sea fishermen, and nearby restaurants serve fresh seafood dishes caught that day. The area also has attractions such as Jeonchon Cave and hot spring baths using seawater from the East Sea, providing a well-rounded tourist experience with sights, food, and activities.','2006-2 Donghaean-ro, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available, Fee (Free)','Open year-round ※ May be closed due to bad weather or harmful organisms',NULL),(819,20,'en','Gyeongju King Sinmun\'s Tomb','This is the tomb of King Sinmun (reigned 681-692), the 31st king of Silla. King Sinmun was the son of King Munmu and worked to integrate the people of the former Baekje and Goguryeo. He established the National Academy, a national educational institution, abolished the practice of providing land to the nobility, and distributed official salaries. To govern the provinces, he divided the country into nine regions and established small cities in five important locations. After King Sinmun\'s death, it is said that a funeral was held east of Nangsang. This tomb is located at the southern end of Nangsang. The tomb is a round mound with a height of 7.6m and a diameter of 29.3m, made by piling up earth. The surrounding stones at the edge of the tomb are shaped like bricks and stacked in five layers, with a cover stone placed on top. A trapezoidal stone is supported on the outside. The upper part of the support stone placed to the south is inscribed with the character \'문 (gate)\', indicating that this is the entrance to the tomb chamber.','453-1 Baeban-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(820,15,'en','Gyeongju Janghang-ri West Five-Story Stone Pagoda','The Janghang-ri site is located in Janghang-ri, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju, on the eastern side of Tohamsan. The exact name of the temple is unknown, so it is referred to as Janghang-ri Site after the name of the village. There were an east pagoda and a west pagoda centered around the main hall, but only the west pagoda, which was possible to restore after being collapsed by tomb raiders, was newly restored in 1932. This 9m tall five-story stone pagoda is a large-scale pagoda that shows typical characteristics of Silla-era stone pagodas, featuring a double base. The upper part only retains the base, while the lower base is relatively wide, providing stability. The four sides of the first-floor body stone are adorned with two pairs of doors carved in the shape of goblins, and each side intricately depicts a pair of guardian deities, showcasing a rare technique. Based on the carving technique, it is evaluated as a work from the 8th century. The overall proportions are beautiful, and the carving technique is excellent, making it a masterpiece that shows a new style of stone pagoda from the early 8th century, and it is a valuable resource for the study of Silla stone pagodas.','Janghang-ri, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(821,61,'en','Gyeongju Baedong Seokjo Yerae Samjon Ipsang','This stone Buddha was gathered and erected in its current location in 1923 from various places scattered at the foot of Namsan in Gyeongju. These stone figures appear to have originally been enshrined as a triad. The central main Buddha has a topknot-shaped head (ushnisha) that is uniquely double-layered, and its surface is smoothly expressed. The square face with a childlike expression is plump, with round eyebrows, eyes looking upward, a closed mouth, deeply carved dimples, and chubby cheeks, all conveying a gentle and compassionate Buddha nature. The cylindrical body, without a defined neck, has large hands, with the left hand lowered and the right hand raised. The heavy-looking robe gives the statue a rigid appearance, but the childlike expression and body convey a warm sense of life. The bodhisattva on the left wears a crown and has a smile on their face, with a slender waist that adds a sense of three-dimensionality. The right hand is placed on the chest while the left hand holds a treasure bottle, indicating that this bodhisattva is Avalokiteshvara. The bodhisattva on the right also depicts a serene inner smile, with a heavily treated body adorned with a thick necklace and beaded decorations down to the ankles. This work, evaluated as a representative piece of 7th-century Silla Buddhist sculpture, exudes a human warmth while also radiating an untouchable religious mystery.','San 65-1 Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(822,89,'en','The-K Gyeongju Hotel Spa Oncheon','The-K Gyeongju Hotel Spa Oncheon is located within the Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Complex, a historical city of Silla. The hotel opened in June 2001 and features a spa world with facilities such as a sauna, outdoor bath, gym, and swimming pool. The self-developed hot spring water is 100% natural, sourced from 630m underground, with a rich supply of 900 tons per day, and is known for its high temperature and the presence of natural sodium, chlorine, and sulfide components due to the dissolution of the constituent rocks and the mixing of hydrogen sulfide. Additionally, it is known to be effective for rheumatism, neuralgia, muscle pain, skin diseases, and anti-aging due to the removal of heavy metals and impurities from the water through devices.','45 Expo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Sinpyeong-dong)','06:00~21:00 (Last admission at 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Closed every Monday',NULL),(823,38,'en','Songcheom Jongtaek, Yangdong Village, Gyeongju','Songcheom Jongtaek in Yangdong Village, Gyeongju, is the main house of the Son family, established by the founder Yangmin-gong Son So (1433–1484) in the 15th year of King Seongjong\'s reign (1484). It is also the birthplace of Yangmin-gong\'s son, Son Jung-don, and his grandson, Lee Eon-jeok (1491–1553). The main gate is in a straight line with the inner house, and behind the sarangchae (men\'s quarters) is a high area with a shrine and a spirit house. The inner house features a hip-and-gable roof with eight sides, while the sarangchae has a gable roof shaped like a person. The sarangbang (guest room) and sleeping room are arranged in an L-shape with a daecheong (main room) in between, and the garden behind the sarangchae has a centuries-old incense tree. Typically, a small sarangbang is placed opposite a large one, but this house has a small sarangbang positioned at a corner to avoid facing the other rooms, which is noteworthy. The design also features a kind of corridor style, which is unique. The house is well-structured and has a beautiful garden behind the sarangchae, making it an important resource for studying traditional houses from the early Joseon period. While the national heritage is generally open for viewing, access may be restricted due to personal circumstances of the owners, so it is advisable to inquire by phone before visiting.','75-6, Yangdong Village Road, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Summer season (April–September): 09:00–19:00; ticket sales close at 18:00. Winter season (October–March): 09:00–18:00; ticket sales close at 17:00. Private homes may not be entered without the owner’s permission; call before visiting.',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','- Village open year-round - Cultural center closed every Monday',NULL),(824,852,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Yongjangsa Temple Stone Buddha','The Gyeongju Namsan Yongjangsa Temple Stone Buddha is a statue carved on a rock face at the site of Yongjangsa Temple on Namsan Mountain in Gyeongju. Along with this statue, the site also features a three-story stone pagoda (Treasure No. 186) and a stone seated Buddha (Treasure No. 187). The statue\'s head is intricately carved with small spiral-shaped hair, and the ushnisha, which appears like a topknot, is large and rounded. The face, with clearly defined eyes, nose, and mouth, displays a gentle smile. The folds of the robe are depicted with densely drawn parallel lines. The right hand rests on the knees with the fingertips pointing to the ground, while the left hand is placed on the abdomen. The halo around the head and body is represented with two lines. There are inscriptions about 10 characters long carved on the outer part of the left shoulder, with the front part reading as \'August of the 2nd year of Taepyeong\' (太平二年八月). Therefore, this stone seated Buddha is estimated to have been created in 977 or 1022.','1-1 Yongjang-ri, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(825,855,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Yongjangsa Temple Three-Story Stone Pagoda','Yongjangsa is well-known as the place where the scholar Kim Si-seup wrote \'Geumosanhwa\'. Currently, only a few stone structures remain, hinting at its past as a temple site. This pagoda stands on a two-tiered base on a high peak of the eastern rocky mountain that surrounds the temple. The lower tier is made of natural rock, with the upper tier placed directly on top. Thus, the natural rock could serve as the lower tier, or the entire underlying mountain could also be considered the lower tier. The upper tier is adorned with pillar carvings at the four corners and center, covered with two stone slabs to finish the base. The pagoda body is constructed with separate stones for the roof and body. The first tier is relatively tall, while the size decreases sharply from the second tier. The roof stone has four layers of support on the underside, and the eaves form a straight line that gracefully curves up at the corners. The original top ornament is missing, leaving only a hole where a metal rod was once inserted. It was reconstructed in 1922 after having fallen, and it is said that the sarira container has been missing for a long time. The harmony of each part is beautiful, and it is a representative work of the late Unified Silla period, harmonizing with the surrounding nature. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','1-1 Yongjang-ri, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Gyeongju National Park: summer season (April–October) 04:00–16:00; winter season (November–March) 05:00–15:00. Access may be restricted due to weather.',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(826,29,'en','Gyeongju Namsandong East and West Three-Story Stone Pagoda','These two pagodas, built in the east and west, are unique examples of paired pagodas that differ in style from the Seokgatap and Dabotap of Bulguksa. The east pagoda adopts the style of a stone pagoda made of brick-shaped stones, while the west pagoda follows the typical three-story pagoda style. The base stone of the east pagoda is widely laid in a double layer, and on top of that, eight well-carved stones are fitted together to form the base (gidanbu). The body and roof stones of the pagoda are made from single stones each. The roof stone has five layers of eaves and rainwater surfaces, just like a brick-style pagoda. The west pagoda has a three-story body built on top of the upper base, with two layers of the base divided into two on one side, where the Eight Guardian Deities are carved. The Eight Guardian Deities appeared after the middle period of Silla and are not merely decorative but express a belief that the pagoda represents the world of Buddha, Mount Sumeru. The body and roof stones of the pagoda are made from single stones, and corner pillars are carved on each layer. The underside of the roof stone has five layers of eaves. While paired pagodas from the Unified Silla period are generally made in the same style, these east and west pagodas are expressed in different styles, making them a rare sight while maintaining overall harmony. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','227-3 Namsan-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(827,72,'en','Gyeongju Talhae Wangneung','Gyeongju Talhae Wangneung is the tomb of Talhae Wang, the 4th king of Silla (reigned 57-80), located in Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, surrounded by a pine forest. The tomb itself is typical, but it is significant as the first stone royal tomb of Silla. This tomb is a round earthen mound, approximately 4.5m high and 14.3m in diameter. No facilities have been constructed around it, and it is presumed to be a stone chamber tomb. At the entrance of the royal tomb, there is a shrine called Sungsinjeon for the rituals of Talhae Wang. Talhae Wang became the first stone king of Silla at the age of 62 and passed away 24 years later. There is a legend about the king: the queen of the country of Dapana (or Wanha, Yongseong) located 1,000 li northeast of Japan gave birth to a large egg after 7 years of pregnancy. Considering it an inauspicious event, the egg was placed in a box and thrown into the sea, reaching the eastern sea at Ajinpo. At that time, an old woman opened it and found a child, whom she raised. Since magpies followed the child, the name Talhae (탈해) was given by taking the character for \'magpie\' (작) and replacing it with \'stone\' (석). Talhae Wang is regarded as the ancestor of the Seok clan and the first stone king of Silla.','San 17, Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available (approximately 80 small cars / 8 large cars)','Open year-round',NULL),(828,52,'en','Gyeongju Mangdeoksa Site','Located at the foot of Nangsang (Wolf Mountain) in Gyeongju, this temple site faces the Four Heavenly Kings Temple. The exact date of its establishment is unclear, but it is said to date back to the reign of King Munmu or King Sinmun of Silla. The current temple site features the remains of the east and west wooden pagodas, the main hall and lecture hall to the north, the middle gate to the south, and the surrounding cloister, showcasing the typical twin-tower layout of the Unified Silla period. Additionally, the stairway remains well-preserved to the south of the middle gate, and the stone pillars for the temple flagpole (treasure) are still intact to the west. This temple was one of the important temples in Gyeongju, along with Hwangnyongsa, Sacheonwangsa, and Hwangboksasa, making it significant.','956 Baeban-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(829,1015,'en','Dongguk University Wise Campus Museum','The Dongguk University Wise Campus Museum is operated by Dongguk University, which is based on Buddhist spirit and aims to cultivate scholarship and character. Located in Seokjang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, the museum was opened in 1983 for the purpose of collecting, organizing, and exhibiting Buddhist relics, as well as conducting archaeological excavations and research. Initially, it used the 3rd and 4th floors of the library building and started as the Gyeongju branch of the Dongguk University Museum. In April 1985, the exhibition hall was expanded and relocated to the 2nd floor of the library, and in 1994, the office and auxiliary facilities were expanded next to the exhibition hall, reaching its current state. The museum consists of an exhibition hall, storage room, research room, and office. Its collection mainly includes Buddhist-related sculptures, paintings, and crafts, along with artifacts excavated from the Gyeongju area, totaling about 3,000 items, including 483 metal items, 311 jade items, 1,622 pottery items, and 99 calligraphy items. Additionally, the museum has excavated Seokjangsa and Cheonryongsa sites on Namsan Mountain in Gyeongju, and in 1994, discovered the Geumjangdae petroglyphs in Seokjang-dong in collaboration with the archaeological art history department and excavation team. In 2011, a child burial site was excavated from a Unified Silla period building site in Seonggeon-dong, Gyeongju.','123 Dongdaero, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, Dongguk University WISE Campus Museum','10:00~16:00','Free','2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Closed every Saturday and Sunday / Public holidays',NULL),(830,1004,'en','Gyeongju Cultural Center','Gyeongju Cultural Center engages in various activities such as research and publication of local history, hosting cultural events and performances, and offering cultural lectures. It operates to promote local culture and preserve traditional culture in the Gyeongju area. The center features a local history exhibition hall showcasing the history and culture of Gyeongju during the Joseon Dynasty, as well as a bell tower, Donggyeonggwan, and educational facilities from the same period. Additionally, a beautiful ginkgo tree designated as a Gyeongsangbuk-do cultural property is located in the center\'s garden, attracting many tourists in the fall.','67-12 Jungang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Dongbu-dong)','09:00~18:00','Free','2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:25:05',NULL,NULL,'Closed on Sundays and public holidays',NULL),(831,850,'en','Hagokji','Hagokji is a reservoir located on Hoguk-ro in Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The average depth is shallow compared to the size of the reservoir. It is known as a great spot to visit in spring due to the double cherry blossom trees. Fishing is not allowed due to the high-voltage power lines passing nearby, posing an electrocution risk. Nearby attractions include Oksan Seowon, Gyeongju Dokrakdang, and the National Yeongcheon National Cemetery.','Duryu-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(832,125,'en','Bohum Golf Club','Bohum Golf Club is a public golf course established within the Gyeongju Bohum Tourist Complex. It was created to contribute to the popularization of golf and the improvement of public health and leisure activities in accordance with the laws regarding the installation and use of sports facilities. The course is designed to maintain the natural landscape, inspiring dynamic challenges for golfers. It is equipped with facilities such as a clubhouse, large restaurant, shade house, locker room, and pro shop.','182-14, Bohum-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(833,1044,'en','Gyeongju Country Club','Gyeongju Country Club is the best public golf course in Korea, leading the popularization of golf in the country. Located in the historical city of Gyeongju, within the Bomun Tourist Complex, it is surrounded by beautiful natural scenery and offers a panoramic view of Bomun Lake and the tourist complex. The fantastic light golf experience at night is a pride of Gyeongju Country Club, equipped with lighting facilities on all holes, allowing you to enjoy golf without hesitation at dawn and night.','182-98 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','From sunrise to sunset',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(834,149,'en','Kolon Garden Golf Course','Kolon Garden Golf Course is designed on natural grass with a view of Mount Toham, and it is open year-round for easy access. It features a 150-meter long driving range with 15 tee boxes. You can enjoy a round of golf in a beautiful forest setting without a caddy and with a manual cart for your health.','289-17 Bulguk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','※ Please refer to the website or contact by phone before visiting',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'※ Please refer to the website or contact by phone before visiting',NULL),(835,118,'en','Gyeongju World Snow Park','The Snow Park within Gyeongju World operates only during the winter season and features a sledding area. It first opened in late 1994 and has expanded its facilities each year, now including dedicated lifts for sledding. The extreme line, Vanheim, boasts an impressive length of 250m, the longest in the southern region. The adult sledding area, Adventure Line Yotunheim, allows for tube and plastic sledding, while the children\'s sledding area, Dream Line Alfheim, is a safe space for kids to enjoy sledding. Additionally, visitors can enjoy snowball fights in the snow-covered village of Plitvice.','544 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Cheongun-dong)','Refer to the website',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Refer to the website',NULL),(836,117,'en','Mauna Ocean Country Club','Located in the great nature of 500m above the East Sea and Dongdaesan, this golf course was designed by field consultant Kim Myung-gil, with construction by Douglas Nickels of Nickels Golf Group, landscape design by Jeong Young-seon of Seoan Landscape, and architecture by Jo Yong-sik of Doo Architecture. It has successfully hosted the \'Kolon-Hana Bank Championship\', a US LPGA Tour event, and the newly launched WEMIX Championship in 2023.','982 Dongnam-ro, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Check website and contact for inquiries',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','On the day of Seollal and Chuseok',NULL),(837,148,'en','Gyeongju Bomun Live Fire Shooting Range','Located in the Bomun Tourist Complex, the Gyeongju Bomun Live Fire Shooting Range offers an indoor shooting experience with imported handguns that are not easily accessible in South Korea. It features a separate shooting range and waiting room, along with a space displaying firearms, photos, and posters, as well as a photo zone where you can take pictures with toy guns. After thoroughly understanding the safety rules, you can relieve stress and experience excitement by hitting targets with real firearms.','424-11 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(838,119,'en','Gyeongju Youth Training Center','The Gyeongju Youth Training Center serves as a dedicated department for youth policy and a space for youth activities, operating since its opening in 1995 to promote healthy growth among youth. The center implements various youth policy projects, including enhancing youth participation and rights, crisis support for at-risk youth, and creating a beneficial environment for local youth.','131 Alcheonbuk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangseong-dong)','- Weekdays 09:00~22:00 - Weekends 09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(839,1195,'en','Mulbangah Samgyetang','Mulbangah Samgyetang is a specialty restaurant for Samgyetang located in Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, serving only Samgyetang. They purchase enough chickens to sell without using frozen chickens, adhering to the principle of selling only what they can use up each day. They also have group seating available, making it a good place for various gatherings.','339-1, Alcheonbuk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~20:30 (Last order 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Samgyetang','Available (30 cars)','Closed every Wednesday',NULL),(840,165,'en','Busan Restaurant','Located right in front of Bulguksa Temple, Busan Restaurant Gyeongju Bulguksa branch boasts a long history and tradition. It is known for providing a hearty and delicious meal to those visiting Bulguksa. The signature menu here is the brisket doenjang jjigae set meal. The doenjang jjigae, served in a hot pot, features a rich soybean paste base with plenty of brisket, boasting a deep and rich flavor. The savory brisket oil blends with the doenjang, creating an even richer umami flavor, and various vegetables such as tofu, pumpkin, and onion are generously included, making it a satisfying meal. The tteokgalbi, loved by people of all ages, has a juicy and tender texture. The seasoning is evenly absorbed, giving it a sweet and salty taste. It is popular among family guests visiting with children, and enjoying it with doenjang jjigae makes for an even more abundant meal. In addition, various Korean dishes such as stone pot bibimbap, sanchae bibimbap, and bulgogi hot pot are prepared, offering a wide selection. The side dishes are also served neatly and cleanly.','32-7 Bulguksin-taekji 7-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Jinhyeon-dong)','08:00~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Brisket Doenjang Jjigae Set Meal / Brisket Doenjang Jjigae Set Meal + Stone Pot Bibimbap / Pork Cutlet / Sanchae Bibimbap, etc.','Available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(841,158,'en','Jangdokdae','Jangdokdae is a Korean restaurant that exudes a rustic and warm atmosphere, filled with traditional jars at the entrance. It is designated as a safe restaurant by the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs and has been selected as an exemplary restaurant in Gyeongju. Jangdokdae is famous for its Cheonggukjang and Sundubu set meals. The Cheonggukjang is made in-house, resulting in a less pungent smell, making it enjoyable for everyone, with a rich and deep flavor. The Sundubu set meal features soft sundubu in a spicy broth. Additionally, the bulgogi hot pot is generous in meat and not sweet, while the bulgogi mushroom stew has a hearty and clean broth flavor. There is also a handmade pork cutlet menu for children.','6-11 Jeongja 3-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Madong)','08:30~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Cheonggukjang Set Meal / Sundubu Set Meal / Eel Set Meal / Bulgogi Hot Pot / Bulgogi Mushroom Stew / Handmade Pork Cutlet, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(842,1200,'en','Bohm Folk Restaurant','Bohm Folk Restaurant is a well-known restaurant in Gyeongju famous for its pork belly, established in 1996 and located near the Bomun Tourist Complex. Bohm Folk Restaurant offers a variety of menus including meals with stews, hot pots, fresh pork belly, and side dishes, among which the chewy fresh pork belly and the beef tripe hot pot made with Korean beef intestines are exceptional. In particular, the fresh pork belly is sourced only from Handong Pork Valley and is cut fresh upon ordering, ensuring reliability and freshness. Grilled directly on a hot iron lid, the fat is rendered away, enhancing the chewy texture. It is a recognized restaurant favored by both tourists and many long-time local customers.','435 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Sinpyeong-dong)','Mon-Sat 11:30-21:30, Sunday 11:00-21:00 ※ Break time 14:00-16:00 (No break time on weekends)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Fresh Pork Belly / Doenjang Stew / Seafood Soft Tofu Stew, etc.','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(843,231,'en','Suseokjeong','Suseokjeong is a traditional Korean restaurant located near the Gyeongju Museum. It is one of Gyeongju\'s representative traditional restaurants, starting with warm sungnyung (scorched rice water) served in earthenware, followed by abalone porridge, tteokgalbi (grilled short rib patties), and royal court japchae (stir-fried glass noodles), all made with care and skill. The interior of Suseokjeong is adorned with frames and folding screens that highlight the unique beauty of Korea.','41 Naeri-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Tteokgalbi Set / Owner\'s Course / Guest\'s Course / Royal Court Bibimbap, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(844,252,'en','Seokha Hanjeongshik','‘Seokha Hanjeongshik’ is a traditional Korean restaurant located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior of the establishment is a modern-style building that exudes a vintage atmosphere that harmonizes well with the menu. The interior features both traditional seating and table seating, allowing guests to choose their preferred seating arrangement. The menu includes lunch specials and various course menus. This place has a dedicated parking lot, allowing for a comfortable dining experience without parking worries.','51-14 Heungmu-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','12:00~21:30 (Preparation time 15:00~16:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Seokha special / Geobukjeongshik / Seokha Jeong Sam / Seokha Jeong I / Seokha Jeong Il / Special','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(845,177,'en','Ipungnyeo Guro Ssambap','Ipungnyeo Guro Ssambap, located near Daereungwon in Gyeongju, is known for serving a generous amount of side dishes that can break the table. The presentation resembles Jeolla-do\'s traditional Korean meal, which is the secret to its popularity. The menu consists solely of ssambap. A side of tteokgalbi is also prepared. Various regional specialties such as Jeolla-do\'s jeotgal and Gyeongsang-do\'s pickled vegetables and napa cabbage salad are served as side dishes. The variety of wrapping vegetables changes with the seasons as they use seasonal vegetables.','155 Cheomseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','09:00~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Ssambap / Tteokgalbi / Sundubu jjigae (seasonal menu)','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(846,1198,'en','Local Restaurant','Local Restaurant has been a staple for over 30 years near the Bomun Tourist Complex in Gyeongju. This place only uses fresh, large Jeju hairtail caught by fishing. The seasoning for the braised dish is made from homemade gochujang and doenjang, not store-bought sauces. They take pride in their ingredients, preparing hairtail and boiling broth daily. The braised hairtail and grilled hairtail made from special large hairtail over 5 pieces are thick and retain their silver sheen. In addition to the basic side dishes, appetizers such as grilled short ribs, thin noodles, acorn jelly, and buckwheat pancakes are provided immediately upon ordering, and seasonal side dishes change daily. Additionally, seaweed soup for children is served as a complimentary dish. Cooking starts as soon as the order is placed, taking about 10-15 minutes for the food to be served. There is also a room that can accommodate up to 105 people.','21 Bukgun-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','09:30~21:00 (Last order 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Hairtail stew / Stone pot set meal / Whole grilled Jeju hairtail set / Abalone set meal, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(847,1196,'en','Old Gyeongju Charcoal','‘Old Gyeongju Charcoal’ is a restaurant located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The signature menu here is various cuts of domestic Korean beef barbecue, and there are also various meal options available for selection according to preference. The basic side dishes include a variety of accompaniments such as leafy vegetables, salad, liver and intestines, mung bean jelly, and kimchi. The restaurant has both traditional seating and table seating, and orders can be placed comfortably through kiosks installed at each table.','447 Cheonggang-ro, Cheonbuk-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00 ~ 21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Beef rib meat barbecue / Marinated beef rib meat barbecue / Chuck eye roll / Flank steak / Beef tartare / Cold noodles / Soybean paste noodles, etc.','Available (20 cars) Fee (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(848,251,'en','Yusujeong','One of the representative dishes of Gyeongju is ssambap (rice wrapped in leaves). Yusujeong, located near Bulguksa Temple, is a restaurant where you can truly experience the taste of ssambap. There is a gas station behind the old Kolon Hotel intersection, and Yusujeong is modestly located behind it. The entrance looks simple and comfortable, as it has been converted from a regular house. Upon entering, rooms are arranged in a ㄷ shape around a courtyard. The courtyard is utilized as a relaxing space with simple tables for enjoying tea after meals. The side dishes that come with the ssambap include over 20 varieties such as fish, meat, doenjang jjigae (soybean paste stew), and garlic salad. The ssam (wrap) comes with fresh and boiled vegetables separately. Due to the fact that it is mainly visited by tourists from other regions, the food has been adjusted to have a milder and cleaner taste, which has been praised by those who have enjoyed it.','24-7 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Madong)','- Weekdays 10:00~16:00 - Weekends 10:00~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Grilled bulgogi ssambap / Nutritional stone pot rice / Seafood pancake / Acorn jelly, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(849,1199,'en','Traditional Millstone Soft Tofu','Using 100% domestic soybeans, traditional methods are employed to make hand-made tofu and soft tofu in a cauldron. Therefore, no preservatives or colorings are used at all. Moreover, the vegetables served with the bossam are grown directly in the restaurant\'s backyard garden and greenhouse. The main dishes are soft tofu stew and tofu hot pot. The soybean residue left after making tofu can be taken home for free.','111 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','08:00 ~ 21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Millstone soft tofu stew / Soft tofu stew / Tofu hot pot / Whole tofu (hand-made) / Green onion pancake, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(853,11,'en','Gyeongju Naemulwangneung','Naemulwangneung, located near Gyeongju Hyanggyo in the Inwang-dong tomb complex, is the tomb of King Naemul, the 17th king of Silla (reigned 356–402), established in 401. It is a mound tomb with a base diameter of 22m and a height of 5.3m, with a natural stone corner exposed around the base, suggesting that a separate stone circle was installed inside, similar to the Muyeolwangneung. There are no records regarding the burial site of Naemulwang, but it is recorded to be located southwest of Cheomseongdae, which matches the current location. It was designated as a historic site on August 27, 1969. Naemul was the second king to ascend the throne from the Kim clan, leading to a monopoly of the throne by the Kim family. He was the first to use the title \'Maripgan\' for kings and imported advanced culture through diplomatic relations with the Chinese state of Jin. When the allied forces of Baekje and Wa invaded, he requested assistance from King Gwanggaeto of Goguryeo to avert the crisis, marking a period of significant national development.','1065 Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(854,87,'en','Gyeongju Gyeongdeokwang Tomb','This site is said to be the tomb of King Gyeongdeok, the 35th king of Silla (reigned 742–765), located on a hill far southwest of the Gyeongju city center. He ascended to the throne during a time when the royal authority of the Silla dynasty began to decline and reformed administrative divisions and official positions. The mound is round in shape and is surrounded by a protective stone circle. The stone circle is shaped like the stone base of a wooden building, with a base stone laid down and facing stones surrounding it. Between the facing stones, supporting stones are placed to create an entrance. The provision of an entrance is seen as an expression of the desire for an open space. A high stone statue with an engraved pattern is placed in front of the tomb. However, stone sculptures such as stone lions, civil official statues, and military official statues, which can be seen in royal tombs from the Unified Silla period, are not present. It is uncertain whether the tomb mentioned in historical records is this one, and some opinions suggest that the techniques used to shape the stone circle and the carving of the twelve zodiac figures belong to the later period of Silla, leading to the view that this tomb may not belong to King Gyeongdeok.','San 8, Bujiri, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(855,884,'en','Chunguidang','Chunguidang is the residence of General Choi Jin-rip (1568–1636), a military official from the mid-Joseon period. When the Imjin War broke out, General Choi led a militia and helped General Kwon Yul during the Jeongyu War. Initially named Heumheumdang, the building was renamed Chunguidang after renovations around 1760. The structure features four rooms in the front and two on the side, with a single-eave, hip-and-gable roof. At the back, there are a main room and a guest room, and to the right, there is a ritual space, showcasing the typical layout of upper-class residences during the Joseon Dynasty. Chunguidang, where he lived, can be seen as the beginning of the Gyeongju Choi family, and part of it is currently operated as a Hanok stay with traditional guest rooms and a tea room. During your stay, you can explore the Chunguidang lounge, the statue of General Choi Jin-rip in Chungui Park, the Chunguidang Museum, and the shrine, as well as the grassy courtyard.','28-17 Ijo 3-gil, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available (approximately 40 small cars)',NULL,NULL),(856,888,'en','Yongsan Seowon (Gyeongju)','Yongsan Seowon was established in 1699, the 25th year of King Sukjong, to hold rituals for the military scholar Jeongmugong Choi Jin-rip. In the 37th year of King Sukjong (1711), it received the plaque \'Sungnyeolsau\' from the king and was later upgraded to a seowon. It was demolished due to the Seowon Abolition Order in the 7th year of King Gojong (1870) but was rebuilt in 1924. A stele pavilion is located slightly southwest of Yongsan Seowon. Choi Jin-rip was born in the present-day Hyeongok-myeon of Gyeongju. During the Imjin War, he raised a militia with his brother Choi Gye-jong, and during the Jeongyu War, he achieved merit in the Battle of Seongpo in Ulsan with Kwon Yul. He died heroically in the Battle of Heomcheon in Yongin during the Byeongja Horan and was posthumously honored as a Minister of Military Affairs and recorded as a model of integrity.','110-34 Poseok-ro, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available (Free)','Closed every Sunday, January 1, and on the days of Lunar New Year and Chuseok.',NULL),(857,31,'en','Gyeongju Jimawangneung','This is the tomb of Jimawang, the 6th king of Silla (reigned 112–134). Jimawang was born as the son of the 5th king, Pasawang, and during his 23-year reign, he repelled invasions from Gaya, Wae, and Malgal. During Jimawang\'s reign, Silla maintained a friendly relationship with Baekje but competed for supremacy with Gaya over the lower Nakdong River. The Wae invaded the eastern border, but after negotiations, a peace treaty was established, and when Malgal invaded from the north, they were repelled with the help of Baekje. The tomb is located 200m south of Poseokjeong, on the western slope of Namsan. It is relatively small among royal tombs, and based on its shape and location, the internal structure is likely a stone chamber tomb.','30 Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(858,30,'en','Gyeongju Seoakdong Tomb Complex','This refers to four large tombs located on a hill behind the Muyeolwangneung in Seoakdong, Gyeongju. All the tombs are circular in shape and have no special structures around them. Some of the surrounding protective stones are exposed, all made of broken stones. They differ from the tombs in the Daereungwon area, which mostly use river stones. The internal structure is presumed to be a stone chamber tomb. There are many smaller tombs distributed around these tombs, all of which are stone chamber tombs. The terrain where these tombs are located is on a ridge extending southwest from Seondosan, and considering the surrounding hills and valleys, it can be inferred that they were created under the influence of geomancy. The first tomb is presumed to be Beopheungwangneung, the second tomb to be Jinhwangneung, the third tomb to be Jinjwangneung, and the fourth tomb to be Munheungdaewangneung. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','750 Seoakdong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(859,60,'en','Gyeongju Beopheungwangneung','This is the tomb of Beopheungwang, the 23rd king of Silla (reigned 514–540). Beopheungwang was the king who completed Silla as a centralized ancient state. To strengthen royal authority, he established the Sangdaedeung and Byeongbu, and promulgated the law code in 520. In 532, he merged with Geumgwan Gaya and first advanced into the Nakdong River basin. He was the first in Silla to use the independent era name \'Gyeongwon\' and sent envoys to the Liang Dynasty in China. In 527, with the martyrdom of Lee Chadon, he adopted Buddhism as the state religion, laying the ideological foundation of the ancient state. The tomb is relatively small for a Silla king\'s tomb, measuring 2m in height and 14m in diameter. Below the tomb, there are natural stones that supported the surrounding stones. Tombs of kings before Beopheungwang are densely located in the flatlands of Gyeongju, making them difficult to identify, while tombs of kings after him are located separately in hills or outskirts, with records of their locations remaining. This change seems to be related to the transformation of royal tombs, and the beginning of this change can be found at Beopheungwangneung, making it an important site.','San 63 Hyohyeon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(860,863,'en','Gyeongju Queen Jindeok Tomb','This tomb is known to be the resting place of Queen Jindeok, the 28th ruler of Silla. Queen Jindeok\'s birth name is Seungman, and she is a cousin of Queen Seondeok. She is the second queen of Silla and the last king of the royal lineage. With the help of Kim Chun-chu and Kim Yu-shin, Queen Jindeok ascended to the throne and reorganized the bureaucratic and military structures during her reign, actively adopting the systems and culture of the Tang Dynasty. She also achieved many victories in frequent wars against Baekje by promoting Kim Yu-shin. It is said that when Queen Jindeok died, she was buried in Sarangbu. The tomb is located alone on the southern ridge of Antaebong. The perimeter is surrounded by stone slabs and support stones, and the support stones are carved with zodiac figures wearing armor and holding weapons. Compared to other royal tombs, the zodiac figures are smaller and the carvings are shallow, indicating that they are from a later period among Silla royal tombs.','San 48, Oru-ri, Hyeongok-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(861,13,'en','Gyeongju Hyo Gong Wangneung','The tomb of King Hyo Gong, the 52nd king of Silla (reigned 897–912), is a circular mound tomb with a height of 5m and a diameter of 21.2m, built by piling up earth. A few stones remain at the bottom of the tomb, which were likely used for protection, suggesting that they are part of the surrounding stones similar to Muyeolwangneung. Otherwise, it is a very simple tomb with no markers. According to records, when the king died in 912, he was named Hyo Gong and was buried north of the temple Sajasasa. There are discrepancies in the records regarding the burial site, but the current location corresponds to the northern point of the site believed to be Sajasasa, so it is not significantly off. Currently, there is a temple site to the south of this tomb, which is presumed to be the site of Sajasasa.','San 14 Baeban-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(862,92,'en','Gyeongju Heungdeokwangneung','This is the tomb of Heungdeokwang, the 42nd king of Silla (reigned 826–836), with a diameter of 20.8m and a height of 6m, making it one of the largest and most formally constructed royal tombs in Silla history. According to the Samguk Sagi and Samguk Yusa, it is said to be a joint tomb with the queen, which is why the size of the mound is relatively large. Under the mound, stone slabs were erected to form a surrounding stone, and between the slabs, wooden pillars were set to secure the slabs, with a capstone placed on top. Statues of the twelve zodiac signs were carved on the pillars according to their respective directions. Radiating stone was laid around the surrounding stone, and a railing was built around it. The railing posts had two round holes drilled at the top and bottom for inserting a stone, but none remain today. At each corner of the mound, a stone lion was placed, and in front of it, a pair of civil and military officials were arranged on either side. Additionally, to the left in front of the tomb, there was a damaged stele that marked the tomb, and the stele and waterway have been lost. The style of this monument indicates that the surrounding stone and the zodiac statues follow the format of the royal tomb of King Wonseong, while the placement of the stone lions follows the format of the royal tomb of King Seongdeok, and the arrangement of civil and military officials is similar to that of either King Seongdeok or King Wonseong\'s tombs. It is said that in the first year of his reign, Queen Janghwa passed away, and Heungdeokwang, who thought only of her for 11 years, eventually passed away. It is said that he willed to be buried with Queen Janghwa, and thus was interred in Heungdeokwangneung.','190-26 Yuktong-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(863,887,'en','Donggang Seowon','Established in 1695 (21st year of King Sukjong) to honor the Confucian scholar Son Jung-don from the mid-Joseon period and to commemorate his high academic virtue. It is located at the foot of Jeosan Mountain, which spans Pohang City and Gyeongju City. The site includes a main hall, lecture hall, east and west dormitories, a stele pavilion, and an administrative building, and was designated as a Gyeongsangbuk-do cultural property on January 20, 1996. Son Jung-don\'s courtesy name was Daebal, and his posthumous name was Gyeongjeol. He was the son of Son So, who quelled the Imsin Rebellion, and studied under Kim Jong-jik. He passed the state examination in 1482 (13th year of King Seongjong) and subsequently held key positions such as Dosungji three times, Daesagan four times, and governor of Gyeongsang, Chungcheong, Jeolla, Pyeongan, and Hamgyeong provinces, eventually being appointed as the Minister of Personnel and Vice Prime Minister, and was selected as a model of integrity.','40-25 Yugumgangjeong-gil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(864,864,'en','Gyeongju Yuyeonjeong Pavilion','Yuyeonjeong Pavilion, located next to Ungok Seowon, was built in 1811 during the 11th year of King Sunjo of Joseon by the Andong Kwon clan to commemorate Kwon Haeng, a high official of Goryeo, and his descendants, Kwon San-hae and Kwon Deok-rin. This pavilion is situated about 50 meters east of the seowon on a valley called Yongchudae, harmonizing beautifully with the surrounding natural scenery. The building has a size of three bays in the front and two bays on the side, featuring a hip-and-gable roof. The ceiling of the main hall is decorated with a well-shaped design to hide the rafters, with semi-circular wooden panels inserted at a 45-degree angle on both sides, creating a very unique appearance. It harmonizes with the surrounding natural scenery, including Yongchu Valley and ginkgo trees, and showcases the architectural techniques of the early 1800s well.','79-19 Saragil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(865,26,'en','Gyeongju Heondeokwangneung','This is the tomb of Heondeokwang, the 41st king of Silla (reigned 809–826), located in Bukcheon, Gyeongju. Heondeokwang\'s real name was Kim Eon-seung, and he became king after killing his nephew, Aejangwang. During his reign, he encouraged agriculture and maintained a close relationship with the Tang Dynasty, but domestic affairs were chaotic due to the rebellions of Kim Heon-chang and Kim Beom-mun. According to the \'Samguk Sagi\', when the king died in 826, he was buried north of Cheonrimsa. The exact location of Cheonrimsa is unknown, but there is a temple site south of this tomb, which is considered to be the site of Cheonrimsa. The tomb is a round mound with a diameter of 26m and a height of 6m. Surrounding the base of the mound, protective stones were placed. The outer stones were arranged in a way that the first layer served as pillars, and flat stones (myeonseok) were placed on top. Between the myeonseok, stones serving as pillars (taengseok) were inserted and fixed. The taengseok were carved with the twelve zodiac signs as a symbolic meaning to protect the tomb, but currently, only five zodiac signs remain: pig (hae), rat (ja), ox (chuk), tiger (in), and rabbit (myo). Outside the protective stones, stone pillars were erected to install a railing, and stones were laid on the ground between the protective stones and the railing. The current appearance was restored in the 1970s, with some of the protective stones and stone railings newly constructed. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','80 Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(866,23,'en','Gyeongju Sinmu Wangneung','This is the tomb of Sinmu Wang, the 45th king of Silla (reigned 839). His birth name was Kim Woo-jing, and he was a cousin of King Heogang. After the death of King Heongdeok, he helped his father in the struggle for the throne but fled to Cheonghaejin after being defeated, later borrowing troops from Jangbogo to oust King Min-ae and ascend to the throne. However, he passed away just three months after taking the throne due to illness. It is said that he was buried in the northwest direction. This tomb is located in Dongbang-dong, southeast of the royal capital, and the name of the hill southeast of the tomb is Hyeongjesan. It is a round mound, 3.4 meters high and 15 meters in diameter, made of piled earth, with no facilities around it.','660 Dongbang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(867,33,'en','Gyeongju Seongdeokwangneung','This is the tomb of Seongdeokwang, the 33rd king of Silla (reigned 701–737), located in a pine forest on the southeastern hill along the road to Bulguksa in Gyeongju. Seongdeokwang was the son of Sinmunwang and his real name was Yung-gi. He actively engaged in exchanges with the Tang Dynasty and led the most stable period of Silla\'s prosperity politically. According to the \'Samguk Sagi\', when the king died in 737, he was buried south of Igeosa, and there is currently a temple site presumed to be Igeosa north of the royal tomb. The base circumference of the tomb is 46m, and its height is 5m. At the bottom of the tomb, protective stones were placed to safeguard it, with stones (myeonseok) about 90cm high surrounding it, and a cover stone (gapseok) placed on top. Between the myeonseok, stones serving as pillars (taengseok) were inserted and fixed, and triangular stones were erected on the outside for support. Zodiac figures were placed between the triangular support stones, but the sculpture of a figure in armor holding weapons on a square stone is severely damaged. In front of the tomb, there are stone statues, and at the four corners of the tomb, stone lions were placed. It appears that there were pairs of civil and military stone figures on either side of the stone statues, but now only one military stone figure and one half of a stone figure remain. The realistic carving techniques of the stone artifacts seen at Seongdeokwangneung belong to the early style of Unified Silla, and the royal tomb is well-preserved as a royal tomb from the Unified Silla period. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','8 Joyang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(868,25,'en','Gyeongju Hyoso Wangneung','This tomb is that of Hyoso Wang, the 32nd king of Silla (reigned 692-702). He ascended to the throne at the young age of 6 as the eldest son of King Sinmun (reigned 681-692), and his mother, Queen Sinmok, served as regent for 8 years. During Hyoso Wang\'s reign, he reorganized the government system and established a medical education institution. He built many fortresses to reclaim the old lands of Goguryeo and opened markets to facilitate the distribution of goods in the royal capital. After Hyoso Wang\'s death, it is said that he was buried east of Mangdeoksa. This tomb is located on the southwestern slope of Hyeongjebong, southeast of the city. About 100 meters to the east is the tomb of his younger brother, King Seongdeok. The tomb is a round mound, 4.3 meters high and 10.3 meters in diameter, made of piled earth. The base is surrounded by natural stones, but only a few remain today. There are no decorations on the tomb, only a spirit stone that marks the place where the spirit resides. It has been confirmed that the internal structure is a stone chamber tomb.','San 8, Joyang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(869,851,'en','Gwanseong Solbat Beach','Gwanseong Solbat Beach is located at the southernmost point among the five beaches in Gyeongju. With breakwaters on both sides, the waves are not high, and the clear blue waters are popular. The pine forest and the long stretch of white sand create a beautiful landscape. It is a quiet beach with excellent natural scenery and well-equipped facilities, allowing for a pleasant water play experience without large crowds. Nearby, in Sindae-ri, Yangnam-myeon, there is a Kolon Golf Course, making it a great place to enjoy marine leisure and leisure activities, and it is also famous as a driving course along the coastal road towards Ulsan. Nearby attractions include Haseo Coastal Park.','Sullyeom-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(870,254,'en','Seokgeodon','Seokgeodon, located in Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, is a specialty octopus restaurant. The name Seokgeodon combines the Chinese characters for \'seokge\' (octopus) and \'don\' (pork), referring to a dish that mixes octopus and pork. It is a delicacy when mixed with the steamed egg that is served as a side dish. The restaurant has a fast table turnover and is popular among locals.','2838 Sanup-ro, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~16:00 (Last order 15:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Seokgeodon / Stir-fried octopus','Available','Every Monday and Friday',NULL),(871,178,'en','Gyeongju Seafood Restaurant Mediterranean','Located in Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongju Seafood Restaurant Mediterranean is a place where you can enjoy various seafood. The menu includes a sashimi platter served with a plate per person, giving a feeling of being treated, as well as the Mediterranean special course consisting of various seafood such as sashimi, assorted grilled fish, grilled lobster, or snow crab legs. Additionally, you can taste fresh flatfish, rockfish, and wild fish as sashimi, and there are also menus like mulhoe (cold raw fish soup) and sashimi rice.','325 Alcheonbuk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Dongcheon-dong)','- 11:40~22:00- Preparation time 15:00~17:00- Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:12','Sashimi platter / Sashimi rice / Mulhoe / Rockfish sashimi / Flatfish / Rockfish etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(872,157,'en','Goduban','Goduban offers a comfortable dining experience using beautiful ceramics from the couple-run Langsan Pottery. The yard is surrounded by flowers and trees, and the entire building is encircled by a vegetable garden and garden. A traditional cauldron is hung in one corner of the yard, where they make kelp tofu in the traditional way and cook with salt baked in a wood-fired kiln using pine wood. There is also a pottery exhibition room where you can admire and purchase beautiful ceramics from Langsan Pottery before or after your meal.','11 Daegisil 3-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Doji-dong)','[Weekdays] - 12:00~15:00 - Last order at 14:00 [Weekends] - 12:00~20:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order at 19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:12','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Godusan Surasang / Igeobansang / Goduban Bapsang / Langsan Bapsang / Tofu Samhap, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(873,104,'en','Gugang Seowon','Gugang Seowon is a Confucian academy established to commemorate the scholarship and virtue of Ikjae Lee Je-hyeon, housing his portrait and tablet. Lee Je-hyeon was a scholar and politician during the late Goryeo period. As a scholar, he played a crucial role in accepting and developing Confucianism. He also excelled in literature, leaving behind many poems and advancing Goryeo\'s classical literature. He made significant contributions to historiography as well. His existing works include \'Ikjae Nango\' in 10 volumes and \'Yeokong Paesul\' in 2 volumes. Gugang Seowon was originally established as a shrine for Lee Je-hyeon during the reign of King Gongmin of Goryeo (1351-1374) and was rebuilt as a seowon in the 12th year of King Sukjong (1686). However, it was closed due to the Seowon Abolition Order in the 8th year of King Gojong (1871) and was restored by local Confucian scholars in 1904. The layout of the seowon is divided into a田-shaped space surrounded by earthen walls. On the left, the outer gate, lecture hall, inner gate, and shrine are arranged in a straight line, while the right side has a historical site and bell tower. Inside the bell tower, the portrait of Ikjae and the wooden blocks of Ikjae\'s writings are preserved. It has been responsible for rituals for the sage and local education, holding ceremonies every February and August by the lunar calendar. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','68-6 Gugang-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(874,7,'en','Guisan Seowon','Guisan Seowon was established in 1786 (the 10th year of Jeongjo) by local Confucian scholars to commemorate the scholarship and virtue of Seo Yu (徐愈). It was originally founded as Guisan Seosa (龜山書社) to enshrine his spirit tablet. In 1839 (the 5th year of Heonjong), it was designated as \'Gusan\' and elevated to a seowon. In 1848, Seo Il-won (徐一元) was additionally enshrined. While it played a role in honoring the sages and local education, it was demolished in 1868 (the 5th year of Gojong) due to the seowon abolition decree by Heungseon Daewongun. It was restored by local Confucian scholars in 1983 and remains to this day. Annual rites are held in February and August.','71-12 Guisan Seowon-gil, Hyeongok-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all the time',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(875,6,'en','Nasan Seowon','Nasan Seowon, located in the large village of Nasan-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, is a place dedicated to the Confucian scholar Baekchon Kim Mun-gi from the early Joseon period, also known as Nasan-sa. This seowon, where the descendants of Kim Mun-gi and the founder of Nasan-ri, Kim Je-hak, hold annual rites, is situated at the southernmost part of Gyeongju and is the only seowon established in the coastal area. Walking from the village hall at the entrance of Nasan-ri to the seowon, one can feel the atmosphere of the Andong Jang clan\'s noble village. Nasan Seowon follows the typical architectural style of Joseon-era seowons, with a site area of 800 pyeong, including one main hall with three rooms, one lecture hall with four rooms, one east dormitory with three rooms, one library with three rooms, one shrine with three rooms, one outer gate, two inner gates, and an office. It was established in 1780 (the 4th year of Jeongjo) but was demolished during the seowon abolition decree in 1868 (the 5th year of Gojong) and was rebuilt in 1936. An annual rite is held on the middle day of March. Kim Mun-gi was born in 1399 (the 1st year of Jeongjong) and his clan is Kimnyeong, with the courtesy name Yeogong. He passed the state examination in 1426 (the 8th year of Sejong) and served as a censor in the Royal Secretariat, a chief secretary, and a minister of the Ministry of Public Works. In 1456 (the 2nd year of Sejo), he was involved in the restoration of King Danjong, led by Seong Sam-mun and Park Paeng-nyeon, and was executed after being discovered. In 1778 (the 2nd year of Jeongjo), he was posthumously promoted to Left Prime Minister and in 1791, he was enshrined at the loyalist shrine of Jangneung, the tomb of King Danjong.','27 Nasan 1-gil, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(876,51,'en','Danggu Seowon','Danggu Seowon is a Confucian academy dedicated to the teachings of Munhui-gong Lee Se-gi, as well as Munhyo-gong Lee Cheon and Songwa-gong Lee Jong-yun. Originally, the Moyeon Seodang, which honored Songwa-gong, was built in the 13th year of Cheoljong (1862), but it was demolished in the 5th year of Gojong (1868), and Danggu Seowon was established in 1983. Lee Se-gi was a renowned scholar during the reign of King Chungnyeol of Goryeo, serving in various high positions. Lee Cheon, the eldest son of Lee Se-gi, excelled in the national examination in the 25th year of King Chungnyeol (1299) and held several important positions. Lee Jong-yun, the 6th descendant of Lee Se-gi, was born in 1431 in Gyeongju and became a government official, promoting education and virtuous governance.','8-3 Danggu Seowon-gil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(877,12,'en','Ungok Seowon','Ungok Seowon, located in Cheongsu-gol, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, is a Confucian academy established to commemorate Gwon Haeng, a founding ancestor of the Andong Gwon clan, and Gwon Sanhae and Gwon Deokrin, who were officials during the Joseon Dynasty. Seowon refers to private local educational institutions established during the Goryeo and Joseon periods to enshrine the tablets of excellent Confucian scholars and conduct rituals for them, as well as to educate and reform local residents. It was demolished due to the Seowon Abolition Order in 1868 but was later restored with a shrine and ritual hall built on the site, and in 1976, it was restored to what is believed to be the site of the Silla Milgoksa. It consists of the tomb hall, Gyeongdeoksa, the lecture hall, Jeonguidang, the east and west study rooms, and the outer three gates, with rituals held annually on the 3rd day of the lunar calendar. About 50m east of Ungok Seowon, on the valley of Yongchudae, there is a pavilion called Yuyeonjeong, built by the Andong Gwon clan to commemorate their ancestors, harmonizing beautifully with the surrounding natural scenery. The ginkgo tree, over 380 years old, is designated as a protected tree in Gyeongsangbuk-do, and its straight and splendid shape attracts many tourists during the autumn foliage season.','79-13 Saragil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (approximately 80 small cars)','Open year-round',NULL),(878,58,'en','Jangsan Seowon','Jangsan Seowon in Gyeongju was established in 1780 (4th year of King Jeongjo) by local Confucian scholars to commemorate the scholarship and virtue of the previous scholar. The previous scholar was a son of the Confucian scholar Hwaejae Lee Eonjeok from the mid-Joseon period. He was extremely filial and accompanied his father when he was exiled due to the Jeongmi Incident, serving him diligently and working hard to spread his father\'s scholarship and deeds. Jangsan Seowon played a role in honoring the sages and local education but was demolished in 1868 (5th year of King Gojong) due to the abolition of seowon by Daewongun. It was restored in November 2006 by descendants in Oksan-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju. The restoration ceremony was held on April 11, 2008. The buildings within the grounds include Seonggye-myo, Jisupdang, and Simgojae. The seowon also houses a collection of literary works.','377-2 Oksanseowon-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(879,57,'en','Jikcheon Seowon','Jikcheon Seowon in Gyeongju is a Confucian academy dedicated to the scholar Suam Jeong Sajin (1567–1616) from the late Joseon Dynasty. Jeong Sajin was born in Yeongcheon, Gyeongsangbuk-do, and his pen name was Gunseop. He studied under the renowned scholar Jang Hyeon-gwang and actively participated in the righteous army during the Imjin War. In 1606 (39th year of King Seonjo), he was recommended as a tutor for a prince and received appointments in 1611 (3rd year of King Gwanghae) for Seoma and Sijik, but he declined them all to focus solely on his studies. Jikcheon Seowon was established in 1711 (37th year of King Sukjong) in Jikcheon, Yeongcheon, but was demolished in 1868 (5th year of King Gojong) due to the abolition of seowon by Daewongun. In 1979, descendants rebuilt it in Daedong-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju. The buildings within the grounds include the shrine Sunghaksa, the lecture hall Yangjeongdang, Boinje, and Sujaemun. The lecture hall Yangjeongdang consists of a wooden floor and side rooms, and it is used for events of the clan and gatherings of local Confucian scholars.','176-9 Daedong-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(880,102,'en','Gyeongju Mauna Ocean Resort','Gyeongju Mauna Ocean Resort is a place that offers accommodation, dining, and recreational cultural facilities. Located on the Dongdaesan plateau, it is a family-oriented resort overlooking the East Sea, equipped with various facilities including a golf course and blue water. The accommodations are in villa and cottage styles. In particular, the water park and kids\' zone are very popular among family travelers with children. Moreover, it is within a 40-minute drive to most famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, making it a place where one can comfortably enjoy both relaxation and sightseeing.','1021 Dongnam-ro, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','15:00~11:00 next day',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(881,156,'en','Banywolsung Wood-fired Pizza','Banywolsung Wood-fired Pizza is a place where you can enjoy freshly baked pizza from a wood-fired oven. The dough is made and aged in the traditional Italian way and baked at 400 degrees in an oak wood-fired oven, resulting in a light and chewy taste. In addition to pizza, a variety of menus such as pasta, risotto, and fried rice are available. The spacious indoor area and wide table spacing allow for comfortable dining, and the interior boasts a sophisticated yet antique atmosphere.','316 Alcheon-nam-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Guhwang-dong)','- 11:30~21:00 - 15:00~16:30 - Last lunch order at 14:30 - Last dinner order at 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Banywolsung Bulgogi / Carbonara / Seafood Spicy Fried Rice / Margherita / Gorgonzola, etc.','Available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(882,159,'en','Hayeonji','Located near the Gyeongju Oryeong, Hayeonji is a restaurant that uses lotus leaves to create various dishes. It is famous for its lotus leaf rice, and offers a vegetarian-based menu for a healthy meal. They also make tofu in-house and use local agricultural products to prepare side dishes for the guests. The sticky rice and nuts lotus leaf rice is savory, and the more than ten side dishes are light.','932-4 Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Tap-dong)','Contact for inquiries',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Wonhyo Sang (Lotus Leaf Rice) / Seondeok Sang (Rice) / Children\'s Tteokgalbi / Lotus Leaf Tofu Jeon / Seafood Pancake, etc.','Available','Contact for inquiries',NULL),(883,1321,'en','Yeondong Fishing Village Experience Village','Yeondong Fishing Village Experience Village is a fishing village located in Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, close to Pohang, Ulsan, and Daegu. The front of the village faces the sea, while the back is bordered by high mountains, providing a cool environment in summer and warmth in winter. It is easily accessible via National Route 3, which connects the city of Gyeongju to the coast, and National Route 31 along the coastline, attracting tourists with its rich and fresh seafood. The village offers snorkeling experiences and accommodations in the fishing village. The snorkeling experience runs for two months in July and August, allowing participants to harvest abalone directly. Accommodations are available at Stay Yeondong, a village pension that can be used year-round, with a beautiful sea right in front of the pension. The waves are gentle, and the water depth is shallow, making it suitable for water activities. The name of the village is said to have originated from three families with different surnames who moved here during the late Goryeo period, forming the village, and it was called Yeondong because of the many lotus flowers in the pond. There is also a story that it was called Yeondong due to the salt pans in the area until just before the liberation at the end of the Joseon Dynasty.','38-1 Yeondong-gil, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~17:00※ Please inquire by phone before visiting',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round※ Please inquire by phone before visiting',NULL),(884,106,'en','Gangdong Water Park','Gangdong Water Park features thrilling outdoor attractions such as the country\'s highest 2.6m Storm Wave (wave pool), family slide, tornado slide, cannonball, and drop slide, as well as indoor attractions like body slides, baby pools, lazy rivers, kids\' pools, and wave pools, making it a water play facility where families and various age groups can enjoy themselves. An all-in package that includes admission, life jackets, meals, and attraction tickets is also available for more convenient use.','391 Bobul-ro, Cheongun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (approximately 2,000 vehicles)','Closed outside of summer season',NULL),(885,112,'en','Korea Popular Music Museum','The Korea Popular Music Museum is located in Gyeongju, a city of history and culture, and consists of four floors from the basement to the third floor. The first floor features a music appreciation room where you can listen to songs flowing from the legendary speaker, Mirophonic. The second-floor exhibition hall showcases the 100-year history of Korean popular music, displaying records from the first song recorded in Korea in 1896 to K-pop albums from the 2000s in chronological order, and offers a listening experience. The third-floor exhibition hall features a 100-year history of audio, displaying rare speakers such as the first speaker made in 1926, the legendary Mirophonic from Western Electric made in 1936, and speakers used by Hitler during World War II. The basement includes an instrument experience room, a children\'s experience room, a coin karaoke room, and a photo zone, providing opportunities for fun and experience.','9 Expo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~18:00 (Last admission 17:00)','[Individual] - Adult 15,000 won - Youth 10,000 won - Child 8,000 won [Group (20 or more)] - Adult 12,000 won - Youth 10,000 won - Child 8,000 won ※ For details, please refer to the website','2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (100 vehicles)','Every Monday, Tuesday (However, if Monday and Tuesday are legal holidays, it will be open as usual)',NULL),(886,83,'en','Gyeongju Jeonghyesaji 13-Story Stone Pagoda','The 13-story stone pagoda located at the site of Jeonghyesa in Gyeongju is a unique type of stone Buddhist pagoda from the Unified Silla period. It is built on a single-tier base made of earth, with a 13-story pagoda body on top, which is a unique appearance not found in similar examples from the Unified Silla period. The first-story pagoda body is massive, while from the second story onwards, both the body and roof stones decrease sharply in size, making the upper stories appear as if they are decorative elements added on top of the first-story pagoda. The large first-story body has square stone pillars at each corner, with auxiliary pillars attached inside to create an entrance. This provision of an entrance is seen as an expression of the desire for an open space. The roof stone is made of a separate stone rather than being carved, and the eaves, which originally formed straight lines, are raised at the four corners. At the top, only the base stone for the decorative element remains. This pagoda, believed to have been built in the 9th century during the Unified Silla period, is evaluated as a valuable resource for the study of stone pagodas of that time due to its rare 13 stories and its deviation from typical styles.','1655 Oksan-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(887,39,'en','Seokjangdong Petroglyphs, Gyeongju','The Seokjangdong Petroglyphs are located on the rock face north of Geumjangdae, where the Seocheon and Bukcheon rivers meet, crossing the Gyeongju plain. This prehistoric artwork is believed to have been created around 15m above the river on a vertical cliff, covering an area of approximately 2m wide and 9m long, and is expressed in abstract and geometric forms. A total of 27 figures have been identified, including 8 geometric patterns, 11 images featuring elements of swords and spears, 4 footprints, 3 female figures, 1 boat, and other animal shapes and difficult-to-interpret images. While they vary slightly in form, they can be categorized into shield shapes, acorn shapes, and flower shapes, with the acorn and flower shapes being unique characteristics not found in petroglyphs from other regions. In particular, the images of female figures combined with swords are believed to have been heavily influenced by the Chilpori style. Discovered in March 1994 by a research team from Dongguk University\'s Department of Archaeology and Art History, the petroglyphs are thought to have been created using techniques such as pecking and grinding, dating back to the mid to late Bronze Age. They exhibit transitional characteristics from animal petroglyphs to geometric petroglyphs. Meanwhile, Geumjangdae is located at the confluence of the Seocheon and Bukcheon rivers, known for its beautiful scenery, which is said to attract geese to rest, and the surrounding area has been developed into the Geumjangdae Wetland Park.','38-9, Seokjang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(888,54,'en','Seongdeokdaewang Sinjong','Seongdeokdaewang Sinjong is a bell that was started by King Gyeongdeok, the 35th king of Silla, in memory of his father, King Seongdeok, and was completed in 771 by his son, King Hyegong. At the top of the bell, there are a dragon-shaped handle and a sound hole, and the body is adorned with a decorative band featuring a pattern of vines from above, four sound holes, four celestial beings, two platforms, and at the bottom, a decorative band of vines and lotus patterns. Overall, it is considered the most outstanding masterpiece among Korean bells due to its elegant shape, splendid decoration, and beautiful, lingering sound.','186 Iljeong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, National Gyeongju Museum','- Weekdays 10:00~18:00 (Last admission 17:30) - Weekends and holidays 10:00~19:00 (Last admission 18:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','Closed January 1 and on the days of Lunar New Year and Chuseok.',NULL),(889,91,'en','Gyeongju Yangdong Mucheomdang','Mucheomdang, located in Yangdong Village in Gyeongju, is part of the ancestral home of Hwaejae Lee Eon-jeok (1491–1553), a Confucian scholar and official during the Joseon Dynasty, and was built in the mid-Joseon period. The building has a size of five rooms in the front and two rooms on the side, divided into three sections inside, with the middle three rooms serving as a main hall and one ondol room on each side. The main hall is open between the front columns, and the side facing the main hall is also open, while the back and side walls are enclosed with doors. The floor plan is L-shaped, with round and square columns supporting the rooms and the maru (wooden floor). The function of this building is an extension of the sarangchae (guesthouse) in a noble residence, used for receiving guests, resting, and reading. It showcases simple yet refined craftsmanship and is built faithfully to the functions of a separate building, preserving the relics of Hwaejae Lee Eon-jeok. The name Mucheomdang reflects the resolve of descendants not to tarnish the legacy left by their ancestors, as it is the pen name of Lee Eon-jeok\'s grandson, Lee Eui-yun (1564–1597). Yangdong Village is a historical village with a tradition of over 500 years and was designated as a UNESCO World Heritage site in 2010. The village is filled with valuable cultural heritage, including nationally designated cultural properties, and the entire village is an important folk material, with guided tours available six times a day.','32-19 Yangdongmaeul-an-gil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Summer season (April–September): 09:00–19:00. Winter season (October–March): 09:00–18:00.',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','Closed every Monday',NULL),(890,130,'en','Firefly Camping Site','Firefly Camping Site, located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, is a place where you can enjoy camping surrounded by nature. In spring, you can see cherry blossoms, in summer, the lush shade of trees, in autumn, colorful fallen leaves, and in winter, charming snow. The camping site offers general camping areas and bungalows. The site sizes vary slightly by area, so it is advisable to check before visiting.','250-13, Daehyeon-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(891,67,'en','Jureongjureong Gyeongju Branch','Jureongjureong is a combination of ZOO, meaning zoo, and Green Lung, which refers to a green space that provides oxygen in the midst of a bleak urban environment. Jureongjureong is the first animal theme park in South Korea where you can meet living beings breathing in the city. It aims to be a place where people can feel the preciousness of life through close interactions without fences, going beyond simply observing animals, and providing rest and healing for modern people in the heart of the city.','80 Expo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Cheongun-dong)','- Weekdays 11:00~17:00 (Last entry at 16:00) - Weekends 11:00~18:00 (Last entry at 17:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','First and third Monday of every month',NULL),(892,10,'en','Samneung Valley Stone Buddha','The seated statue of Buddha carved into the massive natural rock wall in Baedong, Gyeongju, stands 6m tall. It is the largest seated Buddha among the statues on Namsan and is believed to be a stone Buddha in the style that was popular in the late Unified Silla period. The rock itself is slightly tilted backward, making the carved statue appear to gaze up at the distant sky. The figure leans back slightly, and its half-closed eyes seem to look down upon the beings of the secular world. The area from the head to the shoulders is deeply carved to create a three-dimensional effect, while the body is carved very shallowly. Unlike the refined and neat faces of other statues in this area, this statue gives a somewhat rough impression.','341-126 Namsan Circular Road, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Baedong)','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(893,856,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Bulgok Stone Buddha','The Gyeongju Namsan Bulgok Stone Buddha is a seated statue of Buddha carved into a rock in the Buddha Valley at the eastern foot of Namsan Mountain in Gyeongju. This stone statue is the oldest remaining stone Buddha from the Silla period in Namsan, believed to have been created in the late Three Kingdoms period. The valley got its name from this statue, which has a head that appears to be covered by a headdress, extending down to the ears. The face is round and slightly bowed, with swollen eyes and deeply carved lips that radiate an inner smile. The robe draped over both shoulders flows down to cover the pedestal on which the statue sits, with the hem beautifully carved in a wave pattern, creating a harmonious overall appearance. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','56 San, Inwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(894,22,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Tapgok Stone Buddha Statues','The area around Gyeongju Namsan was the site of a temple called Sininsa during the Unified Silla period. On the large rock to the south, traces of wooden structures remain, and the scattered stone pagoda fragments indicate that a south-facing temple was managed with the Buddha statue on the southern side as the main object of worship. Several Buddha statues are artistically depicted on a large square rock that is about 9 meters tall. On the southern rock face, there are three main figures and an independent bodhisattva, while the eastern rock face also features Buddha statues, bodhisattvas, monks, and celestial beings. The Buddha and bodhisattva statues all have lotus-patterned pedestals and halos that symbolize the light emanating from their bodies, each with different postures and expressions. The celestial beings are depicted flying in the sky, and the monk is in a posture of offering to the Buddha and bodhisattva, but all are severely eroded, making detailed carving techniques indiscernible. On the western rock face, there are two Bodhi trees under which Buddha is said to have attained enlightenment, along with a statue of the Buddha. The effort to carve various forms such as Buddha, celestial beings, bodhisattvas, monks, and pagodas on a single rock face shows the artisan\'s intention to depict the Buddhist world in their mind. Although the carving style is highly stylized, the artistic arrangement of the elaborate carvings is unique in our country.','36 Tapgol-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Baebandong)','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(895,37,'en','Seated Stone Buddha at Mireuksan, Gyeongju','This seated stone Buddha, estimated to be from the Silla period, stands at a total height of 4.36m, with the Buddha itself measuring 2.44m. It is the best-preserved stone Buddha from the Silla period currently found on Namsan Mountain in Gyeongju. The head features a small conch shell-shaped hairstyle with a high topknot (ushnisha), and the round face radiates a subtle inner smile. The robe draped over the shoulders appears to hang limply, with parallel folds carved in various places. The hand gestures show the right hand resting on the knee with the fingertips pointing down, and the left hand resting on the abdomen, representing the \'Bhumisparsha Mudra\' (earth-touching gesture), which looks somewhat delicate. The halo (glory) set apart from the statue is highly decorative, featuring small Buddhas and intricate floral and vine patterns. Notably, the back of the halo is inscribed with a slender line depicting the Medicine Buddha, who is said to relieve all ailments, a unique style only seen in places like the Milyang Muboongsa or the Gyeongbuk University halo. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','66-2, Baeban-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(896,891,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Chilbulam Stone Buddha Statues','The Gyeongju Namsan Chilbulam Stone Buddha Statues refer to the seven statues carved on the rock face within Chilbulam. There is a triad statue facing east on a wide rock face, and on the square stone pillar right in front of the triad statue, there are seated Buddha statues carved on each side. The main statue and the two bodhisattvas form the triad, and when combined with the four directional Buddhas carved on the four sides of the stone pillar, there are a total of seven statues, hence the name Chilbulam. The original name of the temple that existed here is not known. The core statue of this group is the seated Buddha in the center of the triad. This statue is draped in a robe that reveals the right shoulder and is in the hand gesture of \'abhaya mudra\' (the right hand raised and the palm facing outward). The directional Buddhas take different hand gestures according to their directions, and the statue on the eastern side, which corresponds to the front, holds a medicine bowl, indicating it is the Medicine Buddha. There are several holes drilled behind the triad, and the stone pillar has grooves, along with scattered roof tile fragments around, suggesting that this was originally a rock cave temple covered by a roof. Fragments of stone scriptures inscribed with the \'Medicine Sutra\' and \'Diamond Sutra\' have been found in this area, indicating that it is related to the folk belief in the Medicine Buddha, wishing for blessings, longevity, health, and good fortune.','San 36-4 Namsan-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open all year round',NULL),(897,866,'en','Gyeongju Namsan Sinsanam Stone Bodhisattva Statue','Gyeongju Namsan can be considered a treasure trove of artifacts and relics, where you can encounter various Buddhist statues from the Three Kingdoms period to the late Unified Silla period. Among them, the 1.4m tall stone Bodhisattva statue is carved on the southern rock directly above Chilbulam. It appears as if it is sitting on a cloud, wearing a three-faced crown, indicating that it is a Bodhisattva statue. The face is plump, and the slightly closed eyes seem to be lost in deep thought, as if observing sentient beings from a world above the clouds. The right hand holds a flower, while the left hand is raised to the chest, expressing the gesture of preaching. The heavenly robe is very thin, realistically revealing the body\'s contours, and the hems of the robe cover the pedestal and hang down long. The halo, equipped with a head halo and a body halo, utilizes the space where the statue sits, making the Bodhisattva statue stand out more, and it appears to be a work from the late 8th century of the Unified Silla period.','36-4 Namsan-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(898,55,'en','Gyeongju Jaemaejeong','Gyeongju Jaemaejeong is a well located at the house of General Kim Yu-sin of Silla. It was built by stacking granite like bricks, and this area is presumed to be the site of the general\'s house. It is said that when General Kim Yu-sin returned from a long time on the battlefield and was about to leave for war again, he passed by his house without seeing his family and drew water from the well to drink on horseback, saying, \'The taste of my home water is just as it was in the old days.\' In 1993, an excavation survey was conducted, uncovering a 70m area centered around Jaemaejeong. The well is 5.7m deep, with the widest part measuring 1.8m and the bottom diameter being 1.2m, made of finely shaped stones like bricks. Next to the well, there is a stone pavilion with a stele written by Lee Man-woon in the 9th year of Gojong (1872).','89-7 Gyodong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(899,18,'en','Gyeongju Dongbang-dong Wayoji','Gyeongju Dongbang-dong Wayoji is a kiln site that was accidentally discovered during land development work in 1977. The National Gyeongju Museum conducted excavations and uncovered nine kilns used for firing pottery and tiles. One of the kilns was found to be a sloped kiln (deungyo) with a total length of 10.5m and a width of 1.72m, utilizing the hillside. Some parts of the ceiling wall of the pottery firing area remain, and there is a high wall between the area where pottery was shaped and the firing room. The excavated tile fragments mostly consist of decorative tiles with patterns of new feathers and lotus flowers that were popular during the Goryeo Dynasty, as well as tiles produced during the Joseon Dynasty. A roof tile inscribed with \'Qianlong\' found at the kiln site is believed to date from the time the kiln site was abandoned, suggesting that the kiln was in operation from the Goryeo Dynasty to the late Joseon Dynasty. To operate a kiln, high-quality clay and water for making pottery and tiles, as well as fuel for firing, are needed. The Dongbang-dong area meets all these conditions, and with a transportation route to the west, it is presumed to have been responsible for pottery production for a long time.','343-4 Dongbang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(900,32,'en','Gyeongju Neungjitap Site','This site was formerly known as Neungjitap or Yeonhwa-tap, where the Neungjitap once stood. The collapsed and abandoned pagoda was investigated multiple times by the Silla Samseong Investigation Team from 1969 and was restored to its current form in 1979. Neungjitap is presumed to be a five-story pagoda made by stacking stones with zodiac figures on all four sides of the base and carving lotus patterns. Additionally, many fragments of clay Buddha statues and a large number of roof tile pieces were excavated, suggesting that there were niches for Buddha statues on all four sides of the pagoda. The base of the pagoda was built with dressed stones, and the top was covered with soil and grass was planted. Around the base, nine zodiac figures were placed in accordance with the directions, with eight of them moved from an unfinished royal tomb site in front of Hwangboksa on the eastern side of Namsan. The upper part of the pagoda was built in the same shape as the base, but it differs in that an additional layer of supporting stones was placed on top. The top of the pagoda was finished with a turtle-shaped roof made of earth. Currently, there are 36 stones carved with lotus patterns stacked around the pagoda, and next to it, there are traces of an earthen mound whose nature has not been clarified. According to the \'Samguk Sagi\', King Munmu of Silla (reigned 661–681) instructed that upon his death, he should be cremated simply within ten days in the courtyard outside the palace. However, a stone inscription of King Munmu\'s tomb was discovered near the Sacheonwangsa site, leading to the assumption that he was cremated at the Neungjitap site in Gyeongju. This is likely why Neungjitap was referred to as Neungsitap.','621-1 Baeban-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(901,71,'en','Gyeongju Seokjosamyeon Buddha','The Gyeongju Seokjosamyeon Buddha is a rock statue from the Unified Silla period located at the site of Gyeongju Guhwalsa. It is approximately 3 meters tall and features a statue carved on each of its four sides, hence it is called a four-sided stone Buddha. The western side depicts Amitabha Buddha of the Western Paradise, the eastern side depicts the Medicine Buddha of the Luminous World, the northern side depicts Maitreya Buddha, and the southern side depicts Shakyamuni Buddha. According to the \'Samguk Yusa\', when King Gyeongdeok of Silla visited Baekryulsa, he heard the sound of chanting from the ground. Upon digging, this rock was discovered, and the Buddha statues were carved on its sides, leading to the establishment of Guhwalsa. While this record is not definitive, it is estimated that the statue was created around this time based on various conditions. The Gyeongju Seokjosamyeon Buddha is notable for its unique arrangement of three-dimensional expressions, relief and intaglio techniques, and representations of seated and standing figures, showcasing the characteristics of early Unified Silla.','4214-76, San-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(902,62,'en','Gyeongju Yuldong Ma-ae Yerae Samjon Ipsang','This is a rock-carved triad of Buddhas (Samjonbul) facing west on the cliff of Byeokdosan in Gyeongju. This statue inherits the style of the stone Buddha at Gyeongju Gulbulsa Temple (Treasure) nearby and is a representative work of the Unified Silla period, featuring Amitabha Buddha in the center, with Avalokiteshvara and Mahasthamaprapta on either side. Amitabha\'s head is very large, with a low topknot (ushnisha) resembling a hat, similar to the style of the stone Buddha at Gulbulsa. The face is plump with a smile. The shoulders are broad and straight, and the clothing draped over the shoulders is thin, revealing the body\'s curves well. The right hand is lowered while the left hand is placed on the chest, with the thumb and middle finger touching, indicating that this statue represents Amitabha. The feet are uniquely positioned sideways rather than forward. The bodhisattva on the left emphasizes a slender femininity compared to the plump main Buddha. The body\'s curves are clearly visible, and the feet are also positioned sideways. The right hand is raised to the shoulder, with the thumb and middle finger touching, while the left hand holds a treasure bottle, indicating that this bodhisattva is Avalokiteshvara. The bodhisattva on the right has a similar appearance and is another attendant bodhisattva, Mahasthamaprapta. Behind the heads of these statues, a round halo is depicted. While this statue is fundamentally similar to the stone Buddha at Gyeongju Gulbulsa, differences in plumpness, foot shape, and clothing folds suggest a slightly different production period.','69 Dudaean-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Yuldong)','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(903,17,'en','Gyeongju Geumcheok-ri Tombs','The tombs of Silla located in the plains of Geumcheok-ri near Gyeongju, where 30 large and small tombs are gathered. According to legend, this is the place where the founder of Silla, Park Hyeokgeose, created over 40 fake tombs to hide the gold (geumja) he received from the heavens. It is said that the real tombs are still buried among these. Although no formal investigation has been conducted, two tombs that were destroyed in 1952 were examined. The tombs are characterized by the Silla-style stone mound tombs (jeokseokmokgakbun), which consist of a rectangular pit dug and a wooden coffin installed. Artifacts such as gold earrings and jade were recovered. The tombs here are all smaller than the flatland tombs in Gyeongju city, suggesting they belong to the lower nobility of Silla. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','192-1 Geumcheok-ri, Geoncheon-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(904,19,'en','Gyeongju Inwang-dong Temple Site','The Gyeongju Inwang-dong Temple Site is presumed to be the site of the Inyongsa Temple. According to the \'Samguk Yusa\', Inyongsa was a temple built to pray for the well-being of Kim In-mun (629-694), the second son of King Muyeol. Records indicate that after the fall of Goguryeo, the Tang Dynasty attempted to conquer Silla and imprisoned Kim In-mun, who was staying in Tang. The people of Silla opened a Gwan-eum temple to pray for his return, but when Kim In-mun died on his way back in the third year of King Hyo-so\'s reign (694), they changed it to a Mita temple to pray for his rebirth in paradise. Inyongsa is the first temple built for an individual rather than a monk or king in Silla, showcasing the form of faith at that time. From 2002 to 2011, the National Gyeongju Cultural Heritage Research Institute conducted four excavations. The site features a typical double-tower layout of Silla, including a rare A-shaped building site, as well as sites for pagodas, main halls, lecture halls, corridors, lotus ponds, and wells.','342 Inwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(905,857,'en','Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power Promotion Center','The Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power Promotion Center showcases the energy we use. The center exhibits the operating principles of various energies, including electric energy, nuclear energy, and renewable energy. If you want to learn about the essential energies in our lives, visiting the Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power Promotion Center is recommended.','1655 Bulguk-ro, Munmu-daewang-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~17:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Every Sunday / Public holidays',NULL),(906,255,'en','Haesolbang','Haesolbang is a seafood kalguksu (noodle soup) specialty restaurant located near Bulguksa Temple. They purchase fresh clams and cockles directly from Jinseo-myeon, Buan-gun, Jeollabuk-do for cooking. The representative menu is seafood clam kalguksu, and they also offer handmade pork cutlets and jjambbong kalguksu as special dishes. It is a family-friendly restaurant that many families visit, and it is located near Gyeongju\'s representative tourist site, Bulguksa Temple.','66-10 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seafood clam kalguksu / Jjambbong kalguksu / Handmade pork cutlet / Cheese pork cutlet / Seafood chives pancake, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(907,164,'en','[Baeknyeonggag] Oebau','Oebau An-gang branch started in 1968 as a small meat restaurant in An-gang market. Inheriting the methods and philosophy of the parents\' generation, who handled only Korean beef and pork honestly, it has been operated with the same heart for 57 years. Over the years, many customers have visited Oebau, establishing it as a local favorite. Oebau uses top-grade Korean beef and fresh pork. All basic ingredients that affect the taste are also selected under strict standards, ensuring safe consumption. The signature dishes include mushroom grilled pork belly and shrimp octopus stir-fry, which are full of smoky flavor and aroma. The mushroom Korean beef hot pot and octopus hot pot are also rich in broth and generous portions, enticing repeat visits.','12 Guburang 3-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mushroom Grilled Pork Belly Shrimp Stir-fry / Mushroom Grilled Pork Belly Stir-fry / Mushroom Grilled Pork Belly Octopus Stir-fry / Mushroom Korean Beef Hot Pot / Mushroom Korean Beef Octopus Hot Pot, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(908,50,'en','Lee Sang-bok\'s Gyeongju Bread Forest Head Branch','Lee Sang-bok\'s Gyeongju Bread Forest Head Branch is a bakery located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The bread from Lee Sang-bok is made using only natural ingredients without preservatives or artificial sweeteners, making it a popular choice among many people. With a long history of boiling red beans and baking bread, the artisan\'s spirit of using only natural ingredients ensures that the taste is excellent and health-conscious. The representative menu is Lee Sang-bok Gyeongju Bread, which captures the traditional taste passed down through generations of the founder\'s techniques. You can enjoy the fantastic harmony of the thin and savory flour shell with the subtly sweet domestic red bean paste. In addition, various breads such as cinnamon bread, glutinous barley bread, and green tea bread are also sold.','212 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bomun-dong)','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(909,825,'en','Gyeongju Donggungwon','Gyeongju Donggungwon is located at the entrance of the Bomun Tourist Complex and was originally used for agricultural test fields and flower cultivation. It was developed to transform agriculture into a tourism resource, creating a year-round experiential tourism facility through the development of new tourism content. The historical records from the Samguk Sagi mention that in the 14th year of King Munmu, our ancestors first cultivated flowers and rare birds and animals at Donggung and Wolji, which were the first botanical gardens in Korea. The diverse historical content unique to Gyeongju is narrated through storytelling, and the modern recreation of Donggung and Wolji, the first botanical garden in Korea, has been realized at Gyeongju Donggungwon. This place allows visitors to see both the \'Donggung Botanical Garden\' and the bird-specialized zoo \'Gyeongju Bird Park\' in one location.','74-14 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Botanical Garden 09:30~19:00 - Bird Park 10:00~19:00 ※ Last ticket sales and entry close at 18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available','Botanical Garden: closed every Monday (or the next weekday when Monday is a holiday), January 1, and on the days of Lunar New Year and Chuseok. Bird Park: open year-round.',NULL),(910,873,'en','Gyeongju Choi\'s House','Located at the site of the royal palace of the Silla Dynasty, Gyeongju Choi\'s House is the ancestral home of the Choi family in Gyeongju. It has been inhabited for nine generations, and although it is said that this house was built around 1700, the exact date is unknown. The building consists of a sarangchae (men\'s quarters), an anchae (women\'s quarters), and a main gate, with the main gate having a small room and a large storeroom. The sarangchae was opposite the inner courtyard but was destroyed in a fire in November 1970, leaving only the site. The anchae behind the sarangchae is open in a square shape, but the main building has a \'ㄷ\' shaped floor plan, and the \'ㄱ\' shaped sarangchae and the straight main gate were combined. Additionally, there is a family shrine (gamyo) separately arranged to the northwest of the anchae, with a straight path leading south that is impressive. There is a flower garden behind the anchae, adding beauty to the house\'s layout, and it is well-preserved as an example of a traditional Yangban house from the Joseon Dynasty, making it an important resource. The original name at the time of designation was Gyeongju Choi Sik\'s House (慶州崔植氏家屋), but as the Gyeongju Choi family has lived here for generations and it is widely known as the wealthy Choi\'s house in Gyeongju, the name was changed to Gyeongju Gyodong Choi\'s Historic House in January 2007. (Source: Cultural Heritage Administration)','19-21 Gyocheon-an-gil, Gyeongju (Gyodong)','09:30~17:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Last Monday of every month',NULL),(911,86,'en','Golgulam Taphoni (Gyeongbuk East Coast National Geopark)','Golgulam is the first stone cave temple in Korea, located in Yangbuk-myeon, Gyeongju. It is believed to have been created in the 6th century by a group of monks who came from India, utilizing the natural cave (taphoni) that existed here. The andesitic tuff found in the Golgulam area was formed when the East Sea was created as Japan, which was once connected to the Korean Peninsula, pulled away. The pulling force affected the Golgulam area, causing the ground to crack, and volcanic sediments accumulated in the gaps, forming andesitic tuff. It is relatively weak against wind and rain, making it easier to erode. As the wind and rain eroded the rock, the large and small rock fragments included in the rock created numerous holes, which grew larger during the interglacial and glacial periods of the Quaternary. These numerous holes are referred to as taphoni. Golgulam is a stone cave that has been shaped from these taphoni caves, where Buddhist statues have been placed. This is very unique in a country where hard granite is prevalent, indicating that the Silla people had a good understanding of the properties of the rocks. Thus, Golgulam is a valuable site where naturally developed taphoni and Silla Buddhist culture harmonize.','101-5 Girim-ro, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(912,95,'en','Namsan Granite (Gyeongbuk East Coast National Geopark)','Located south of Gyeongju, Namsan is a long oval-shaped granite mountain centered around Geumobong and Gowi-bong. Granite is harder and less eroded by rain and wind compared to commonly used stones like marble or limestone. Therefore, the numerous cultural assets of Namsan have been well preserved over a long time due to this characteristic of granite. Furthermore, Namsan granite is known to have been used in the construction of cultural assets representing Silla, such as the Seokgatap and Dabotap. The Silla people utilized the rocky cliffs of Namsan to create notable Buddhist statues among Namsan\'s cultural assets, such as the Seated Three Buddhas, Seated Sakyamuni, and Seated Buddha, which were naturally formed by vertical cracks that commonly develop in Namsan granite. It is presumed that the reason the granite in Namsan has more vertical cracks than other granites is due to fault activity that occurred in this area a long time ago.','341-126 Namsan Circular Road, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(913,842,'en','Gyeongju Yangnam Columnar Joint','The Gyeongju Yangnam Columnar Joint, located in Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, was designated as a natural monument on September 25, 2012, due to its recognized scale and diversity of forms of columnar joints developed along the East Coast. Columnar joints refer to hexagonal pillars formed mainly from volcanic rocks such as basalt. The columnar joints that make up the Gyeongju Yangnam Columnar Joint exhibit various shapes, including fan-shaped columnar joints, lying columnar joints, tilted columnar joints, and upward protruding columnar joints, all gathered in a short coastal area. Among these, the fan-shaped columnar joints, which are rounded, are a rare example globally, and their formation process has not yet been clarified, attracting the interest of many geologists.','498-13 Donghaean-ro, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all the time',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(914,830,'en','Hwarang Village','Gyeongju Hwarang Village is a place that reinterprets and expands the spirit and culture of Hwarang, our precious cultural heritage, opening a new paradigm for youth training activities, global experiential tourism, and cultural relaxation. Hwarang Village not only serves as a youth training facility but also has surrounding facilities such as the Hwarang Exhibition Hall for family tourists to enjoy content, a gathering place for relaxation and healing, a children\'s playground, and pleasant walking paths, making it a new landmark in Gyeongju known for its beautiful night views. Additionally, Hwarang Village conducts facility rental projects for various purposes such as global experiential education, culture and tourism, relaxation programs, youth training and exchange, and cultural activities.','123 Seokhyeon-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Hwarang Exhibition Hall] 09:00~18:00 [Accommodation] 14:00~11:00 next day [Camping Ground] 13:00~12:00 next day',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,'Available (10 large / 200 small cars)','Closed January 1 and during the Lunar New Year and Chuseok holidays.',NULL),(915,874,'en','Gyeongju Myeonghwal Fortress','Gyeongju Myeonghwal Fortress is a Silla-era mountain fortress surrounding Myeonghwal Mountain and played a significant role in the defense of the capital along with Namsan Fortress, Seohyeong Fortress, and Bukhyung Fortress. The circumference of the fortress is about 6 km, and it features both earthen and stone walls, with the stone walls reflecting the early Silla construction method using unrefined natural stones. According to the \'Samguk Sagi\', in the 4th year of King Silseong (405), Japanese troops attacked Myeonghwal Fortress, but they were repelled, indicating that it was built before that time. Additionally, in the 15th year of King Nulji (431), the Japanese pirates besieged and attacked this fortress, highlighting its importance in protecting the capital of Silla, Geumseong. From the 18th year of King Jabi (475) to the 10th year of King Soji (488), this place was used as a palace. During Queen Seondeok\'s reign, Bidam and others used this fortress as a base for rebellion, but it was suppressed by the government troops led by Kim Yushin. A stone monument from the 12th year of King Jinheung (551) was discovered around the fortress, providing information about the construction, including the chief engineer, workers, and construction period, indicating that it was initially an earthen fortress that was later rebuilt as a stone fortress. It is currently stored in the National Gyeongju Museum.','Bohmun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(916,108,'en','Gyeongju Hwabaek Convention Center','HICO (Hwabaek International Convention Center) is an exhibition and convention center located in the Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Complex, a representative tourist area in Korea. The name HICO is derived from the Silla era\'s consensus system called \'Hwabaek\'. Hwabaek is a decision-making body based on unanimous agreement. Located in the heart of the Bomun Tourist Complex, it has the significant advantage of hosting various events, accommodations, and tourism all in one place. With state-of-the-art meeting and exhibition facilities and various amenities, it is the best convention center for successfully hosting diverse events for organizers and participants.','507 Bomun-ro, Sinpyeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(917,875,'en','Gyeongju Wind Power (Hill of Wind)','Located at the summit of Johaengsan, adjacent to Tohamsan, the Gyeongju Wind Power Complex is situated. This commercial wind power complex aims to produce eco-friendly clean energy, currently operating a total of 7 wind turbines. It generates enough electricity to power about 10,000 households annually. The impressive giant wind turbines lined along the mountain ridge are known as the Hill of Wind, and it is open to the public year-round. There are spaces for visitors, including the observation deck Gyeongpungru, walking trails, and picnic table zones. It is particularly famous for its beautiful sunsets, and many people visit to enjoy the starlit night sky after sunset, making it a new healing spot in Gyeongju.','1056-185 Bulguk-ro, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(918,242,'en','Cafe Flavius','Cafe Flavius is located in the Bomun Tourist Complex in Gyeongju. Its exterior gives the feeling of being in the Colosseum in Rome, Italy, making it popular. The interior is beautifully decorated, providing many photo opportunities. Thanks to the view of Bomun Lake, the atmosphere is great, making it an ideal date spot. Pets are allowed only in the outdoor area. During the summer season, drinks containing mountain ginseng are sold, adding freshness with homegrown rosemary and apple mint.','132-16 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','10:00~21:00 (Last order 20:40)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Flavius Vienna ice / Croffle / Sangria ice / Brownie gelato / Heonasan mountain ginseng latte ice, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(919,144,'en','Gondalbi Camp','Gondalbi Camp is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 37 km away from Gyeongju City Hall. You can reach it by driving along Yongdam-ro, Geonpo Industrial Road, and Dansuk Road. The travel time is approximately 50 minutes. This place is surrounded by forests, allowing for a nature-friendly camping experience. Additionally, there is a valley nearby where you can enjoy both water activities and camping. The campsite has 17 general camping sites, all made of crushed stone. The site size is 6m wide and 7m long, accommodating personal trailers and caravans. The management office rents out camping equipment such as extension cords, fire pits, heating devices, and tableware. The campsite operates on weekends and closes for maintenance from January to February each year. Nearby attractions include the Gyeongju National Park Dansuk Mountain area and Unmun Lake, making it convenient for combined tourism, and there are several restaurants operating around the tourist sites.','58-31 Hashin-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 14:00 - Check-out 12:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(920,143,'en','Gaon Nuri Camping Experience Site','Gaon Nuri Camping Experience Site is located in Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 19 km from Gyeongju City Hall. Accessible by car via Baekryul-ro, Yongdam-ro, and Saean-hyeon-ro, it takes about 30 minutes to arrive. This site, remodeled from an old school into a camping site, is filled with unique facilities. It features a small library for children, a playroom, a maze, and a movie theater, along with a bamboo forest walking path, a water experience area, and a ping pong room, providing plenty of activities for children. The camping site has 46 general camping sites, consisting of 36 gravel sites and 10 deck sites, and personal trailers and caravans are allowed. The management office rents out extension cords, fire pits, heating devices, tableware, and sleeping bags. Heading towards Gyeongju City Hall from the camping site allows for linked travel to famous tourist spots like Daereungwon, Cheomseongdae, and the National Gyeongju Museum. There are also many restaurants nearby offering a variety of cuisines.','2037, Hoguk-ro, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(921,142,'en','Gyeongju Byeolbit Maru Glamping Site and Pension','Gyeongju Byeolbit Maru is located in Cheonbuk-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 11 km from Gyeongju City Hall. Accessible by car via Industrial Road, Cheonbuk Road, and Cheonggal Road, it takes about 20 minutes to arrive. Located in a forest, this site has 18 glamping units. The glamping rooms are equipped with beds, camping chairs, and air conditioning, but do not have toilets, showers, or sinks inside. The outdoor private deck includes ice boxes, cooking utensils, tableware, and integrated tables with chairs, and wireless internet is available on-site. Barbecue use is prohibited for fatty meats like pork belly due to fire hazards. Minors must be accompanied by guardians, and pets are not allowed. There are no tourist attractions nearby, and for linked tourism, visitors must head towards Gyeongju City Hall, where many restaurants are available.','1-75, Saeteoheungnim-gil, Cheonbuk-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(922,141,'en','Munbok Mountain Camping Site','Munbok Mountain Camping Site is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It takes about an hour to reach from Gyeongju City Hall. Located at the foot of Munbok Mountain, it allows visitors to fully enjoy the benefits of pristine nature. The changing scenery with the seasons delights the eyes. The camping site has 70 general camping sites. The 50 gravel sites measure 10m by 7m, while the 20 deck sites measure 6m by 6m. From 10 PM to 7 AM, a quiet mode is enforced, and from midnight, a sleeping mode is in effect. Reservations for more than 3 teams are not allowed, and each site accommodates 2 adults, 2 children, and 1 vehicle. Hammocks are not allowed in all areas, and smoking is only permitted in designated areas. Nearby attractions include National Unmun Mountain Natural Recreation Forest and Gajisan Provincial Park, making it easy to travel.','333-199, Munbok-ro, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(923,140,'en','Gyeongju Oryu Camping Site','Gyeongju Oryu Camping Site is located in Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 35 km from Gyeongju City Hall. Accessible by car via Gyeonggam-ro, Tohamsan-ro, and National Route 31, it takes about 50 minutes to arrive. Located in front of Oryu Goara Beach, one of Gyeongju\'s representative beaches, this site attracts many visitors during summer for swimming and camping. The camping site has 8 general camping sites and 28 caravans. The general camping sites are all made of gravel, while the caravans are equipped with beds, air conditioning, refrigerators, sinks, cooking utensils, tableware, toilets, and showers. The camping site operates year-round, but personal trailers and caravans are not allowed. The nearby Oryu Goara Beach, along with Najeong Fine Sand Beach and Yangpo Port, offers rich tourist resources. Several restaurants are also operating nearby.','2468-14, Donghaean-ro, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Caravan] - Check-in 14:00 - Check-out 11:00 [Camping Site] - Check-in 13:00 - Check-out 11:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(924,139,'en','Gyeongju Tent House Glamping','Gyeongju Tent House Glamping is located in Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 17 km from Gyeongju City Hall. Accessible by car via Industrial Road, Geonpo Industrial Road, and Cheonggang-ro, it takes about 20 minutes to arrive. This site, transformed from an old school into a camping site, has a clean and luxurious feel. All facilities are well-maintained, and the luxury is felt in the glamping experience. The camping site has 15 glamping units and 45 general camping sites. The glamping rooms are equipped with beds, air conditioning, fans, refrigerators, and the outdoor private deck includes camping tables, camping chairs, and cooking utensils. The general camping sites are all made of gravel, with site dimensions of 8.5m by 10m. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju Yangdong Village and Jeungmyeong Natural Ecological Park. Several restaurants are also operating near the former Bujo Station.','5, Wangsinsupgol-an-gil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(925,138,'en','Gyeongju Healing Camp','Gyeongju Healing Camp is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 31 km from Gyeongju City Hall. Accessible by car via Yongdam-ro, Geonpo Industrial Road, Dansuk-ro, and Jangsa-gil, it takes about 40 minutes to arrive. This site is a experiential recreation village located in Dabang Village, surrounded by 23 peaks, known for its dense natural forest and clean valley. The camping site features 18 glamping units and 15 car camping sites. The glamping rooms are equipped with beds, air conditioning, etc. The outdoor private space includes tables, chairs, ice boxes, kitchenware, and barbecue facilities. The camping area consists of 8 deck sites and 7 gravel sites. It operates year-round, and reservations can be made online in real-time. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju National Park Dansuk Mountain District, making it easy to travel.','418-55, Jangsa-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(926,137,'en','Greenhouse Camping Site','Greenhouse Pension Auto Camping Site is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 39 km from Gyeongju City Hall. This camping site harmonizes with a clear valley and lush forest, attracting many visitors during vacation seasons to enjoy camping and water activities in the refreshing forest. The camping site has 25 general camping sites, all made of gravel, with site dimensions of 7m by 7m. Personal trailers and caravans are allowed, and small dogs are permitted. The management office rents extension cords to campers. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju National Park Dansuk Mountain District and National Unmun Mountain Natural Recreation Forest, making it easy to travel.','91-6, Daehyeon-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(927,135,'en','Sannae Byeolbit Auto Camping Site','Sannae Byeolbit Auto Camping Site is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 46 km from Gyeongju City Hall, accessible via the Gyeongbu Expressway, Dansuk-ro, and Munbok-ro, taking approximately 50 minutes. The site is easily accessible as it is adjacent to the road. The camping area is set in a forest, allowing for camping and relaxation in nature. There are 12 general camping sites made of gravel, with site dimensions approximately 6-8m wide and 7-10m long. Fire pits, electricity, and wireless internet are available. Personal trailers and caravans are allowed, with the same fees as general camping sites. The management office rents out tents, extension cords, and heating devices.','333-13, Munbok-ro, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(928,134,'en','Camp ING','Camp ING, located in Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, is about 13 km away from Gyeongju City Hall. It features a camping site converted from an old school in the forest, offering many nostalgic sights. The campsite consists of 30 car camping sites, with 28 gravel sites and 2 deck sites. The site dimensions are 8m wide and 10m long for gravel, and 5m by 5m for the deck. Personal trailers and caravans are allowed, and camping equipment such as extension cords, fire pits, and heating devices can be rented from the management office. It operates on weekends year-round. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju Yangdong Village and An-gye Reservoir, as well as various restaurants including Chinese, Korean, and snack shops.','47, Homyeongkeungol-gil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(929,1197,'en','Jodul Kalguksu','Jodul Kalguksu is a famous Kalguksu restaurant located near the Bomun Tourist Complex in Gyeongju. The signature dish here is Dongjuk Kalguksu, which is made with plenty of fresh seafood, featuring chewy noodles and a cool, rich broth. Seafood pancake is also popular, topped with squid and various seafood, boasting a crispy and savory taste. In addition to Kalguksu, various menus such as clam Kalguksu, perilla seed Kalguksu, and spicy Kalguksu are available for selection according to preference. It is a beloved restaurant that often has a wait during lunch hours.','3-6 Bukgun-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','- 10:00~21:30- Preparation time 16:00~17:00- Last order 20:50',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Dongjuk Kalguksu / Shrimp seafood pancake / Water gun clam soup / Cream soybean noodle soup, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(930,1031,'en','Jeonwonilgi Auto Camping Site','Jeonwonilgi Auto Camping Site is located in the clear nature of Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, boasting a pleasant environment where valleys and dense forests come together. The sites are available in various forms, such as near the valley, close to the swimming pool, and in forested areas, allowing you to enjoy camping according to your preferences. Personal caravans and trailers are allowed, and small pets can also enter if leashed. The campsite is equipped with facilities for family travelers, including a swimming pool, valley, and spaces for children to play, as well as clean restrooms, showers, and washbasins. You can enjoy nature in a spacious site and relaxed atmosphere, and it is a great place to enjoy both camping and travel as it is close to various tourist attractions in Gyeongju.','590-7 Munbok-ro, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 14:00 - Check-out 12:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(931,1033,'en','Hyu & Lock Auto Camping Ground','Hyu & Lock Camping Ground is located in Seokjang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 5 km from Gyeongju City Hall, taking approximately 15 minutes to reach. The camping ground is situated on a low mountain, offering a stunning view below. Facilities such as showers and restrooms are well-maintained, and there are 64 car camping sites, all with gravel flooring. Access for camping trailers and caravans is free, and pets are also allowed. The management office offers rental of camping equipment such as extension cords and heating devices. Nearby, there are many representative tourist attractions of Gyeongju, including Daereungwon, Cheomseongdae, and the National Gyeongju Museum, as well as many active restaurants to enjoy culinary delights.','110-49 Seokhyeon-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Seokjang-dong)','- Check-in 14:00~21:00- Check-out 13:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(932,1034,'en','Like a Spring Day','Like a Spring Day is a camping ground located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, conveniently allowing access to Gyeongju\'s representative tourist sites such as Cheomseongdae and Bulguksa, as well as Pohang\'s Yeongildae Beach and Jukdo Market for combined tourism. There are various restaurants in the vicinity, making it easy to enjoy both travel and cuisine. The camping ground features crushed stone auto camping sites, and personal caravans and trailers can also be used. The facilities, including gender-separated restrooms, showers, and washbasins, are kept clean, and there is a children\'s playroom and a cozy walking path, making it a comfortable stay for family campers.','2522-12 Hokuk-ro, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 14:00- Check-out 13:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(933,136,'en','Yongcheon Tori Auto Camping Site','Yongcheon Tori Auto Camping Site is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 42 km from Gyeongju City Hall, reachable by car via Yongdam-ro, Geonpo Industrial Road, Dansuk-ro, and Munbok-ro, taking about an hour. Surrounded by forests, it offers a refreshing atmosphere, and a valley is just a few steps away, perfect for escaping the summer heat. During apple harvest season, visitors can participate in apple picking for a fee, taking home 1 kg of apples. The camping site has 18 car camping sites made of gravel. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju National Park, National Unmun Mountain Natural Recreation Forest, and Unmun Lake, making it a great spot for travel.','390, Daehyeon-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(934,814,'en','Tourism History Park','Established as part of the Gyeongju Tourism Comprehensive Development Plan in 1971, the Tourism History Park was created to commemorate the opening of the Bomun Tourist Complex on April 6, 1979, which laid the foundation for the tourism industry as Korea\'s first tourist complex. The park symbolizes infinite tourism development and is designed to connect the past, present, and future in the form of a Möbius strip. The park is adjacent to Bomun Lake, allowing visitors to enjoy the scenery while walking along the park\'s trails. Inside the park, there are photo zones set against the backdrop of Bomun Lake, various sculptures, and shaded benches. In spring, the area is adorned with pink cherry blossoms, and in autumn, the colorful foliage attracts many tourists.','Gyeongsangbuk-do, Gyeongju-si, Bukgun-dong 114-11','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(935,145,'en','Yongcheonsu Camping Site','Located in Madong, Gyeongju, this site has good accessibility and is a great location for exploring the nearby historical sites of Gyeongju, including Bulguksa Temple. It is a free camping site where you can enjoy a day picnic without a tent. Facilities for children include a swimming pool for water activities and a boating area.','13-14 Madongkeunmaeul 5-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 15:00 - Check-out 11:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(936,146,'en','The Forest Camping Site','Gyeongju The Forest Camping Site is close to a valley where water activities are possible and features a large grassy area, trampoline, outdoor swimming pool, and sand playground, making it a great camping site for children. The spacing between sites is wide for comfort. Reservations must be made in real-time via the internet or by phone. After booking a site, you can choose your spot on a first-come, first-served basis.','731-107 Naewae-ro, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(937,107,'en','Silla Wolsung Daegun Danso','Silla Wolsung Daegun Danso is a place where the 11th descendants of the Wolsung Park family are enshrined, established by the Wolsung Park Family Association in 2005. Wolsung Daegun refers to Park Eon-ui, the 8th prince of King Gyeongmyeong, the 29th descendant of Park Hyeokgeose of Silla. Park Eon-ui became the founder of the Wolsung Park family when he was conferred the title of Wolsung Daegun. Silla Wolsung Daegun Danso features a wide lawn and various plants and trees, making it a pleasant place for leisurely walks. It is also conveniently located near Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and Donggung and Wolji, making it easy for combined tourism.','534-1 Poseok-ro, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available',NULL,NULL),(938,237,'en','Bulguksa Milmyeon','Bulguksa Milmyeon is a famous restaurant in Gyeongju known for its refreshing milmyeon (cold noodles). The signature menu is a set that includes mulmilmyeon (cold milmyeon) and grilled meat. The noodles here are made with corn starch and dried mulberry leaves, giving them a very chewy texture. Other options include bibimmilmyeon (spicy cold noodles) and grilled meat, as well as spicy pepper milmyeon and grilled meat. All menu items are available for takeout, and the restaurant has group seating available for gatherings. Parking can be found at the nearby Bulguksa Public Market. Nearby attractions include Seokguram and Bulguksa, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','29 Bulgukjangteo-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Gujeong-dong)','- 11:00~19:00 - Last order for lunch 15:50 - Preparation time 16:00~17:00 - Last order for dinner 18:50',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mulmilmyeon + Grilled Meat / Bibimmilmyeon + Grilled Meat / Spicy Pepper Milmyeon + Grilled Meat / Dumplings, etc.','Not available','Closed during Seollal and Chuseok holidays',NULL),(939,235,'en','Hanuri Garden','Hanuri Garden is a Korean beef specialty restaurant located under Myeonghwal Mountain Fortress. The signature menu is Korean Beef Yukhoe Bibimbap. Other dishes include Korean Beef Mulhoe, Korean Beef Tteokgalbi Set, and premium Korean beef rib meat. The restaurant is conveniently located near Gyeongju Donggungwon and Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Complex, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','218 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bomun-dong)','11:00~21:30 (Preparation time 15:00~17:00) * Operates without preparation time on weekends',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Premium Korean Beef Soup / Premium Korean Beef Soft Tofu / Korean Beef Handmade Tteokgalbi Set / Korean Beef Yukhoe Bibimbap / Korean Beef Rib Meat / Korean Beef Mulhoe, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(940,179,'en','Nakji Masil','Nakji Masil is located in the Bomun Tourist Complex in Gyeongju, and its signature dish is Nakgobsae (stir-fried octopus with noodles). In addition, it serves stir-fried octopus, seafood pancakes, etc. All menus are available for takeout. It is a large establishment with two floors that can accommodate 200 people, making it suitable for group dining and reservations are possible. As a specialty store for Nakgobsae that reflects the characteristics of the Gyeongju region, it is a popular restaurant with fresh ingredients and careful cooking. The crispy seafood pancake is also very popular. There are many famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju nearby, such as Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and the National Gyeongju Museum.','9 Bukgun-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','- 11:00~21:00 - Preparation time 15:30~17:00 - Last order 20:30 ※ Operates without preparation time on weekends',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Nakgobsae / Seafood pancake / Nakgob / Stir-fried octopus etc.','Available','Day before and on the day of Seollal and Chuseok',NULL),(941,249,'en','Tohamhye','Tohamhye is a traditional Korean restaurant famous for its braised short ribs. The signature menu includes Tohamhye special, which allows you to taste braised short ribs, cheonggukjang (fermented soybean paste stew), and barley rice all at once. There is also a soybean paste set meal that comes with doenjang jjigae instead of cheonggukjang. The restaurant has group seating available and reservations can be made. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju Donggungwon and Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Complex, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','3-3 Sanggangseon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Baebandong)','11:20~18:00 (Last order 17:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Set meal / Braised short ribs / Galbitang, etc.',NULL,NULL,NULL),(942,234,'en','Jeongsugaseong','Jeongsugaseong is a place where you can enjoy a traditional Korean course meal while looking out at the mountains and valleys through the windows of a beautiful hanok. The signature menu is the Lotus Leaf Rice Jeongsugaseong Course. Other options include West Coast Blue Crab Soy Sauce Crab Set, Korean Beef Bulgogi Set, and Plum Korean Beef Mulhoe Set. The restaurant has group seating available and reservations can be made. The parking lot is spacious, making it convenient for visits, and the food is neatly presented, making it an ideal restaurant for family gatherings or visits during travel. Nearby, there are many famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including the UNESCO World Heritage Site Seokguram Grotto, Bulguksa Temple, and Cheomseongdae.','318 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','10:00~21:00 (Last order 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Lotus Leaf Rice Jeongsugaseong Course / Beef Short Rib Stew / Domestic Blue Crab Soy Sauce Crab / Beoseongpo Barley Grilled Fish, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(943,233,'en','So-ok','So-ok is a popular restaurant located on Hwanglidangil. The signature menu is beef short rib stew. Other dishes include grilled ribs and seaweed rice balls. The popular beef short rib stew is known for its tender texture that melts in your mouth and spicy seasoning. There is no dedicated parking, but you can use the nearby public parking lot. The restaurant is surrounded by famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, such as Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and the National Gyeongju Museum.','29 Poseok-ro 1050beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','10:30~21:00 (Preparation time 15:30~17:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Beef Short Rib Stew / Seaweed Rice Balls / Napa Cabbage Pancake / Grilled Ribs, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(944,232,'en','Hyanghwajeong','Hyanghwajeong is located on Hwanglidangil in Gyeongju. You can taste Gyeongju Yukhoe Bibimbap, Cockle Salad Bibimbap, Seafood Pancake, and Gyeongju Mulhoe (cold raw fish soup). The Yukhoe Bibimbap is known for its fresh raw beef and rich flavor, while the seafood pancake is crispy and packed with abundant seafood ingredients. The restaurant does not have dedicated parking, so you must park in nearby public parking lots or along the road by Gyeongju Park High School. There are many famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including the National Gyeongju Museum.','17 Sajeng-ro 57beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Sajeng-dong)','- 11:00~21:30 - Last order for lunch 15:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order for dinner 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Cockle Salad Bibimbap / Seafood Pancake / Gyeongju Yukhoe Mulhoe / Gyeongju Yukhoe Bibimbap, etc.','Not available',NULL,NULL),(945,243,'en','Nulbom Tteokgalbi Ssambap','Nulbom Tteokgalbi Ssambap is a ssambap specialty restaurant with over 20 years of history. To provide healthy and differentiated food, they make their own soybean paste from scratch. It is located about 3.3 km from Bulguksa Station. The signature menu is the woong-ryong pot rice set. Other offerings include beef bulgogi woong-ryong ssambap and stir-fried pork woong-ryong ssambap. All menu items are available for takeout. The restaurant has group seating and reservations are possible. Nearby, there are many famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including the UNESCO World Heritage Site Seokguram Grotto, Bulguksa Temple, and Cheomseongdae.','107 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','09:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Woong-ryong pot rice set / Woong-ryong (beef bulgogi) / Woong-ryong (Korean beef tteokgalbi) / Woong-ryong (stir-fried pork), etc.','Available','Every Thursday',NULL),(946,180,'en','Jinsuseongchan','Jinsuseongchan is located inside Gyochon Hanok Village. The signature dish is marinated crab in soy sauce with female blue crabs. In addition, you can taste Jinsuseongchan set meal, green onion bulgogi set meal, and beef tartare bibimbap. Meals can be enjoyed in private rooms and outdoor tables. Pets are allowed, but a leash is mandatory. You must also bring plastic bags for waste disposal. There are many famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju nearby, such as Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and the National Gyeongju Museum.','39-9 Gyochon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Gyodong)','- 10:30~21:00 - Weekday preparation time 16:00~17:30 - Weekend preparation time 15:30~16:30 - Last order 19:50',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Marinated crab in soy sauce / Traditional abalone rib stew / Beef tartare bibimbap / Bulgogi bibimbap etc.','Not available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(947,244,'en','Dosol Village','Dosol Village is a Korean restaurant located near Daereungwon in Gyeongju, featuring a 140-year-old hanok. The signature menu includes chicken stew, cheonggukjang, and muk salad, served as the Surisan set. Other offerings include assorted pancakes, old-style bulgogi, and green onion pancakes. The restaurant has group seating and private rooms, making it a great place for various gatherings. Nearby tourist attractions include Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and the National Gyeongju Museum.','8-13 Sonhyoja-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','- 11:00~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Surisan set / Assorted pancakes / Green onion pancakes / Tteokgalbi / Spicy stingray salad, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday to Wednesday',NULL),(948,238,'en','Yeongyang Charcoal Grilled Ribs Gyeongju Branch','Yeongyang Charcoal Grilled Ribs Gyeongju Branch is a specialty restaurant for Korean beef charcoal grilling that has been in operation for nearly 50 years. It is a place where Korean beef, aged for 12 hours in low-temperature refrigeration, is grilled. The marinated grilled beef rib meat, which is mixed with the seasoning sauce and served immediately upon order, is a delicacy. Various cuts of Korean beef, such as rib meat and skirt steak, can be enjoyed as marinated or salt-grilled dishes.','79 Bonghwang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Seobudong)','[Weekdays] - 10:30~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 20:30 [Weekends] - 10:30~21:30 - Last order 21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Marinated Korean beef rib meat / Marinated Korean skirt steak / Salt-grilled Korean beef rib meat / Yukhoe / Cold noodles, etc.','Available','Lunar New Year and Chuseok holidays',NULL),(949,181,'en','Gungnim Clam Kalguksu','Gungnim Clam Kalguksu is located about 4 km from Bulguksa Station. The signature dish is clam kalguksu (noodle soup). Fresh clams brought from Gochang, Jeonbuk, and chopped chives are mixed with aged kalguksu noodles, creating a cool and savory dish. In addition, you can taste bossam (boiled pork), tofu, seafood pancakes, etc. It is common to eat bossam with clam kalguksu. All menus are available for takeout. The restaurant has group seating and reservations are possible. Nearby are famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including the UNESCO World Heritage Site Seokguram, Bulguksa, and Cheomseongdae.','193 Saegol-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','11:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Clam kalguksu / Shitake mushroom bossam / Seafood pancake / Cold kalguksu etc.','Available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(950,182,'en','Dolphin Sashimi Restaurant','Dolphin Sashimi Restaurant is located near Najung Port. You can view the sea in front of Gampo from inside the restaurant. The signature dish is premium Gampo mulhoe (cold raw fish soup). In addition, you can taste spicy soup, sashimi, and sashimi rice. Some menus are available for takeout. Various mulhoe dishes are famous, and the sashimi rice is generously filled with live fish, flying fish roe, and vegetables, making it a popular menu item along with abalone porridge. You can enjoy your meal while appreciating the ocean view. Najung Fine Sand Beach is close to the restaurant, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','1888-10 Donghaean-ro, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~21:00 (Preparation time 15:00~16:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Premium Gampo mulhoe / Pohang-style bibim mulhoe / Haechun mulhoe / Sashimi rice etc.','Available','Every Monday (However, if Monday is a substitute holiday or legal holiday, it will be closed the next day)',NULL),(951,1205,'en','Bomun Garden','Located in Gyeongju, North Gyeongsang Province, Bomun Garden specializes in meat dishes. The signature menu is Hanwoo Galbitang (beef rib soup). Other dishes include Tteokgalbi Set, Spicy Beef Short Ribs, and Seafood Soft Tofu. The restaurant has group seating available and reservations can be made. Nearby attractions include Donggungwon, Gyeongju Bomun Tourist Complex, Cheomseongdae, and the National Gyeongju Museum, making it a popular spot for tourists.','142-3 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bomun-dong)','Weekdays 10:20~20:30 (Break time 15:20~17:00 / Lunch last order 14:40 / Dinner last order 19:40) Weekends 10:00~20:30 (Break time 15:30~17:00 / Lunch last order 14:40 / Dinner last order 19:40)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hanwoo Galbitang / Spicy Beef Short Ribs / Pork Ribs Stew / Spicy Pork Ribs Stew / Hanwoo Handmade Tteokgalbi / Hanwoo Mulhoe, etc.','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(952,127,'en','Pension 600 Camping Site','Pension 600 is located in Dongbang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It takes about 15 minutes to reach by car, approximately 6 km from Gyeongju City Hall. This camping site is surrounded by forests, allowing you to experience nature as it is. Additionally, it has various facilities such as a cafe, seminar room, swimming pool, karaoke room, foot volleyball court, and billiard room, providing plenty of entertainment beyond camping. The camping site has 7 caravans, 4 of which are large and 3 are small. The rooms are equipped with beds, sofas, tables, air conditioning, sinks, cooking utensils, tableware, toilets, and shower rooms. The outdoor private deck has barbecue facilities under an awning to protect against wind and rain. Nearby are many representative tourist attractions of Gyeongju, such as Bohum Tourist Complex, Cheomseongdae, and Hwangnyongsa. There are also many restaurants nearby, making it great for food lovers.','61, Janggol-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Dongbang-dong)',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(953,173,'en','Kongi-rang','The signature menu of Kongi-rang is Kongi-rang Jeongsik. It can be ordered for two or more people, and each person can choose their preferred stew. The stews available are old-style sundubu, kimchi sundubu, cheonggukjang sundubu, and biji jjigae, totaling four types. When individuals select their stews, they are served with gochujang bulgogi, wrapping vegetables, and 15 side dishes. Additionally, you can enjoy hwangtae gui jeongsik and donkatsu. Nearby is the UNESCO World Heritage site Seokguram, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','97 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','- Weekdays 10:00~20:00 - Weekends 08:00~21:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Kongi-rang Jeongsik / Hwangtae gui jeongsik / Donkatsu / Assorted jeon, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(954,126,'en','Gyeongju Chou Auto Camping Site','Gyeongju Chou Auto Camping Site is located near downtown Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Exit the Gyeongbu Expressway at Gyeongju IC, pass through the Gyeongju Museum intersection, and take National Route 7 towards Ulsan, where you will see the entrance stone of \'Cheonsun Temple\'. Turn right there and enter the farm road (embankment road) to find a large tiled house. This site also operates a mugwort farm and is popular among foreigners as a guesthouse. It has 41 auto camping sites divided into areas A, B, and C. Its greatest advantage is its optimal location for exploring Gyeongju\'s famous tourist attractions. Therefore, it attracts many visitors for both tourism and camping. Nearby are famous attractions such as Gyeongju Museum, Anapji, Bulguksa, and Bohum Tourist Complex, making it easy to plan combined tours. There are no restaurants nearby, but various eateries are operating around Anapji and Bohum Tourist Complex.','3549-30, Industrial Road, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Dongbang-dong)',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(955,1035,'en','Oasis Glamping','Gyeongju Oasis Glamping is located in a refreshing forest in Gujeong-dong, Gyeongju. It feels like a fortress. The camping ground offers glamping and caravan options. Inside the rooms, there are beds, air conditioning, refrigerators, microwaves, tables, heating devices, and electric kettles. Nearby, there are many jewel-like tourist attractions in Gyeongju, such as Tohamsan, Seokguram, Bulguksa, and Bomun Tourist Complex, making it great for sightseeing.','85-17 Saegol-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Gujeong-dong)','- Check-in 15:00- Check-out 11:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(956,123,'en','Cheongseokdeul Auto Camping','Cheongseokdeul Auto Camping is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 40 km from Gyeongju City Hall and is a space where clear valleys and dense forests coexist. Many visitors come during the vacation season to enjoy valley water activities and forest experiences. The camping site has 27 auto camping spots, of which 25 are gravel and the rest are decked. Personal trailers and caravans are also allowed.','176-9 Daehyeon-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(957,75,'en','Samneung Forest','Samneung Forest is a pine forest located west of Namsan in Gyeongju, where the three royal tombs are situated, harmoniously surrounded by beautiful trees. Namsan in Gyeongju refers to both Geumosan in the north and Gowi Mountain in the south, serving as a sacred site where the ancient kingdom of Silla discussed important national affairs, and it is a spiritual space of Silla and Gyeongju, rich in cultural heritage such as early palaces, royal tombs, and Buddhist sculptures. It is also the literary hometown where Kim Si-seup stayed in the Geumosan area of Namsan and engaged in various literary activities, including the first novel of Korea, Geumosan Myth. Gyeongju is a historical city that holds various historical forests, making it a famous location for photographers. The sunlight filtering through the winding pine trees is truly magical, and the azaleas blooming between the pines in spring are one of the beautiful sights.','Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(958,1030,'en','Wolgyesu Camping Site','Wolgyesu Auto Camping Site is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, where you can enjoy leisurely camping in nature surrounded by dense forests and valleys. In summer, it is popular among family campers as you can enjoy water activities in the valley. The campsite has crushed stone and deck sites, allowing you to choose a space that suits your preferences, and you can relax comfortably in a pleasant environment surrounded by forests. Personal trailers and caravans are allowed, and it is also a plus that you can camp with small pets. The management office offers rentals for camping equipment such as reels and fire pits, making it more convenient to use. It is a great camping site in Gyeongju to enjoy healing in the natural scenery created by clear valleys and forests.','758 Munbok-ro, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 13:00 - Check-out 12:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(959,122,'en','Ogle Ogle Auto Camping Site','Ogle Ogle Glamping is located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 33 km from Gyeongju City Hall. You can reach it by driving along Yongdam-ro, Geonpo Industrial Road, and Dansuk Road. The journey takes about 40 minutes. The site is situated at an elevation of 250m, providing stunning views below. If you are lucky, you can enjoy the mist covering the mountains. At night, the lights from the pension village below create a beautiful scene. The camping site has 11 glamping units, each equipped with beds, bathrooms, showers, and fans, while the outdoor space includes a sink, cooking utensils, dishes, a refrigerator, a camping table with chairs, a hammock, and barbecue equipment. The camping site operates year-round, and reservations can be made online in real-time. Nearby is the Gyeongju National Park Dansuk Mountain area, and about 30 minutes by car is the Bomun Tourist Complex, making it easy to connect for tourism. There are also many restaurants around the tourist area.','1637-32 Munbok-ro, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(960,853,'en','Geoncheon Cypress Forest','In Gyeongju Geoncheon, there is a forest where you can fully experience and feel phytoncides. This is the Geoncheon Cypress Forest located at the foot of Dongseoksan Mountain in Songseon-ri. Here, cypress trees stretch out their trunks generously. A 500m long walking path made of decking is installed among the cypress trees. There are also pavilions set up in various places, making it a nice spot to take a break.','535-2 Songseon-ri, Geoncheon-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(961,876,'en','Mujangsan','There is a mountain where King Munmu is said to have buried weapons and helmets after completing the unification of the Three Kingdoms. This mountain, known as Dongdaebongsan, is located next to Hamwolsan and Tohamsan, and is referred to as Mujangbong. It takes about 15 minutes by car from the Bomun Tourist Complex to reach the entrance of the Mujangsan hiking trail in Amgok Village. This rural village, famous for its water parsley, becomes crowded with hikers in the autumn. The wide grassland at the summit of Mujangsan attracts crowds wanting to see the cluster of silver grass. This area was a pasture until the 1980s, and after the pasture closed, silver grass began to grow naturally, forming a cluster. The beautiful scenery has gained popularity, becoming a backdrop for dramas and movies, further increasing its fame.','Amgok-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00 ※ Comply with national park visiting hours',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(962,799,'en','Jeonchon Yonggul','Jeonchon Yonggul, a natural sculpture created by waves and time, is a marine erosion cave located near Jeonchon Port in Gampo, Gyeongju. There are two caves, Saryonggul and Danyonggul, which, as the names suggest, contain legends about dragons. It is said that four dragons lived in Saryonggul, guarding the four cardinal directions, while one dragon lived in Danyonggul, protecting the village of Gampo. The two caves, which show passages that dragons might have used, are points along the Gampo Kkakji Walking Trail, which is part of the storytelling walking path in Gampo-eup, and can be encountered while walking along the Haepalang Trail, section 11 of the East Coast trekking course. Until recently, it was a military operation area and not open to the public, but with the development of the Haepalang Trail, a wooden deck walking path has been created along the coast, making it easy to reach Saryonggul.','39 Jangjin-gil, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (Approximately 100 small vehicles)','Open year-round',NULL),(963,110,'en','Wolsung Nuclear Power Promotion Center','Located in Gyeongju, the Wolsung Nuclear Power Promotion Center is a space where you can learn in-depth about energy and nuclear power, which are always around us but not well understood. It exhibits various topics, including the history of energy, the principles of electric energy generation, the process of nuclear power generation, and the mysterious world of radiation. In particular, it is rich in exhibits, video materials, and interactive games designed for children and teenagers to understand easily and enjoyably, making it highly educational. This promotion center is very suitable for field trips or family visits, stimulating curiosity about science and instilling a correct understanding of energy.','671 Donghaean-ro, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 09:00~17:00 - Saturdays 10:00~17:00','Free','2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Every Sunday / Legal holidays',NULL),(964,154,'en','Suhyup Live Fish Direct Sales Center','Suhyup Live Fish Direct Sales Center is located in Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is adjacent to Gampo Port, where you can purchase fresh seafood. The first floor of the direct sales center sells live fish and various seafood such as snow crabs. The second floor is a restaurant where you can eat sashimi purchased on the first floor after paying a set-up fee. Nearby are Oryu Goara Beach, Jeonchon Solbat Beach, and Najung Fine Sand Beach.','91 Gampo Port Road, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Varies by store',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Varies by store',NULL),(965,121,'en','Tohamsan Rock Glamping','Tohamsan Rock Glamping is located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, on Bobul-ro. It is about a 5-minute drive from Bulguksa and Bomun Resort, with a wide view of the Hadong Reservoir right below. Guests can use both pension and glamping facilities, with amenities including an outdoor swimming pool, barbecue area, and basketball court. There is no convenience store within the glamping site, so it is advisable to purchase necessary items at a medium-sized mart located 10 minutes away by car.','190-17 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','- Check-in 15:00 - Check-out 11:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(966,153,'en','Gampo Public Market','Gampo Public Market is located in Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. An oil market is held on the 3rd and 8th of every month. Visiting the market on market days allows you to find fresh seafood caught in front of Gampo and a variety of dried seafood. Notably, you can purchase Gampo\'s specialty, the flatfish, and seaweed at affordable prices. The bus stop in front of Gampo Public Market has city buses to Gyeongju and intercity buses to Ulsan.','115 Gampo-ro, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Varies by store',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Varies by store',NULL),(967,49,'en','Gyeongju Eupseong','Gyeongju Eupseong, a major cultural heritage symbolizing a millennium of Gyeongju after the Silla period, is located in the center of Gyeongju city. While the center was Wolsung during the Silla period, it shifted to Gyeongju Eupseong after the Goryeo period. It was the heart of Gyeongju where administrative, residential, and military functions gathered until the Goryeo and Joseon periods. It was first constructed during the Goryeo period and has been recorded to have been repaired several times during the Joseon period, with the current restored appearance dating back to the 21st year of King Yeongjo (1745). The restored Gyeongju Eupseong has a circumference of 2.3 km, and there were four main gates leading into the fortress from the east, west, south, and north. All four gates have been lost, but the eastern gate, Hyangilmun, has recently been restored. The remaining section of the wall, about 100 meters to the east, has been rebuilt, and the fortifications, watchtower, and eastern gate have been restored and opened to the public in November 2018.','31 Dongmun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukbu-dong)','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(968,871,'en','Naa Beach','Naa Beach is located in Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The beach is a mix of pebbles and sand. Many people enjoy fishing here. Especially, the pine forest allows free tent setup, making it a popular spot for camping. Cooking is prohibited, but many visit for car picnics and car camping. Nearby are Nasandeul Park and the Tomb of King Munmu of Silla.','17-1 Naa 4-gil, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(969,81,'en','Jeonchon Port','Jeonchon Port was designated as a fishing village tourism complex by the government in 2004 and began to transform into a tourist port. In 2009, a remodeling project was carried out, equipping it with a parking lot, plaza, floor fountain, pergola, pavilion, wooden deck promenade, and an observatory. In particular, the view of the peaceful harbor from the Jeonchon Port observatory is impressive. Night landscape lighting has also been installed on the breakwater, making it beautifully illuminated at night. The horse sculpture at the entrance of Jeonchon Port, known as Geomasaeng, is also a sight to see. There are many stories related to horses in the Jeonchon Port area. There is a village called Geomajang near Jeonchon Port, which is said to be named Geomasan because the northern mountain range of Jeonchon Port resembles a lying horse. Additionally, during the Silla period, it is said that soldiers were stationed here to prevent invasions by Japanese pirates, which is where the name Geomajang for the nearby village originated.','1245-11 Jeonchon-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(970,847,'en','Gyeongju Pink Muhly (Gyeongju Pink Muhly Habitat)','The Gyeongju Pink Muhly habitat can be found around Cheomseongdae. Every autumn, the area around Cheomseongdae blooms in pink. Since 2017, the city of Gyeongju has been developing the pink muhly habitat for tourism content. Thanks to the unique color of the cultural heritage and pink muhly, it has become very popular for landscaping as a tourist attraction. You can take beautiful landscape photos with the fully bloomed pink muhly and Cheomseongdae together.','839-1 Inwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, Cheomseongdae area','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(971,860,'en','Heungmu Road Cherry Blossom Path','The Heungmu Road Cherry Blossom Path can be found by crossing the Seocheon Bridge from Gyeongju Terminal and turning right at the first intersection. This place was selected as one of the \'100 Beautiful Roads in Korea\' by the Ministry of Construction and Transportation in 2007. The reason for its selection as a beautiful road will be naturally understood if you visit Heungmu Road in spring. The cherry trees on both sides of the road touch each other, creating a beautiful cherry blossom tunnel that shades the sky. During the spring when the cherry blossoms are in full bloom, the road becomes a parking lot for numerous visitors, so traveling by bicycle or on foot may be faster than by car. In summer, it is a green path, and in autumn, it is beautiful with fall foliage.','Chunghyo-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(972,111,'en','TtoBot Junk Art Museum','The TtoBot Junk Art Museum is located in the Jangbogo Hall within the Gyeongju Expo Park. The museum is modeled after the transforming car TtoBot, allowing children to easily understand and experience junk art and art trick art. It is a great place to visit with children as you can see giant TtoBots up close. Activities such as badge making, boxing robot experiences, and robot car experiences are also available. Nearby, there are Blue One Dianas CC and Gyeongju Blue One Blue Sky Glamping, making it a good place for combined visits.','614 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~17:00 (Last admission 16:00)','※ For details, please inquire by phone','2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(973,848,'en','Heungmu Park','Heungmu Park is named after General Kim Yu-sin, who was posthumously honored as Heungmu Daewang. The road leading to General Kim Yu-sin\'s tomb is called Heungmu Road. The park is not large, but it has a wide lawn and trees providing shade, making it a popular resting place for Gyeongju citizens. The walking paths are well-maintained, making it a great place for healing.','9-2 Chung-hyo-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(974,846,'en','Geumjangdae','In Gyeongju, there is a story about \'Samgipalgae,\' which refers to three rare treasures and eight strange phenomena. Among the eight strange phenomena, \'Geumjangnak-an\' refers to the scenery viewed from Geumjangdae, where the Seocheon and Bukcheon meet, which was so beautiful that even geese stopped to rest. Geumjangdae boasts stunning views and scenery. It was reopened to the public in 2012 after reconstruction. The pavilion is equipped with night landscape lighting, and from the pavilion, you can see the night view of the Hyeongsan River and the city of Gyeongju at a glance.','San 38-9 Seokjang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','06:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(975,78,'en','Gyeongju Jinpyeong Wangneung','Gyeongju Jinpyeong Wangneung is the tomb of Jinpyeong Wang, the 26th king of Silla (reigned 579-632). Jinpyeong Wang established a new central government office to solidify his independent royal authority. He also effectively repelled invasions from Baekje and Goguryeo through diplomatic relations with the Sui and Tang dynasties of China and worked on the restoration of Gyeongju Myeonghwal Fortress for the defense of the capital. It is a round earthen mound tomb, 7.9m high and 36.4m in diameter. The base of the tomb is surrounded by natural stones, but only a few remain today. Given its size, it is clearly a royal tomb and is characterized by its location in the middle of a plain.','608, Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(976,849,'en','Dongchangcheon Cheongnyong Waterfall (Cheongnyong Artificial Waterfall)','Dongchangcheon Cheongnyong Waterfall is an artificial waterfall located in the Dongchangcheon valley. It is surrounded by mountains in a clean area. In summer, water flows refreshingly from the top of the cliff behind the river. This place is a popular site for campers. During the summer peak season, finding a spot is as difficult as picking stars from the sky. Additionally, many family travelers come here for water play in the summer. To ensure safe water play, lifeguards are stationed during the peak season.','Wae-chil-ri, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(977,41,'en','Gangdong Resort Private Condo','Gangdong Resort is a comprehensive year-round leisure resort located in Gyeongju, offering a golf course, condominium, and water park. The concept of the Gangdong Resort Private Condo is a castle on a hill. It has been designed to blend elegantly with the diverse nature while considering modern spatial aesthetics. Above all, it has been carefully crafted to be a space for peaceful relaxation without disturbance. The resort features materials such as the Moai statues from East Island, sculptures from Seokguram, the Topkapi Palace in Istanbul, and the Chambord Castle in France. The grandeur of the overall exterior gives a sense of deepening tradition and shining honor over time.','391, Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(978,828,'en','Korad Clean Nuri Park Koradium','Korad Clean Nuri Park Koradium is located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Koradium features an exhibition hall where visitors can gain correct information and knowledge about the radioactive waste disposal site and management projects, as well as a resting area indoors. There is also an observation deck that offers a panoramic view of the East Sea and the tomb of King Munmu. This theme park, where nature and science are harmonized, provides a leisure culture space for visitors\' relaxation and small events, along with walking paths and experiential learning areas suitable for the whole family. The parking lot is equipped with eco-friendly solar facilities for lighting, and an outdoor stage for learning and performances for local residents is also provided.','1249 Donghaean-ro, Munmudaewang-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:30~17:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Every Saturday, Sunday / Legal holidays',NULL),(979,115,'en','Kidult Museum','The term \'Kidult\' is a combination of \'Kid\' and \'Adult\', referring to adults who possess the pure emotions and tastes of children, making it a family-friendly space. It is the largest Kidult museum in Gyeongbuk and represents the Bomun area in Gyeongju. Visitors can explore various exhibits showcasing modern life, including the world\'s first projector, a candle projector, Edison’s phonograph, and radios from the 60s to 80s. There are over 50,000 diverse exhibits and character figures, ranging from childhood movie and cartoon characters like Gundam, Star Wars, and Taekwon V to popular Marvel characters.','132-16 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','10:00~18:30 (Last admission 18:00)','- Adults 9,000 KRW - Youth (middle and high school students) 8,500 KRW - Children (36 months to 6th grade) 8,000 KRW','2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available (approximately 200 small cars)','Open year-round',NULL),(980,1037,'en','Car Going on Two Wheels','Car Going on Two Wheels is a glamping site located on the outskirts of Gyeongju. There are a total of 17 cabanas in different styles: Hangul, Cube, and VIP. The interiors are equipped with air conditioning and heating facilities, and particularly feature individual jjimjilbang (Korean sauna) rooms. The swimming pool can be used like an indoor pool with heated water and is quite large. ATV, three-wheeled electric motorcycles, bumper cars for toddlers, and bicycles are available for free, and there are also VR game experience facilities and karaoke, making it a place rich in activities to enjoy within the camping site.','278-182 Oechililbu-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 15:00 - Check-out 11:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(981,1002,'en','Hwangnyongsa History and Culture Center','Located in GuHwang-dong, Gyeongju, the Hwangnyongsa History and Culture Center is an exhibition hall built right next to Hwangnyongsa Site. It aims to shed new light on the historical significance of Hwangnyongsa and embodies the desire for its restoration, established to share the research and excavation results of Hwangnyongsa Site with the public. It allows visitors to experience the grandeur of the Silla-era national temple by reproducing and exhibiting artifacts excavated from Hwangnyongsa Site. Inside, there is a 3D audiovisual room that captures the process from the establishment to the destruction of Hwangnyongsa, and a Silla history exhibition room displaying artifacts unearthed during the excavation process. On the first floor, there is also a model tower reproducing the 9-story wooden pagoda of Hwangnyongsa at a scale of 1/10. Next to the model tower exhibition room, there is a lobby café overlooking the Hwangnyongsa Site.','64-19 Imhae-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (GuHwang-dong)','Weekdays: 09:00–18:00. Weekends and public holidays: April–October 09:00–19:00; November–March 09:00–18:00. Last admission is 30 minutes before closing.','[Individual] - Adult 3,000 won - Military personnel and middle/high school students 2,000 won - Children 1,500 won [Group] - Adult 2,000 won - Military personnel and middle/high school students 1,500 won - Children 1,000 won ※ Free: Under 6 years old / Over 65 years old','2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:29:04',NULL,NULL,'Closed January 1 and on the days of Lunar New Year and Chuseok.',NULL),(982,150,'en','Sky Glamping','Located at the foot of Mount Toham, this glamping site has a total of 18 cabana tents, each with one room and a deck terrace. It is equipped with two queen-size beds, bedding, a refrigerator, a vanity, a mirror, a BBQ table and grill, air conditioning, and an electric mat. Facilities include a convenience store, restrooms, showers, a washbasin, and a swimming pool (summer). Pets are not allowed. It is not far from Gyeongju Bomun Complex, making it great for enjoying Gyeongju tourism during the day and for accommodation, with an outdoor water play area suitable for children.','328-10 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(983,151,'en','Adelia','Located in the Gyeongju Bomun Complex, this glamping site offers a spacious and green lawn garden for healing in nature. It also has various facilities such as a water slide swimming pool and kids\' theme areas, making it great for families and couples. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju World, Bulguksa Temple, Cheomseongdae, and Hwanglidangil, allowing you to enjoy famous tourist spots in Gyeongju.','14-13 Hadongbunjeobanjil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(984,120,'en','Sanrae Caravan Pension Sannae','Sanrae Caravan Pension Sannae is a caravan and pension located in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju. There are 6 caravans available, with options for American traditional style and Korean style. It features a valley and a separate outdoor swimming pool, making it great for summer water activities with children. The address is in Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, making it convenient for tourism in Gyeongju as well as nearby Cheongdo Unmunsan and Unmunsa. In spring, cherry blossoms bloom along the valley, and in autumn, the foliage is spectacular.','351 Daehyeon-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(985,131,'en','Eden Auto Camping Site','Eden Auto Camping Site is located in Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. You can enjoy a view of the blue sea from the camping site, where the sound of waves is like a song. In addition to camping, you can also use the pension. It has a swimming pool, playground, and water play facilities, making it great for enjoying summer with children. It is also convenient for enjoying famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju. Pets are not allowed.','2507-2, Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(986,1203,'en','Gosaekchangyeon','Gosaekchangyeon is a specialty restaurant for Korean beef grilled short ribs located near Bulguksa Temple. The traditional Korean house provides a serene atmosphere and spacious, comfortable indoor space, making it a great place to visit with family. The signature dish, handmade Korean beef grilled short ribs, uses domestic fresh meat, infused with a smoky flavor, and retains its juiciness, melting in your mouth with a deep flavor. Additionally, the spicy-sweet marinated pork belly is a popular dish that disappears quickly with a bowl of rice due to its chewy texture and umami flavor. The dried pollack soup and dried pollack soft tofu stew are clean and refreshing broth dishes that provide comfort and satisfaction even after the meal. All side dishes are served neatly, preserving the natural flavors of the ingredients without excessive seasoning.','58-4 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Madong)','10:00-20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Korean Beef Grilled Short Rib Set / Pork Grilled Short Rib Set / Mixed Grilled Short Rib Set / Pork Belly with Spicy Sauce, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(987,877,'en','Sambulsaji','Sambulsaji is located in Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The temple features the Daeungjeon, Sanshingak, and the treasure Gyeongju Baedong Stone Buddha Triad. The Gyeongju Baedong Stone Buddha Triad is believed to have been created during the Three Kingdoms period and was assembled in 1923 from stone statues and materials scattered at the foot of Namsan in Gyeongju.','692-25 Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, Sambulsaji','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(988,258,'en','Gyo-dong Ssam-bap','Gyo-dong Ssam-bap is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has appeared on the MBC program. The representative menu includes pork bulgogi ssam-bap, duck bulgogi ssam-bap, and Korean beef bulgogi ssam-bap. Additionally, it serves 6-buchon yukgaejang and gondalbi bibimbap. There are group seating arrangements inside, and reservations are also possible. Nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae and Daereungwon.','77 Cheomseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','11:00~21:00 (Break time 16:00~17:00 / Last order 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Gyo-dong Ssam-bap Set Menu (A, B, C)','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(989,1157,'en','Yangji Dabang','Yangji Dabang is a cafe with an old-fashioned Dabang concept located on Hwanglidangil. The cafe\'s interior, along with vintage items, exudes a strong retro vibe. A music box filled with LPs is one example. Tables are available both indoors and outdoors, allowing guests to enjoy drinks and desserts in various spaces. The representative menu includes Yangji Supener with Americano topped with Injeolmi cream and rice cake skewers, Yangji Cream Latte with Cafe Latte topped with Injeolmi cream and rice cake skewers, and sweet Dabang coffee with cream and sugar. Additionally, fluffy soufflé is a popular menu item here.','7-2 Sajeng-ro 57beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Yangji Supener / Strawberry Soufflé / Yangji Cream Latte / Scotch Cream Latte, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(990,260,'en','Tofu Village','Tofu Village is located in Madong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has appeared on the MBC current affairs program. The representative menu is the special spicy soft tofu set. Other offerings include spicy soft tofu set, perilla seed soft tofu set, white soft tofu set, cheonggukjang set, village tofu mushroom stew set, herbal bossam set, tofu steak, and seafood pancake.','168-3 Bulguk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Madong)','08:30 ~ 20:00 (Last order 19:00) Monday 08:30~16:00 (Last order 15:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Spicy Soft Tofu Set / Perilla Seed Soft Tofu Set / Village Tofu Mushroom Stew Set / Handmade Pork Cutlet, etc.','Available','Closed every Tuesday',NULL),(991,176,'en','Giwa Buckwheat Makguksu','Giwa Buckwheat Makguksu is located in GuHwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a representative makguksu specialty store near Hwanglidangil. The signature menu features mulmakguksu made with Hanwoo bone broth and over ten ingredients, and bibimmakguksu characterized by a sauce made with over ten ingredients and fruits. Additionally, gomguksu and boiled pork are available. The boiled pork is known for its tenderness, and the mulmakguksu is famous for its refreshing broth. The establishment is clean and has seating suitable for group visits. Nearby is Hwangnyongsa Stone Pagoda, making it easy for combined sightseeing.','91 Bunhwang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (GuHwang-dong)','- 11:00~20:00 - Preparation time 15:30~16:30 - Last order 19:30 ※ No preparation time on weekends',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mulmakguksu / Bibimmakguksu / Gomguksu / Boiled pork, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(992,263,'en','Matjarang','Matjarang is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The representative menu is the stone pot set meal, which includes beef bulgogi, grilled croaker, grilled flounder, various side dishes, and stews. Other offerings include glutinous barley Korean beef galbi set, Matjarang set, soft tofu set, and seafood pancake. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings, and reservations are possible. It has a large parking lot that can accommodate over 40 vehicles, allowing for a comfortable meal without parking worries.','329 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','09:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Stone Pot Set Meal / Glutinous Barley Korean Beef Galbi Set / Matjarang Set / Soft Tofu Set / Seafood Pancake','Available (40 vehicles) (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(993,152,'en','Sarabong CC','Sarabong CC is located in Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clubhouse is surrounded by 36 holes of course on both sides, providing a comfortable and wide view from the clubhouse. The holes, differentiated by 9-hole units, harmonize while maintaining their independence, allowing players to enjoy the best conditions. The course maximizes the use of natural terrain, enhancing the thrill of the game. The course utilizes the valley as it is and regenerates natural streams and ponds, creating holes that feel as if they are nestled in nature.','577-189 Naewae-ro, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','※ Varies depending on the golf course situation, please inquire by phone',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(994,40,'en','Seongho Resort','Seongho Resort is a condo-style resort located in Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features over 140 rooms and small and large banquet halls suitable for corporate meetings, seminars, and ceremonies. The rooms include family rooms, superior rooms, ambassador suites, deluxe suites, and royal suites. Facilities include banquet halls, an outdoor swimming pool, a horseback riding area, a fitness club, a restaurant, a convenience store, a café, a sauna, a karaoke room, and a barbecue area.','636, Yeongji-ro, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do',NULL,NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(995,1194,'en','Namjeong Everyday Meal Restaurant','Namjeong Everyday Meal Restaurant is a Korean restaurant popular for its stir-fried dishes. It has been remodeled from a charming home with a tiled roof, providing a comfortable atmosphere. The signature dishes are Stir-fried Octopus, Stir-fried Pork, and Stir-fried Jjamppong which includes both pork and octopus. It is served with over ten side dishes, and when you mix the stir-fried dishes with rice in a large bowl, it tastes like a homemade meal, which is why it is famous. Regular customers often refer to it simply as the Jjamppong restaurant due to the popularity of the Stir-fried Jjamppong.','3, Baeri 1-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Baedong)','09:00~20:00 (Last order 19:20)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Stir-fried Jjamppong / Stir-fried Octopus / Stir-fried Pork / Kimchi Stew, etc.','Available','Closed every Tuesday',NULL),(996,245,'en','Geumsanjae Kalguksu','Geumsanjae Kalguksu specializes in kalguksu and chive pancakes, located across a small tunnel famous as the Korean version of Spirited Away in Gyeongju. The clean broth and chewy noodles of kalguksu are known for their mild and slightly sweet taste. Just as famous as the kalguksu is the exterior scenery, featuring beautiful mountains and tranquil hanok. It is also recommended to take a walk along the nearby walking paths after the meal.','71 Heungmu-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Chunghyo-dong)','09:00~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Perilla seed kalguksu / Kalguksu / Chive pancakes / Boiled pork, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(997,79,'en','Bunhwangsa Cheongbori Field','Every spring, a fresh green barley field unfolds around Bunhwangsa in Gyeongju. Barley sown just after Chuseok provides a unique sight from early spring to early summer, and when viewed from the Bunhwangsa parking lot towards Hwangnyongsa, the deep green barley field stretches endlessly against the backdrop of the Hwangnyongsa History and Culture Center. The blue sky, warm sunlight, and the barley swaying in the spring breeze stir the hearts of onlookers. At sunset, the barley, tinted by the sunset, sparkles in golden light, adding to the charm of a thousand-year-old Gyeongju.','94-11, Bunhwang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(998,85,'en','Bomun Forest Food Village','Bomun Forest Village, located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, is a beautiful natural village surrounded by the majestic Myeonghwal Mountain and the vast Bomun Lakes. It is conveniently located near the Jinpyeong King Tomb, Bomun Temple Site, Myeonghwal Mountain Fortress, and the Silla Royal Capital Forest, making it easy for travelers to stop by. In particular, the embankment behind the Bomun Forest Village, which connects Myeonghwal Mountain Fortress to Jinpyeong King Tomb, is named \'Seondeok Queen Road\', and every spring, the double cherry blossoms bloom abundantly, making it a beloved hidden spring flower spot for locals. As you stroll along the path lined with pink double cherry blossoms, you will find benches and photo zones perfect for resting along the way. The Hanok Village visible from the surrounding trail is Bomun Forest Food Village. It offers a hearty meal with a variety of dishes including a generous set menu, charcoal-grilled ribs, spicy soup, roasted duck, soft tofu, and buckwheat noodles.','Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Varies by store',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Varies by store',NULL),(999,886,'en','Yukbujeon','Yukbujeon, formerly known as Yangsanjae, is a shrine that enshrines the tablets of the six village chiefs from the six divisions that existed in Silla before its founding and holds rituals in their honor. In 57 BC, the six village chiefs from Alcheong Yangsan Village, Dolsan Goheo Village, Chuisan Jinji Village, Musan Daesu Village, Geumsan Gari Village, and Myeonghwal Mountain Goya Village gathered on Alcheong Hill to elect Park Hyeokgeose, born from an egg, as the first king of Silla. Subsequently, the third king of Silla, King Yuri, honored their contributions to the founding of the nation by bestowing surnames: Yi for Yangsan Village, Choi for Goheo Village, Jeong for Jinji Village, Son for Daesu Village, Bae for Gari Village, and Seol for Goya Village, thus becoming the progenitors of these surnames. Yukbujeon is arranged with Yunjukdang on the east side and Ikikjae on the west side, passing through the outer gate, Daedeokmun, followed by the inner gate, Hongikmun. Inside Hongikmun stands the main building, Ipdeokmyo, which is not open to the public except on ritual days.','37-10 Namgan-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1000,48,'en','Silla Royal Capital Forest','To prevent flooding in the river area of the royal capital during the Silla Dynasty, a forest called \'Orisu\' was created from Gyeongju Myeonghwal Mountain Fortress to Bunhwangsa Temple, spanning 5 ri, or 2 km. The Silla Royal Capital Forest, located at the entrance of the Bomun Tourist Complex, is a recreation of that Orisu forest. The Silla Royal Capital Forest holds the history of flood control projects from the Silla period. Designed as a forest where the kings of Silla walked 1,500 years ago, it was opened to the public in 2007 during the World Cultural Expo. There is a first phase of the royal capital forest created towards Guhwanggyo, and a second phase of the forest towards the Forest Head Food Village. Thanks to the wide lawn and green tree-lined paths, it is also popular as a place to enjoy a leisurely picnic. It is conveniently located near major tourist attractions, making it a great resting spot for both citizens and tourists.','885-6 Guhwang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1001,1182,'en','Sangalrae Dakgalbi Main Branch','Sangalrae Dakgalbi Main Branch is located in Seonggeon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The restaurant is large with many tables, so the waiting time is not long. The signature menu includes regular dakgalbi and spicy dakgalbi, both made with domestic chicken. The seasoning includes turmeric powder and curry, providing a unique taste, and the fried rice is a delicacy. All dishes are cooked in the kitchen and served ready to eat at the table, making it convenient. Nearby famous tourist attractions include Hwanglidangil, Daereungwon, Cheomseongdae, and Donggung and Wolji.','25 Geumseong-ro 395beon-gil, Seonggeon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~22:00 (Last order 21:10)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Dakgalbi / Spicy Dakgalbi','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1002,840,'en','Geumjangdae Waterfront Park','Geumjangdae, a towering rock by the Hyeongsan River in Gyeongju, has been known since ancient times as a place where geese stop to rest, hence the name Geumjangnak-an (金藏落雁). This place, which served as the backdrop for Kim Dong-ri\'s short story \'The Shaman\'s Daughter,\' features a pavilion with a tiled roof, making it a great spot to enjoy the old-fashioned atmosphere. The Geumjangdae Wetland Park, located at the entrance of Geumjangdae, was created to provide a space for visitors to observe and explore the flora and fauna of the Hyeongsan River by adding educational and experiential functions to the naturally formed wetland. The park has gained attention on social media due to its picturesque green scenery and a single abandoned wooden boat, making it a popular photo spot. Especially during cherry blossom season, couples dressed in tuxedos and dresses line up for wedding photos. From April to May, bright yellow canola flowers bloom, allowing visitors to enjoy the fresh spring days. The walking paths are well-equipped, making it easy for people of all ages to walk and enjoy.','1211-1 Seokjang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all the time',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1003,854,'en','Geumgoksa Temple (Gyeongju)','Geumgoksa Temple (金谷寺), located in Gyeongju, North Gyeongsang Province, was founded around 585 by the monk Won-gwang, who established the first secular precepts of the Great Vehicle Buddhism during the reign of King Jinpyeong of Silla. After being destroyed and looted by the Japanese during the Imjin War, the temple and its pagoda were lost. It is said that around 1935, the current abbot Cheongun\'s grandmother, who was foraging for herbs near the temple site, discovered the current location of Geumgoksa Temple by following the sound of a wooden fish. Since 2009, continuous restoration and management have shaped the current appearance of Geumgoksa Temple.','758 Duryu-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open year-round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1004,1854,'en','Dongbang Station','Dongbang Station is a train station located in Dongbang-dong, Gyeongju, situated between Bulguksa Station and Gyeongju Station on the Donghae-Nambu Line. It began operations in 1919 as an unmanned station and was referred to as a local station at that time, but it was renamed to its current name in 1927. Dongbang Station was upgraded to a regular station in 1951, but as the number of passengers continued to decline, it became an unmanned station again in 2005 and is currently used as a signal station, with no trains stopping there. It only briefly halts when two trains running on the single track of the Donghae Line pass each other in opposite directions. Dongbang Station, once a quiet minor station with few visitors, has started to gain attention again due to the orange-colored trumpet vine that fills the walls in summer. The vibrant trumpet vine in full bloom combined with the faded Dongbang Station sign creates a unique atmosphere.','3490-5 Sanup-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Dongbang-dong)','Open all the time',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1005,124,'en','Camp ING','Camp ING is located in Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is about 13 km away from Gyeongju City Hall. You can reach it by driving along Yangjeong-ro and Industrial Road. The travel time is approximately 20 minutes. This place has transformed an abandoned school in the forest into an emotional camping site. As you slowly explore the camping area starting from the entrance, you will find attractions that evoke old memories. There are 30 car camping sites, consisting of 28 gravel sites and 2 deck sites. The site size is 8m wide and 10m long for gravel, and 5m by 5m for the deck. Personal trailers and caravans are allowed. The management office rents out camping equipment such as reel lines, fire pits, and heating devices. Nearby attractions include Gyeongju Yangdong Village and Angye Reservoir, making it easy to plan a combined trip. There are also various restaurants nearby, including Chinese, Korean, and snack shops.','47, Homyeonggeun-gol-gil, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 14:00 - Check-out 13:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(1006,132,'en','Sannae Nature Camp','Sannae Nature Camp is located in Daehyeon-ri, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The camping site is surrounded by forests and has a valley, making it incredibly nature-friendly. It has 10 glamping units equipped with facilities for daily life, such as beds, toilets, shower rooms, sinks, and cooking utensils. There are also 4 auto camping sites made of gravel. Facilities include a swimming pool, trampoline, convenience store, and barbecue area, perfect for beating the summer heat. Nearby is Gyeongju National Park, and within a 30-minute drive, you can find famous tourist attractions like Cheomseongdae.','80-19, Daehyeondonggol-gil, Sannae-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Check-in 15:00 - Check-out 11:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(1007,1191,'en','Sanhae','Sanhae is a charcoal grill specialty restaurant located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The traditional Korean house style exterior and interior are eye-catching. The signature menu is grilled pork cooked over a charcoal fire. In addition, you can also enjoy dishes like soy sauce marinated crab, kimchi stew, and cheonggukjang.','130-5 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bomun-dong)','- 11:00~20:30- Preparation time 15:30~17:00- Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Charcoal Grilled Meat / Soy Sauce Marinated Crab / Cheonggukjang / Doenjang Stew, etc.','Available','Day before and on the day of Seollal and Chuseok',NULL),(1008,1193,'en','Daerung Galbi','Daerung Galbi is a meat restaurant where you can enjoy beef ribs at reasonable prices. The signature dishes are the female cow short ribs and marinated female cow short ribs. The marinated short ribs are available in limited quantities each day. If you want to try a variety, you can order the assorted female cow beef. Other options include female cow rib meat, boneless braised short ribs, and Yukhoe, as well as meal options like beef soup, king rib soup, Yukhoe Bibimbap, and Yukhoe Cold Noodles.','27, Poseok-ro 1068beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','[Weekdays] - 11:30~21:30 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 20:30 [Weekends] - 11:30~21:30 - Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Female Cow Short Ribs / Female Cow Rib Meat / Marinated Female Cow Short Ribs / Assorted Female Cow Beef, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1009,1192,'en','Cheongryong Mother-in-Law Korean Restaurant','Cheongryong Mother-in-Law Korean Restaurant is a Korean cuisine specialty restaurant located in Jinhyeon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The menu offers a variety of Korean dishes such as Bulgogi Jeongol, Tofu Mushroom Jeongol, Seafood Sundubu, Mother-in-Law Bibimbap, and Tteokgalbi. The Tofu Jeongol and Bulgogi Jeongol are particularly popular, and many people visit for the generous servings. The interior is not very large but provides a cozy atmosphere for comfortable dining. Nearby is Bulguksa Temple, making it a popular spot for tourists. It is known as a must-visit restaurant for Bulguksa.','55, Jinhyeon-ro 2-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Jinhyeon-dong)','08:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Tteokgalbi Set / Seafood Sundubu / Mother-in-Law Bibimbap / Stone Pot Bibimbap, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1010,1183,'en','Notjeon Guksu','Notjeon Guksu is a noodle shop located in a quiet rural area. Noodles are cooked immediately after ordering, so there may be a short wait, but they are served in rustic bowls topped with kimchi, seaweed flakes, zucchini, and seasoning sauce, with a pleasant anchovy broth aroma. It may look shabby, but it is an old favorite.','55-8 Cheomseong-ro, Sajeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Janchi Guksu / Bibim Guksu / Hoe Guksu / Pajeon / Chive Jeon, etc.',NULL,'Every Tuesday',NULL),(1011,1184,'en','Eun-Ah Hwae Town','Located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, Eun-Ah Hwae Town offers fresh seafood caught directly from Eun-Ah 1 and 2. You can enjoy a variety of menus including fresh sashimi, mulhoe, sashimi rice bowl, abalone porridge, grilled rockfish, spicy soup, and seaweed soup. You can dine while looking closely at the sea, and there is ample parking space available for group use. Additionally, affordable lodging is available.','12-40 Daemidgil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Assorted sashimi / Abalone porridge / Spicy soup / Mulhoe, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1012,1190,'en','Sobakage','Sobakage is a specialized shop for Mazesoba located in Hwanglidangil, Gyeongju. Mazesoba is a combination of \'maze\' meaning \'to mix\' and \'soba\' meaning \'noodle\'. It features various food ingredients neatly arranged on top of the noodles, reminiscent of bibimbap in Korea. Based on Nagoya-style Mazesoba, they carefully prepare a variety of dishes such as Abura Soba, Basil Soba, and Mapo Soba, with chewy noodles and rich sauces. It is a popular dining spot for lunch or dinner during your trip to Gyeongju, suitable for solo dining or meals with friends and loved ones.','25-5 Cheomseong-ro 99beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','- 11:00~21:00- Preparation time 15:30~17:00- Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Nagoya Mazesoba / Doniku Mazesoba / Abura Soba / Midori Soba, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1013,1189,'en','Hiknic','A white-toned cafe located on the way to Hwanglidangil from the bus terminal. Lettering cakes can also be ordered. The interior of the cafe is clean and stylishly decorated, with photo spots scattered throughout. The combination of taste, interior, and service allows for a satisfying time.','738-2 Taejong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 11:00~19:00- Weekends 10:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hiknic French Toast / Crème Brûlée Latte / Cream Latte / Black Cream Latte / Black Latte, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1014,1202,'en','Mano Restaurant','Located in Hwangseong-dong, Gyeongju, Mano Restaurant is a cost-effective Western cuisine restaurant. The interior features soft lighting and an antique atmosphere, making it a great place for family dining, friend gatherings, and dates. The menu includes a variety of dishes such as tenderloin steak, sirloin steak, mentaiko cream pasta, bacon shrimp pilaf, gorgonzola pizza, seafood stew pasta, and also offers course meals. In particular, the mentaiko cream pasta is moderately spicy and has an excellent umami flavor, making it a must-try dish. There is also a private space that can accommodate about 8 people, making it suitable for group gatherings.','61-21 Hwangseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangseong-dong)','- 11:40-22:00 - Preparation time 15:00-17:00 - Last order 21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mano Course / Special Course / Korean Beef Tenderloin Steak / Pasta, etc.','Available','Closed on the first Sunday of every month',NULL),(1015,1185,'en','Onu-i','Onu-i Cafe, located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, is a cafe operated by actual siblings. The interior features a harmonious blend of rich wood tones and white tones, creating a pleasant atmosphere. There are fewer than 10 tables, and there is also a room-style space inside. The restroom is unisex but spacious and clean, equipped with women\'s products. In addition to signature menu items unique to Onu-i, coffee, tea, and beverages, a variety of cakes and desserts are also available.','59 Baekryul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Dongcheon-dong)','08:00~17:30 (Last order 17:25)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Onu-i cream latte / Onu-i aged latte / Onu-i rice cake powder / Onu-i Gyeongju bread, etc.',NULL,'Every Saturday and Sunday',NULL),(1016,1186,'en','Oscar\'s Cafe','Oscar\'s Cafe, located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, is a cafe remodeled from a house, providing a cozy, quiet, and comfortable atmosphere. It creates delicious desserts and cakes using butter and animal cream without margarine and shortening. Cakes and beverages may vary seasonally to enjoy seasonal fruits. You can also taste unique menu items with Oscar\'s personality, along with fragrant coffee, tea, and drinks.','13-4 Yongdam-ro 104beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangseong-dong)','11:00~21:30 (Last order 21:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Rare cheesecake / Berry gateau chocolat / Lemon meringue cake / Americano / Cafe latte, etc.','Not available','Every Monday',NULL),(1017,1201,'en','Gyeongchunjae','Gyeongchunjae is a bibimbap specialty restaurant located near Bulguksa Temple in Gyeongju. It is a popular restaurant that satisfies many customers\' tastes with neat Korean dishes made from fresh ingredients and appropriate seasoning.','61-7 Jinhyeon-ro 2-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Jinhyeon-dong)','08:00-16:00 (Last order 15:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seafood Stone Pot Bibimbap / Cockle Bibimbap / Chive Bibimbap / Grilled Mackerel, etc.','Available','Closed every Tuesday',NULL),(1018,239,'en','Yellow','Yellow is a cafe located in Cheongun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It harmonizes traditional Korean architecture with modern buildings, allowing guests to enjoy drinks while overlooking Bomun Lake. Due to the many stairs and glass railings in the cafe, children under 14 are not allowed inside for safety reasons. The signature menu is slow coffee, and other offerings include banana pudding, ssukssukpener, Americano, homemade vanilla bean latte, and einspänner. The nearby Bomun Tourist Complex makes it easy to plan a connected trip.','375-16 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~22:00 (Last order 21:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Slow coffee / Blueberry pudding / Walnut cream cheese wrapped in dried persimmon / Banana pudding, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1019,236,'en','Aden','Cafe Aden is a bakery hanok cafe located in Sinpyeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, where many people come to enjoy drinks while overlooking Bomun Lake. The signature menu includes homemade flu prevention tea made with cinnamon sticks, honey, fresh apples, and lemon juice, as well as Gyeongju coffee topped with homemade cream that adds the nuttiness of Udo peanuts. Additionally, you can enjoy cinnamon apple aid, cocoa flat white, and organic tea.','34 Hanguk Tourism 1beon-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Sinpyeong-dong)','10:00~22:00 (Last order 21:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Gyeongju Coffee / Cheomseongdae Coffee / Cold Prevention Tea / Cinnamon Apple Aid / Strawberry Latte, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1020,230,'en','35mm','35mm is a bakery cafe located in Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern and grand building is divided into A, B, and C sections, and the interior features floor-to-ceiling glass, allowing guests to enjoy brunch, bakery items, and drinks while overlooking the lake and sea. Additionally, pets are allowed in the outdoor area.','11-13 Hudong-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 09:30~19:00 (Last order 18:30) - Weekends 09:30~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','35 Latte / 35 White Spritz / Avocado Coffee / American Plate / Korean Beef Bulgogi Sandwich, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL);
INSERT INTO `PLACE_I18N` VALUES (1021,229,'en','No Words','No Words is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is the most famous cafe in the area known as Hwanglidangil and has two floors. The decor has a vintage feel, and after checking for available seats, you can order on the second floor, where staff will bring your coffee to your table. The signature menu is espresso, but long black, cappuccino, and latte are also popular, especially the Excellent Latte, which comes topped with ice cream. There tends to be a long wait on weekends, and ordering one drink per person is mandatory. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby attractions such as Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond.','744 Taejong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 12:00~18:30 (Last order 18:00) - Weekends 11:00~18:30 (Last order 18:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Espresso / Long Black / Latte / Latte + Ice Cream / Flat White, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1022,170,'en','Gabang Bangwa','Gabang Bangwa is a hanok cafe located in Sajeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, where traditional sensibility and a serene atmosphere are well-preserved. Visitors can enjoy traditional drinks and desserts in an interior that retains the beauty of hanok, making it a favorite among travelers. The signature menu is wagashi, which is made entirely by hand, and the ingredients and designs change with the seasons, pleasing both the eyes and the palate. There are also various drinks that pair well with wagashi, such as omija tea made from organic ingredients grown in Mungyeong, sweet and fragrant apricot ade, and smooth matcha cream latte, allowing for personal preferences. It is conveniently located near Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond, making it a great travel route to combine with a cafe visit. If you want to feel relaxed in a traditional atmosphere, visiting Gabang Bangwa is recommended.','61-7 Cheomseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Weekdays] 11:00~18:00 [Weekends] 11:00~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Wagashi / Omija tea / Hongmaesil tea / Misutgaru / Jeju green tea / Boseong hojicha / Milk tea, etc.','Not available','Closed every Wednesday',NULL),(1023,228,'en','Galchi Jorim Tobaki Restaurant','Galchi Jorim Tobaki Restaurant is a traditional Korean food specialty restaurant located in Bukgung-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is housed in a grand hanok, but the interior is decorated in a sophisticated style like a cafe. The parking lot is conveniently located right in front of the restaurant, and the spacious table arrangements allow for a relaxed dining experience. This restaurant specializes in galchi (hairtail fish) using only the galchi caught in Jeju, offering a variety of side dishes in a clean setting. There are group seating options available for family gatherings or group meals. The signature menu includes galchi jjigae (stew) with dolsot rice, available for orders of two or more. Other menu items include abalone dish set, abalone soft tofu, grilled galchi with dolsot rice, abalone porridge, and seafood pancake, with a principle of one meal per person for elementary school students and above. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby Bomun Tourist Complex and Gyeongju CC.','21 Bukgung-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:30~21:00 (Last order 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Jeju Whole Grilled Galchi Set / Galchi Jjigae + Dolsot Rice / Abalone Dish Set / Abalone Soft Tofu / Buckwheat Jeon, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1024,226,'en','Gyeongju Bliss Coffee','Gyeongju Bliss Coffee is a hanok cafe located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features a large building with a vintage exterior and a plant-themed interior, attracting many visitors. It has seating for groups, making it suitable for various gatherings, and pets are allowed. The signature drink is the flat white topped with signature cream, but they also offer a variety of bakery items, sandwiches, and quiches alongside Americano. It is close to Nam Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bulguksa Temple and Seokguram Grotto, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','158 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Bliss Penne / Bakery / Mushroom Soup and Baguette / Jambon Beurre, etc.','Available','Every Thursday',NULL),(1025,225,'en','Gyeongju Dabang','Gyeongju Dabang is located in Hwango-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a dessert cafe featured on a TV program, decorated with vintage items to create an atmosphere reminiscent of the 80s and 90s. The signature drinks include Cheomseongdae latte, made with ice cubes shaped like Cheomseongdae and sweet condensed milk, and Injeolmi waffle, as well as yuzu ade with a rich flavor of yuzu and cream matcha latte topped with soft cream. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond, and Palwujeong Hangover Soup Street.','121-1 Wonhyo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwango-dong)','11:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Cheomseongdae Latte / Cheomseongdae Affogato / Sangria / Grape Ade, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1026,169,'en','Gyeongju Milmyeon Main Branch','Milmyeon is a dish created by North Korean refugees who fled to Busan during the Korean War. Gyeongju Milmyeon Main Branch has inherited that milmyeon technique and has implemented the original taste of milmyeon using traditional methods. The broth is made by simmering Hanwoo bones, herbal medicine, and various vegetables for 24 hours, and the noodles are freshly made upon order. A unique feature of this place is that when you order milmyeon, it comes with grilled meat cooked over charcoal. There are also menus for mixed milmyeon with sauce and hand-made dumplings, as well as a platter of grilled meat.','7 Hanlimwon, Siraeduk-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:40~19:00 - Preparation time 15:50~16:30 - Last order 18:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Milmyeon + Grilled meat / Mixed milmyeon + Grilled meat / Grilled meat platter / Hand-made dumplings, etc.','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(1027,224,'en','Godo Coffee','Godo Coffee is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a hanok cafe next to the stone wall path of Daereungwon, attracting many visitors due to its pleasant atmosphere. The signature drink is Americano made from beans roasted in-house, and they also serve cream shower. Other options include cafe latte, vanilla latte, strawberry latte, peach grapefruit tea, and hand-drip coffee. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae, Hwanglidangil, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond. The indoor area operates as a no-kids zone.','22 Sonhyoja-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Cream Shower / Americano / Cafe Latte / Strawberry Latte / Kusmi Tea, etc.','Not available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(1028,183,'en','Gohyang Milmyeon Main Store','Gohyang Milmyeon Main Store is located in Hwangodo, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, and is a representative restaurant in Gyeongju known for its milmyeon (wheat noodles). It has appeared on various lifestyle information broadcasts. The signature dish is mulmyeon, which is made with broth boiled for more than three days with beef bones and herbal medicine, and the chewy and bouncy noodles are excellent. In addition, you can taste bibim milmyeon, yubu on milmyeon, and steamed dumplings, making it a great place to visit year-round. The interior is neat and has group seating, making it suitable for various gatherings.','7 Taejong-ro 791beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:30~19:30 ※ Early closing when ingredients run out',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mulmyeon / Bibimyeon / Yubu on milmyeon / Potato dumplings / Grilled beef etc.','Available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(1029,223,'en','Gyodong Jipbap','Gyodong Jipbap is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a place where you can enjoy hearty home-cooked meals, attracting many visitors. The signature dish is the grilled pork marinated in soybean paste, served as a home-style meal. Other dishes include spicy chicken bulgogi home-style meal, spicy gochujang jjigae (stew), grilled mackerel home-style meal, and grilled eel rice bowl home-style meal. Takeout is also available. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond.','127 Cheomseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~21:00 (Last order 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Grilled Pork Home-style Meal / Grilled Eel Rice Bowl Home-style Meal / Gochujang Samgyeopsal Home-style Meal / Chadol Doenjang Jjigae & Grilled Mackerel Home-style Meal, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1030,222,'en','Gureung','Gureung is located in Bukgun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a hanok cafe near Bomun Lake that attracts many visitors. The signature dish is the cream brulee souffle, which can only be tasted at this cafe. You can also enjoy Gureung coffee, which is filled with thick cream, and Gureung milk tea made from eight types of black tea. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and there are many tourist attractions nearby, including the Gyeongju World Automobile Museum, Seondeok Park, and Gyeongju Donggungwon. Pets are allowed outdoors.','12-8 Bukgun 3-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Strawberry Souffle / Cream Brulee Souffle / Gureung Coffee / Mango Smoothie / Flat White, etc.','Available','Every Thursday',NULL),(1031,256,'en','Gungsang Gakchiwoo','Gungsang Gakchiwoo is located in Yonggang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It specializes in chicken dishes and attracts many visitors from all over the country, not just Gyeongju. The signature menu is native chicken baeksuk (boiled chicken), and you can also enjoy samgyetang (ginseng chicken soup), seafood pancake, whole octopus bulgogi hot pot, and sanchae bibimbap (mixed rice with mountain vegetables). Some menu items, including native chicken baeksuk, are available for takeout. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are famous tourist attractions such as Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Hanok Village, and Donggung and Wolji.','20-16 Yonghwang-guhwaek 4-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Yonggang-dong)','11:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Native chicken baeksuk / Seafood pancake / Whole octopus bulgogi hot pot / Tofu kimchi, etc.','Available (Dedicated free parking lot)','Open year-round',NULL),(1032,221,'en','Giwagol Matdol Sundubu','Giwagol Matdol Sundubu is a Korean restaurant that makes sundubu (soft tofu) daily from pure domestic soybeans. It has a traditional atmosphere in both its exterior and interior. It opens at 8:30 AM, making breakfast possible. The signature dish is sundubu jjigae (tofu stew). Other dishes include perilla sundubu jjigae, hand-made tofu jeongol, hand-made tofu, pajeon (green onion pancake), dumplings, and kongguksu (cold soybean noodle soup).','142 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 08:30~20:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 19:30 ※ Open without preparation time on weekends ※ May close early if ingredients run out',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Sundubu Jjigae / Hand-made Tofu Mushroom Jeongol / Perilla Sundubu Jjigae / Mucheong Siraegi Jjigae, etc.','Available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(1033,220,'en','Knife','Knife is located in Najung-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It offers a view of the sea in front of Gyeongju, attracting many visitors. The signature drink is Americano, and you can also enjoy cafe latte, vanilla latte, condensed milk latte, handmade caramel latte, and Knife cinnamon. It is close to Donggyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Najung Port and Najung Fine Sand Beach, making it easy to combine sightseeing.','1858-4 Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~17:00 (Last order 16:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Knife Cinnamon / Americano / Cafe Latte / Fresh Chocolate Latte / Omija Ade, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1034,1176,'en','Najungegamyeon','Najungegamyeon is a ramen specialty restaurant located in Najong-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a place where you can enjoy unique ramen while appreciating the East Sea. With beautiful scenery and delicious food, it attracts visitors year-round. The signature menu is the Hongge Ramen, which features a whole red crab. Other options include the Chadolbaki Ramen with a mild flavor, Eomuk Ramen with Busan handmade fish cake, and Egg Takk Ramen that allows you to savor the original taste of ramen. It is close to Donggyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Najong Port and Najong Fine Sand Beach.','1862 Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Weekdays 09:30~19:00 (Break time 15:00~16:30, Last order 18:00) Saturday 09:00~20:00 (Break time 15:00~16:30, Last order 19:00) Sunday 08:00~19:00 (Break time 14:30~16:00, Last order 18:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hongge Ramen / Chadolbaki Ramen / Eomuk Ramen / Egg Takk Ramen / Tteokgalbi / Cheese Ramen, etc.','Available Fee (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(1035,184,'en','NaeNam Meat Restaurant','NaeNam Meat Restaurant is located in Ijo-ri, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a recommended meat restaurant by locals specializing in pork. The signature dishes are pork belly and neck meat. You can adjust the thickness when ordering, choosing from thin, regular, or thick, and you must order a minimum of three servings. In addition, you can taste doenjang jjigae (soybean paste stew) etc. The interior has group seating, making it suitable for various gatherings. It is close to Naenam IC and near Gyeongju National Park Namsan District.','41-5 Yongsan-gangbyeon-gil, Naenam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~21:00 (Last order 20:20)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Pork belly / Neck meat / Doenjang jjigae / Rice etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1036,219,'en','Domi','Domi is an Italian restaurant located in Nodong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It uses fresh ingredients for cooking and offers Mediterranean-style meals that are easy on the stomach. The signature dish is shakshuka. You can also enjoy goulash, pizza, and gambas al ajillo. There is no parking available, but you can use the nearby Haedong parking lot for free for 1 hour. It is close to Gyeongju IC and famous tourist spots like Cheomseongdae, Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, and Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond.','10 Jungang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:30~21:00 - Preparation time 14:30~17:00 - Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Shakshuka / Margherita / Punggi Pizza / Durup Pizza / Gorgonzola Pizza, etc.','Not available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1037,227,'en','La Fleur','La Fleur is located in Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features a vintage exterior and a clean interior that stands out. The signature drink is Americano, and you can also enjoy cafe latte, vanilla latte, cafe mocha, Dutch coffee, and Dutch latte. Additionally, the brunch menu consisting of Korean dishes is also very popular. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae, Bomun Tourist Complex, and Gyeongju CC, which are packed with famous tourist spots.','421-11 Alcheonbuk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Americano / Cafe Latte / Vanilla Latte / Einspänner / Open Sandwich, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1038,1145,'en','Ryomi','Ryomi is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a famous Japanese restaurant on Hwanglidangil. Many people intentionally visit while traveling in Gyeongju. The signature dish is the futomaki, which includes tuna, pickled radish, cucumber, and burdock. Additionally, steak rice bowl, goma soba, chilled citrus soba, chicken skin karaage, and giant shrimp tempura can also be enjoyed. The interior has seating for groups, making it suitable for gatherings. It also has the advantage of allowing pets. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae, Bomun Tourist Complex, and Gyeongju CC.','1058-1, Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~21:00- Preparation time 15:00~17:00- Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Goma soba / Sapporo-style soup curry, futomaki','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1039,218,'en','Ryoko','Ryoko means \'travel\' in Japanese and offers guests a small journey on the dining table. It is famous for its delicious tonkatsu near Daereungwon. Built in a hanok style, it has a vintage exterior and a clean interior. The main menu includes four items: curry, katsu, noodles, and omurice, each with its own charm, attracting a diverse range of customers of all ages.','24 Cheomseong-ro 99beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~21:30 - Preparation time 15:30~17:00 - Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Ryoko Katsu / Ryoki Noodle / Ryomura Rice / Rose Curry / Shrimp Tempura, etc.','Not available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1040,217,'en','Mulcheon Hanwoo','Mulcheon Hanwoo is located in Mulcheon-ri, Cheonbuk-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and interior stand out. There are group seating areas available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu item is Hanwoo Galbit Sal. Other options include Hanwoo Bulgogi, Hanwoo Flower Sirloin, Hanwoo Snowflake Galbit Sal, House Doenjang Hanwoo Stew, and House Doenjang Pork Stew. All Hanwoo served to customers is of the highest grade. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Gyeongju CC, Bomun Tourist Complex, and Sono Bell Gyeongju.','451, Cheonbuknam-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Monday~Saturday] - 11:30~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~16:00 - Last order 20:00 [Sunday] - 11:30~20:00 - Preparation time 15:00~16:00 - Last order 19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','House Doenjang Hanwoo Stew / Hanwoo Bulgogi / Yukhoe Bibimbap / House Doenjang Pork Stew / Flower Sirloin, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1041,185,'en','Milmyeon Restaurant Main Store','Milmyeon Restaurant Main Store has been specializing in milmyeon since 1972, making it the first milmyeon specialty store in Gyeongju with over 50 years of operation. It has been introduced multiple times as a milmyeon restaurant on TV programs, especially appearing on \'Master of Living\'. Here, the bibim milmyeon is served with chewy noodles topped with pickled radish, spicy sauce, boiled pork, and boiled eggs, and the mulmyeon served in a clean broth is very popular. All ingredients are sourced domestically, and the broth is made only with beef bones.','9 Taejong-ro 791beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~19:00 (Last order 18:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mulmyeon / Bibim milmyeon / Handmade dumplings','Available','Every Thursday (However, if Thursday is a legal holiday, it operates normally)',NULL),(1042,248,'en','Basil','Basil is a hanok cafe located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Its vintage exterior and nature-friendly interior stand out. Basil is right next to Hadong Reservoir, offering excellent views. The wide field in front of the cafe transforms into a beautiful flower garden depending on the season. In spring, it is filled with canola flowers and Shasta daisies, while in summer, sunflowers and cockscombs abound. Famous as a sunflower spot, Basil sells \'Sunflower Aid\', a drink resembling sunflowers, which combines the freshness of passion fruit and pineapple. Other menu items include \'Basil Latte\' topped with homemade red bean cream and \'Basil Patbingsu\' made with domestic handmade powdered grain and boiled domestic red beans. Both menu items are characterized by their sweet yet luxurious taste. The cafe is close to Nam Gyeongju IC, and nearby are the UNESCO World Heritage site Seokguram and Blue One Resort.','88 Hadongmoan-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 09:30~21:00 (Last order 20:40) - Weekends 09:30~21:30 (Last order 21:10)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Sunflower Aid / Basil Latte / Basil Patbingsu / Real Strawberry Latte / Americano, etc.','Available (approximately 100 small cars)','Open year-round',NULL),(1043,216,'en','Cheommi','\'Cheommi\' means \'pleasant and joyful\' in Chinese. Located in Yonggang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, Cheommi always prepares food with a cheerful and joyful heart, delivering healthy flavors to customers with great care. The signature menu items are Jjamppong with a base of beef bone broth accompanied by fresh clams and various mushrooms and vegetables, and Jajangmyeon made with only meat and onions without adding water for a rich flavor. Additionally, the lunch special, available for two or more orders, is very popular. Various Chinese dishes and course meals are also available.','11, Yangjeong-ro 328beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st Floor','- 11:00~21:00 - Weekday preparation time 14:45~17:00 - Weekend preparation time 14:30~17:00 - Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seafood Jjamppong / Lunch Special / Jajangmyeon / Yukmi Gan Jajang / Spicy Gan Jajang / Fried Rice, etc.','Available','Open year-round ※ Please call in advance during Seollal and Chuseok',NULL),(1044,215,'en','Jinju Cold Noodles Namgaok','Jinju Cold Noodles Namgaok is located in Eupcheon-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a cold noodle specialty restaurant near the Gyeongju Yangnam Jusangjeolli Observatory. The clean exterior and modern interior stand out. Although it is not directly in front of the sea, you can enjoy your meal while looking at the ocean. It has been featured in MBC\'s current affairs program. The signature menu item is Mul Naengmyeon. Other options include Bibim Naengmyeon, Yukjeon Bibimbap, Yukjeon, and Buckwheat Dumplings. It is close to Donggyeongju IC, and nearby are Naehwa Beach and Nasandeul Park.','497, Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Weekdays] - 11:00~20:10 - Preparation time 16:00~17:00 - Last order 19:40 [Weekends] - 11:00~20:40 - Last order 20:10',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mul Naengmyeon / Bibim Naengmyeon / Yukjeon / Yukjeon Bibimbap / Buckwheat Dumplings, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1045,168,'en','Janggun Amso Charcoal','Janggun Amso Charcoal is a Hanwoo specialty restaurant located in Seokjang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is popular for its excellent taste at affordable prices, attracting many visitors. The interior has crushed stone flooring, and tables are arranged on top, allowing guests to enjoy the feeling of grilling meat outdoors. The signature menu is Janggun rib meat. Other dishes include Janggun flank steak, Janggun sirloin, Janggun chuck flap, Janggun marinated ribs, and Janggun assorted platter. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Hwanglidangil, Daereungwon Stone Wall Road, and Cheomseongdae.','13 Bueong-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Weekdays] - 10:30~21:30 - Preparation time 15:00~16:00 [Weekends] - 10:30~21:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Janggun rib meat / Janggun flank steak / Janggun sirloin / Janggun chuck flap / Janggun marinated ribs / Janggun assorted platter, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1046,214,'en','Lee Jae-won Confectionery Workshop','Lee Jae-won Confectionery Workshop is located in Seobu-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a cake specialty shop with a sophisticated exterior and calm interior. No preservatives or additives are used when making cakes. Only high-quality ingredients like 100% milk butter are used. The signature menu item is Whole Cake No. 2. Other options include Slice Cake, Cookies, Americano, Cafe Latte, Vienna Coffee, and Hot Chocolate. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Hwanglidangil, Daereungwon Dolddam-gil, and Cheomseongdae.','89, Bonghwang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seasonal Fruit Cake / Americano / Cheesecake / Tiramisu, etc.','Available','Every Sunday and Monday',NULL),(1047,213,'en','East Angle Bakery Cafe','East Angle Bakery Cafe is located in Suryum-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Thanks to its location against the backdrop of the Gyeongju sea, visitors can enjoy beautiful views while enjoying their drinks both inside and outside the cafe. The signature menu item is Sea Salt Coffee. Other options include Espresso, Black Sesame Cream Latte, Americano, Cafe Latte, and Lemonade. A variety of bakery items are also available. The cafe is structured over two floors, and the beautiful view from the second floor is particularly famous. Parking is available in front of the store and along the roadside. It is close to Donggyeongju IC, and nearby are Gwanseong Solbat Beach and Jinri Beach.','4, Haebyeon Gongwon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~19:00 (Last order 18:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Americano / Tangerine Latte / Vanilla Latte / Strawberry Latte / Sweet Potato Latte, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1048,212,'en','Uma Wang Main Branch','Uma Wang is located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The antique exterior and calm interior stand out. There are group seating areas available, making it suitable for various gatherings. It has been featured in several broadcasting programs. The signature menu is the hearty Hanwoo Soup (Naju style). Other options include Hanwoo Mulhoe, Nak-sam Galbitang, Thin Skin Meat Dumplings, Yukhoe Bibimbap, Golf Club Galbitang, and Golf Club Galnak Soup. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Bomun Tourist Complex, Gyeongju CC, and Gyeongju World.','168, Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~21:00 (Preparation time 15:00~17:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hanwoo Yukhoe Mulhoe / Hanwoo Mokgalbitang / Hanwoo Yukhoe Bibimbap / Golf Club Galbitang, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1049,211,'en','Woorong Gaksi Ssam Bap','Woorong Gaksi Ssam Bap is a Korean restaurant located in Baedong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Korean house, it has an antique exterior and a calm interior. The signature menu is Woorong Ganjang Doenjang Ssam Bap. Other specialties include Woorong Ganjang Doenjang Je-yuk Ssam Bap and Woorong Sashimi Salad Ssam Bap. You can also enjoy various types of fresh leafy vegetables, which can be refilled at the self-service corner for a healthy meal. Please note that there may be a wait on weekends.','21, Samneung 2-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~20:00 - Preparation time 15:30~16:30 - Last order 19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Woorong Ganjang Doenjang Ssam Bap / Woorong Ganjang Doenjang Je-yuk Ssam Bap / Woorong Salad / Ganjang Doenjang, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1050,210,'en','Woorong Gaksi','Woorong Gaksi is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Upon entering the building topped with blue tiles, visitors are greeted by a clean interior. There are group seating areas available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu items are Woorong Ganjang Doenjang and Grilled Bulgogi. Other options include Woorong Sashimi Salad and Hanwoo Tteokgalbi. The taste of Woorong Ganjang Doenjang is particularly rich, and fresh leafy vegetables are provided for a healthy and hearty meal. There is a spacious parking lot available, making it easy to visit. It is close to Donggyeongju IC and nearby is Blue One Dianas CC.','198, Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 09:30~20:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 19:00 ※ No preparation time on weekends',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Woorong Ganjang Doenjang / Woorong Sashimi Salad / Grilled Bulgogi / Hanwoo Tteokgalbi, etc.','Available','Every Wednesday',NULL),(1051,209,'en','Yaejeong','Yaejeong is located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Korean house, it exudes an antique charm from the exterior. The interior is also in the traditional style, with group seating available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is the Yaejeong Hanjeongshik, which features a full spread of delicious dishes. Other options include Lotus Leaf Rice Hanjeongshik, Bulgogi, Galbijjim, and Grilled Hwangtae. It is well-known among tourists and locals as a top spot for Hanjeongshik.','120, Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Yaejeong Hanjeongshik / Lotus Leaf Rice Set / Je-yuk Set / Nutritional Stone Pot Rice Set, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1052,186,'en','Yangnam Seafood Kalguksu','Yangnam Seafood Kalguksu is a noodle shop located in Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is situated along the Wave Sound Road section from Eocheon Port Gallery to Haseo Port. Located by the coastal cliffs, you can enjoy kalguksu while looking at the sea. The signature dish is seafood kalguksu made with fresh seafood and locally sourced mugwort noodles. The crispy seafood pancake is also a delicacy. In addition, you can taste spicy kalguksu, mugwort bibim kalguksu, and king dumplings.','472 Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seafood kalguksu / Seafood pancake / Spicy kalguksu / Mugwort bibim kalguksu etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1053,208,'en','Wildflower Diary Cafe','Wildflower Diary Cafe is a dessert cafe located in Wangsin-ri, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern exterior and nature-friendly interior space stand out, and the spacious cafe site gives the feeling of walking through a botanical garden. There are group seating areas inside, making it suitable for various gatherings, but it is an adults-only garden cafe as only those aged 14 and above are allowed. The cafe has many photo zones and plenty of outdoor seating, which are also advantages. The signature menu item is Grapefruit Remembrance, and you can also enjoy Mont Blanc, Peach Juice, Americano, Cafe Latte, Mugwort Milk Tea, as well as Croffles and Scones. It is close to Bukgyeongju IC and Gangdong IC, and nearby is the UNESCO World Heritage Site, Yangdong Village.','332-6, Ogeum-gun-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~21:00 (Last order 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Orange Bianco / Special Affogato / Blancer Chocolate / Lavender Soft Ice Cream, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1054,207,'en','Yard','Cafe Yard is a brunch cafe located within the Bomun Tourist Complex in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It was featured in the SBS current affairs program. The stylish exterior and clean interior are eye-catching. Additionally, enjoying the changing scenery with cherry blossoms in spring and lush greenery in summer is a special feature. The signature menu is a handmade strawberry cake. Other options include the Yard English Plate made with soft English muffins and sausage bacon, and the Yard American Plate, which offers both luxury and value in brunch menus.','2 Cheongun 2-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 09:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30) - Brunch 09:00~15:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Yard English Plate / Hamon Campagne / Basil Cold Pasta / Guacamole Open Rye Baguette, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1055,187,'en','After Work Charcoal Grilled Ribs','After Work Charcoal Grilled Ribs is a beef restaurant located in Sajung-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It specializes in Hanwoo beef and has been in business for over 30 years, having been featured on TV programs. The signature dish is ribs, along with salt-grilled, bulgogi, and flank steak. Side dishes include radish salad, green onion salad, lettuce, and seasoned vegetables, and the soybean paste stew is also delicious. The meat is fresh, but prepared ingredients may run out early. There is group seating, making it a recommended place for family gatherings or company dinners.','190 Geumseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:30~21:30 (Preparation time 15:00~16:40)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hanwoo ribeye salt / Hanwoo ribeye marinated / Hanwoo large ribs salt / Hanwoo large ribs marinated / Hanwoo flank steak salt etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1056,206,'en','Seasoning','Seasoning is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior is traditional Hanok style, giving it a vintage look, while the interior feels calm and clean. It is known as a pasta restaurant, attracting many visitors. The signature menu is Prawn Rice, which combines shrimp and chili sauce. The cream pasta flavored with chili oil and shrimp is also a delicacy. Other options include truffle pasta made with three types of mushrooms and oil, and ragu pasta cooked with bacon and ragu sauce. There is no dedicated parking, but public parking nearby can be used. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Daereungwon Stone Wall Path and Cheomseongdae.','25-2 Cheomseong-ro 99beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 10:30~21:00 - Preparation time 15:30~17:00 - Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seasoning Pasta / Prawn Rice / Squid Ink Risotto / Cream Pasta, etc.','Not available','Closed every Tuesday',NULL),(1057,205,'en','Hyangmisa','Hyangmisa is a cafe located on Hyangridang-gil in Gyeongju. The small building with a white tone evokes a retro sentiment and is decorated with large glass windows. Since coffee is roasted on-site, you can enjoy coffee while smelling the aroma of roasted beans. The signature menu is filter coffee, and there are coffee options like espresso, americano, and cafe latte that offer deep flavors. Various beans and coffee-related merchandise are also sold.','734 Taejong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~18:00 (Last order 17:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Filter Coffee / Espresso / Americano / Cafe Latte / Short Latte, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1058,204,'en','Steel Room','Steel Room is located in Nodong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The stylish exterior and calm, heavy interior are notable in this Western-style restaurant. The signature menu is Beef Wellington, made by wrapping beef in pastry and baking it. You can also enjoy beef steak served with smooth carrot puree, tomato sauce, and sautéed onions, as well as sweet shrimp and fragrant seaweed pasta with special sauce and fresh noodles. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Daereungwon Stone Wall Path, Cheomseongdae, and Gyeongju Joksam Site Museum, making it great for combined travel.','87 Wonhyo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','17:00~24:00 (Weekend preparation time 15:00~17:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hanwoo Tenderloin Beef Wellington / Lobster Bisque Shrimp Risotto / Sweet Shrimp Seaweed Fresh Noodle Pasta / Homemade Bacon Cream Gnocchi, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1059,203,'en','Start Coffee','Start Coffee is located in Najung-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and modern interior are eye-catching. You can enjoy drinks while overlooking the sea in front of Gyeongju. Most seats are arranged to have a view of the sea. The signature menu is Start Coffee, which is based on a savory latte topped with black sesame cream. Other options include a sweet and heavy-bodied Cafe Latte and Start Basic, which is cold brew topped with cream. There are group seating arrangements available for gatherings. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Najung Fine Sand Beach and Gampo Port.','1862 Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~19:00 (Last order 18:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Start Coffee / Start Basic / Americano / Cafe Latte / Affogato, etc.','Available','Closed every Tuesday',NULL),(1060,257,'en','Hyundai Ssambap','Hyundai Ssambap is a ssambap (rice wrapped in leaves) restaurant located in Daebon-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Initially specializing in natural wild flatfish dishes, it has now combined sashimi and ssambap, making ssambap the representative menu. There are sashimi ssambap and grilled fish ssambap, and a set menu that allows you to taste both. Other offerings include mulhoe (cold raw fish soup), hoe-deopbap (sashimi rice), and daegu-tang (cod soup). The side dishes served with seaweed soup are diverse, and seaweeds like miyeok, tot, and dashima can be enjoyed as ssam. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Gyeongju Munmu Daewang Tomb and Najung Goun Sand Beach, making it possible to combine sightseeing.','88 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','10:00~20:00 (Weekdays preparation time 15:30~17:00 / Last order 19:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Set (Grilled fish + Sashimi ssambap) / Sashimi ssambap / Grilled fish / Mulhoe / Hoe-deopbap / Daegu-tang, etc.','Available (Free)','Every Tuesday (if Tuesday is a holiday, closed the next day)',NULL),(1061,202,'en','Picnic','Picnic is a cafe that feels like stepping into a fairy tale, designed with a green indoor garden concept and comfortable, cozy furniture to create a relaxing healing space. Operating under the slogan \'Special experiences create special memories,\' it plans various programs to create memories with guests. The essence of the cafe, coffee, and the accompanying bakery and desserts are consistently maintained for taste and high quality. Unique to Picnic are the Gyeongju specialties, Park Il-seop Burger and Park Il-seop Kaimak Set.','15 Daregil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 10:00~19:00 (Last order 18:30) - Weekends 09:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Park Il-seop Kaimak Set / Picnic Sandwich & Salad / Picnic Sandwich & French Fries / Bulgogi Pizza / Park Il-seop Sourdough Bread, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1062,201,'en','Society Donkey','Society Donkey is located in Hwangodong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The red brick exterior and modern atmosphere of the interior stand out. It is famous for its pizza and pasta, always bustling with people. The signature menu includes a fun-named pizza called Mole Pizza, topped with cheese, cherry tomatoes, and yogurt sauce on a thin crust. Other options include Peacock Pasta, Donkey Cream Pasta, Molchicken Curry, and Gambas al Ajillo. It is recognized as a safe restaurant by the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Hwangseong Park, Cheomseongdae, Donggung and Wolji, and the National Gyeongju Museum, making it great for combined tourism.','127 Imhae-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Mole Pizza / Trinity Salad Pasta / Lasagna / Mole Cream Pasta, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1063,200,'en','Sodis Coffee','Sodis Coffee is a large cafe located in Oryuri, Hyeongok-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exotic exterior and sophisticated interior are impressive. You can enjoy Matcha Cream, Americano, Cafe Latte, Flat White, Scotch Cream Latte, and Sodis Blend Black Tea. There are group seating arrangements available for various gatherings. There is a parking lot that can accommodate over 50 cars at once. Only small dogs under 10 kg are allowed, and they must be on a leash and have waste bags, and only the outdoor area can be used. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Bomun Tourist Complex and Gyeongju CC.','161 Hyeongsan-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~22:00 (Last order 21:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Nutty Cream / Scotch Cream Latte / Nutty Cream / Matcha Cream / Americano, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1064,199,'en','Sandre','Sandre is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The vintage exterior and clean interior stand out. The signature menu includes handmade Tteokgalbi, fried dishes, Sambaccho Bossam, Tofu Gangjeong, Japchae, Jeon, and Salad in the Usulcho Jeongsik. Other options include Geumunhwa Jeongsik, Baekbokryeong Jeongsik, and Hasuwo Jeongsik. A la carte dishes include Mushroom Sweet and Sour. You can scoop rice from a personal pot and pour water to enjoy Nurungji as a dessert. There are group seating arrangements available for various gatherings, and private rooms are also prepared. It is recognized as a safe restaurant by the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. Reservations are not accepted, and entry is on a first-come, first-served basis. It is close to Nam Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Bulguksa and Seokguram.','299-5 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:30 (Last order 19:20)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hasuwo Course / Baekbokryeong Course / Mushroom Perilla Soup / Sambaccho Bossam, etc.','Available','Closed every Monday',NULL),(1065,198,'en','Bulgukjeong Tteokgalbi','Bulgukjeong Tteokgalbi is located in Madong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, and is famous for its 50-year tradition of delicious food. The signature menu includes Tteokgalbi and Doenjang Jjigae, as well as Tteokgalbi Jeongsik with over 10 side dishes and spicy Sundubu Jeongsik. Additionally, breakfast is available for the entire menu, including Lotus Leaf Rice Jeongsik with basic side dishes. In summer, cool Naengmyeon and Naengmilmyeon, as well as Hanwoo Mulhoe, are popular, and Chodang-style Sundubu and Turmeric Gondeurebap are well-known for their taste. The interior is spacious, and there is a parking lot available for easy access.','69 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Gondeure Namul Bibimbap / Mul Naengmyeon / Naengmilmyeon / Hanwoo Mulhoe / Handmade Tteokgalbi Jeongsik, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1066,197,'en','Bomun Hanwoo','Bomun Hanwoo is located in Sinpyeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It only serves premium Hanwoo beef and grills it using domestic charcoal. Inside, there are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is grilled Hanwoo. Other options include Hanwoo Yukhoe, Hanwoo Bulgogi Jeongol, Hanwoo Yukhoe Bibimbap, Hanwoo Gomtang, and Cold Noodle Set. It has a spacious parking lot, making it easy to visit, and the interior features large windows for good lighting, enhancing the dining experience. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex, Gyeongju CC, and Gyeongju World.','9 Expo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (K-Pop Museum)','- 11:30~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hanwoo Yukhoe / Hanwoo Bulgogi Jeongol / Hanwoo Yukhoe Bibimbap / Hanwoo Gomtang, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1067,167,'en','Baekrihyang Hwangseong Main Branch','Baekrihyang Hwangseong Main Branch is located in Hwangseong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features a modern exterior and a clean interior. As you enter the narrow road, a large building and spacious parking lot come into view, contrary to expectations. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is sweet and sour pork. In addition, you can enjoy almost all dishes offered at Chinese restaurants, including uni jjajang, tray jjajang, jjamppong, seafood fried rice, large chili shrimp, and yangjangpi. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby are Hwangseong Park, Cheomseongdae, and the National Gyeongju Museum.','13-7 Hwangseong-ro 69beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~21:00 - Preparation time 15:00~16:00 - Last order 20:40',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Uni jjajang / Seafood jjamppong / Tray jjajang / Sweet and sour pork / Spicy pork / Large chili shrimp, etc.','Available (30 cars) (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(1068,196,'en','Cafe Gwaeryeong','Cafe Gwaeryeong is a Hanok cafe located in Gwaeryeong-ri, Oedong-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features a charming atmosphere with the main building and a separate building where pets are allowed, along with a spacious garden. The calm interior space is also notable. The signature menu is Americano. Other options include Cafe Latte, Hand Drip Cappuccino, Vanilla Latte, Sweet Red Bean Latte, and Einspänner. It is close to Nam Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Tohamsan Natural Recreation Forest, UNESCO World Heritage Seokguram, and Bulguksa Temple, making it rich in tourist resources. Pets are allowed, but leashes and waste bags must be brought.','12 Gwaeryeong-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~18:30 (Last order 18:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Americano / Cafe Latte / Hand Drip / Cappuccino / Vanilla Latte, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1069,195,'en','Cafe Road 100','Cafe Road 100 is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a large cafe consisting of two buildings, Hanok and Western-style. Inside, there are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Ocean Latte, which allows you to experience the refreshing sweetness of fruits. The Bulgogi Panini, which includes bulgogi, tomatoes, and mozzarella cheese in squid ink ciabatta, is also popular. In addition, Americano, Elderflower Ade, Pasta Salad, etc. are available. It is close to Nam Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Nostalgic Dal-dong Village, Bulguksa Temple, and Seokguram, making it easy to plan connected tourism.','100 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Friday to Wednesday 10:00~21:00 - Thursday 10:00~18:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Ocean Latte / Americano / Sweet Red Bean Soup / Elderflower Ade / Bulgogi Panini, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1070,261,'en','Cafe Marche','Cafe Marche is a hanok cafe located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior is quaint, but inside, desserts are displayed in a charming manner. Many customers visit because of the beautiful cafe photos posted on social media. The representative menu is the Matilda cake, which combines a rich chocolate sheet with sweet chocolate sauce. Other offerings include a dense carrot cake with orange caramel sauce and Earl Grey scones that allow you to enjoy the fragrant aroma of Earl Grey. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Hwanglidangil, Daereungwon Dol-dam-gil, and Cheomseongdae.','22-7, 81 Cheomseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st floor','Daily 09:00 - 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Matilda Cake / Carrot Cake, Blueberry Jam Butter Scone, Earl Grey Scone, etc.','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(1071,262,'en','Cafe Sol','Cafe Sol is a hanok cafe located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has a garden and allows pets. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The representative menu is Americano. Other offerings include solar latte, cafe latte, vanilla latte, einspänner, and lemon mint tea. There is no parking available, so you need to use the nearby public parking lot. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Hwanglidangil, Palwujeong Haejang-guk Street, and Cheomseongdae.','62-8, 1092 Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st floor','10:30~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Solar Latte / Solar Latte / Pure Milk Ice Cream / Lychee Chamomile Iced Tea / Chocolate Latte, etc.','Not available (Use nearby public parking)','Open year-round',NULL),(1072,194,'en','Page Nine','Page Nine is located in Bukgung-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exotic exterior and modern atmosphere of the interior stand out. Visitors can enjoy drinks or food while overlooking the view near Bomun Tourist Complex. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Hamburger Steak. In addition, Americano, Espresso, Cappuccino, and Cafe Mocha are also available. The coffee is well-received for its popular taste without acidity. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex and Gyeongju CC.','132-24 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:50~21:00 (Last order 20:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Sirloin Pork Cutlet / Hamburger Steak / Americano / Cappuccino, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1073,166,'en','Hwasan Charcoal & Handmade Tofu','Hwasan Charcoal is located in Hwasan Hanwoo Charcoal Complex in Cheonbuk-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been in operation for over 30 years and is well-known as a Hanwoo restaurant. It has appeared on KBS 2TV\'s current affairs program \'Saengsaeng Jeongbong\'. The signature menu is salt-grilled rib meat. Other dishes include marinated rib meat, yukhoe, sirloin, flank steak, cold noodles, and homemade soybean paste stew. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. It is close to Bukgyeongju IC, and nearby is Luna X Golf Course.','460 Cheongang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Monday to Saturday 11:00~21:00 - Sunday 11:00~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Salt-grilled rib meat / Yukhoe / Marinated rib meat / Sirloin / Flank steak / Cold noodles, etc.','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(1074,193,'en','Hwangnam Bibimbap','Hwangnam Bibimbap is a popular restaurant located on Hwanglidangil in Gyeongju. The traditional Hanok building has large glass windows that allow for views of the outside scenery. The signature menu is the raw beef bibimbap with domestic raw beef and Beolgyo cockles combined with a special sauce. The thick pork ribs that evoke nostalgic flavors can be enjoyed together with raw beef in the raw beef rib bibimbap, and the cockle rib bibimbap is also very popular. Additionally, the Hwangnam Special allows you to taste raw beef, cockles, ribs, and bibimbap all at once, so you can choose according to your preference.','11 Cheomseong-ro 73beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 10:00~21:00 - Preparation time 15:30~17:00 - Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Raw Beef Cockle Bibimbap / Hwangnam Special / Raw Beef Rib Bibimbap / Cockle Rib Bibimbap / Raw Beef Mulhoe, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1075,192,'en','Hidden C','Hidden C is located in Oryu-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features a modern atmosphere with a stylish interior. Visitors can enjoy drinks or desserts while admiring the sea in front of Gampo, attracting many visitors year-round. The signature menu is Iced Americano, and Cold Brew, Cream Cold Brew, Cafe Latte, and Vanilla Latte are also available. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Oryu Goara Beach, Gampo Port, and Najung Fine Sand Beach, making it easy to plan connected tourism. Pets are allowed, but leashes and waste bags must be brought.','2560 Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~19:30 (Last order 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Americano / Espresso / Peach Iced Tea / Chocolate Latte / Green Tea Latte, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1076,1180,'en','Gyeongju Original Kongguk','Gyeongju Original Kongguk is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been featured in various broadcasts such as TV Chosun\'s current affairs program and SBS\'s current affairs program. The traditional Hanok architecture gives it a vintage appearance and a charming atmosphere. The interior has seating for groups, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is warm kongguk. It is divided into three options: served with black sesame, black beans, honey, and glutinous rice donuts. Other dishes include kongguksu, cold radish kongguk, sundubu jjigae, fresh soybean leaf soup, and fresh seafood pancake. It is close to Gyeongju IC and surrounded by famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village.','113 Cheomseong-ro, Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 09:00~19:45- Morning preparation time 10:30~11:30- Afternoon preparation time 16:30~17:30- Last order 19:15',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Warm Kongguk / Cold Radish Kongguk / Kongguksu / Perilla Sundubu, etc.','Available','Every Sunday / Lunar New Year and Chuseok holidays',NULL),(1077,1163,'en','Guhwang Banjum','Guhwang Banjum is a Chinese restaurant located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, known for its very affordable prices but excellent taste, making it a popular choice for those craving Chinese food. The signature menu items are the seafood-rich Jjamppong and the non-greasy Jajangmyeon. Jjamppong and Jajangmyeon are available in small, medium, and large sizes, allowing customers to choose according to their appetite. Additionally, various Chinese dishes such as Gan Jajang, Sweet and Sour Pork, Udon, and Spicy Rice are available. They also sell Jjamppong broth, Japchae, and fried dumplings as side dishes.','239 Wonhyo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~16:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Jajangmyeon / Spicy Rice / Jjamppong / Udon, etc.','Not available','Every Sunday',NULL),(1078,1109,'en','Dain Spicy Pork Rib Stew','Dain Spicy Pork Rib Stew is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Korean house, it exudes a vintage charm from the outside. The interior creates a clean yet nostalgic atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu includes spicy pork rib stew, which is divided into spicy, medium, and mild flavors. Additionally, Dain offers pork belly, soybean paste stew, cheese fried rice, and egg fried rice. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and famous tourist attractions such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village are nearby.','25 Wonhwa-ro 181beon-gil, Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~21:00 (Preparation time 15:00~16:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:25:05','Spicy Pork Rib Stew / Domestic Fresh Pork Ribs / Cheese Fried Rice / Egg Fried Rice, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1079,1179,'en','Daegejang Sundubu Geumseonggwan','Daegejang Sundubu Geumseonggwan is located in Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been featured in various broadcasts, including SBS current affairs programs and KBS 2TV current affairs programs. The exterior shows traces of time, and the interior creates a clean atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Daegejang Sundubu, which is made by mixing whole Daege (king crab) with crab meat and sauce, cooked with sundubu (soft tofu). The Abalone Seafood Stew, made with various seafood including abalone, is also popular among many visitors. Other options include Bulgogi Stew, Seafood Pajeon, Flower Crab Soy Sauce Marinated Crab, Flower Crab Seasoned Crab, and Abalone Steamed Dish. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex, Gyeongju Donggungwon, and Gyeongju World, making it convenient for combined travel.','117 Chodang-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~20:00- Preparation time 15:00~17:00- Last order 19:40',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Daegejang Sundubu / Sundubu Jjigae / Abalone Seafood Stew / Bulgogi Stew, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1080,188,'en','Donggung Banjeom','Donggung is located in Bukgung-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been featured in KBS 2TV current affairs programs and MBC current affairs programs. The exterior exudes the charm of traditional Hanok, and the interior creates a clean atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Sundubu Jjamppong. In addition, various Chinese dishes such as Spicy Pepper Jajangmyeon, Bokbunja Chapssal Tangsooyuk, Uni Jajangmyeon, and Seafood Fried Rice are available. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex, Gyeongju Donggungwon, and Gyeongju World, making it easy to plan a connected trip.','27 Bukgung-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~21:00 (Last order 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Sundubu Jjamppong Rice / Spicy Pepper Jajang / Uni Jajang / Spicy Sichuan Jjamppong, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1081,161,'en','Bandosikdang','Bandosikdang is an old rib restaurant in Gyeongju. It is a well-known local restaurant among locals, where you can grill Korean beef ribs over a charcoal fire. When you order the main menu items such as Korean beef ribs, marinated ribs, salt-grilled rib meat, and marinated rib meat, the owner will also tell you how to enjoy them deliciously. With the quality and taste of the meat, along with the friendliness, it is a restaurant that tourists visiting Gyeongju return to.','83 Hwarang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','16:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Korean Beef Ribs / Marinated Korean Beef Ribs / Salt-grilled Rib Meat / Marinated Rib Meat, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1082,189,'en','Benjamass','Gyeongju Benjamass Cafe is a luxurious cafe located in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It offers a sophisticated interior and spacious environment, with a variety of coffee and dessert menus that are popular. The carefully prepared coffee and desserts are particularly attractive, making it a beloved spot for visitors enjoying Gyeongju tourism. It is a popular place where many people can comfortably spend time in a serene atmosphere harmonized with nature.','369 Alcheonbuk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~24:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Brunch / Shrimp Salad / Steak Mushroom Salad / Americano / Cafe Latte, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1083,1162,'en','Bubul Eo-tang Myeongga','Bubul Eo-tang Myeongga is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior reflects the elegance of a traditional Korean house, and the interior creates a nostalgic atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu item is Eo-tang Hand-made Dumplings. In addition, various Eo-tang dishes such as Eo-tang Kalguksu, Eo-tang Dumpling Soup, Eo-tang Hangover Soup, Eo-tang Rice, and Spicy Eo-tang Hand-made Dumplings are available. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include the nostalgic Dal-dong neighborhood and the UNESCO World Heritage site Seokguram, making it ideal for combined travel.','174-17 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hadong)','- 10:00~20:00 - Preparation time 15:00~16:30 - Last order 19:20',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Eo-tang Hand-made Dumplings / Eo-tang Kalguksu / Eo-tang Dumpling Soup / Eo-tang Hangover Soup, etc.','Available','Every Sunday to Monday',NULL),(1084,1181,'en','Buyong','Buyong is a Chinese restaurant located in Geumjang-ri, Hyeongok-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern exterior and clean atmosphere of the interior stand out. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu features a variety of course meals. Other dishes include uni jjajangmyeon, seafood udon, and seafood jjambbong.','30 Geumjang 1-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:10~21:30 (Last order 20:40)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Seafood Jajang / Spicy Uni Jajangmyeon / Chinese Cold Noodles / Oyster Jjambbong, etc.','Available (Free)','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1085,1206,'en','Samneung Gohyang Handmade Noodles','Samneung Gohyang Handmade Noodles is located in Baedong, Gyeongju, North Gyeongsang Province. It has been featured in various broadcasts such as KBS 2TV current affairs programs and SBS current affairs programs. The traditional Hanok exterior and vintage atmosphere of the interior are notable. There is group seating available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is handmade noodles made from local wheat, and grain noodles are also popular. Other dishes include Hanwoo Beef Head Boiled Meat, Seafood Pancakes, and Acorn Jelly. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Silla Wolsung Daegun Danseong, Samneung Forest, and Gyeongju Namsan, making it great for combined travel.','2 Samneung 3-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','08:30~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Local Wheat Handmade Noodles / Grain Noodles / Hanwoo Beef Head Boiled Meat / Seafood Pancakes, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1086,162,'en','Songjeongwon Sundubu','Songjeongwon Sundubu is located in Sirae-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and calm atmosphere of the interior stand out. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is the old-fashioned sundubu, and the seafood sundubu is also popular among many. In addition, you can taste marinated crab, seasoned crab, stir-fried squid, and pork soy sauce bulgogi. The restaurant closes early when all ingredients are used up.','23 Gumae 1-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Weekdays] - 10:00~16:30 [Weekends] - 10:00~15:30 ※ Closes when ingredients are exhausted / Call before visiting',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Old-fashioned Sundubu / Seafood Sundubu / Marinated Crab / Pork Soy Sauce Bulgogi, etc.','Available (Free)','Every Monday',NULL),(1087,190,'en','Suramilmyeon','Suramilmyeon is a Jjamppong specialty restaurant located in Dongcheon-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and traditional atmosphere of the interior stand out. It offers a rich Jjamppong filled with various seafood such as abalone, mussels, clams, scallops, and shrimp, along with plenty of vegetables, providing a refreshing yet deep flavor that enhances when eaten with fluffy rice. It is a principle to order one menu per person. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex, Gyeongju Donggungwon, and Gyeongju World, making it easy to plan a connected trip.','286 Yangjeong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~14:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Special Jjamppong / Seafood Jjamppong, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1088,845,'en','Jungle Media Park','Jungle Media Park is an immersive media art exhibition hall located in Sinpyeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It offers a new and unique experience where visitors can walk through spaces that were only felt in imagination, beyond the monitor frame. There are various attractions, including the mysterious jungle of jaguars overflowing with life, a temple where you can uncover the secrets of ancient civilizations through a journey in lost time, and the underwater world filled with colorful marine life. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby the Bomun Tourist Complex and Cheomseongdae, allowing for combined tourism.','B1, 465-67 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Weekdays 10:00~19:00 (Last admission 18:00) - Weekends 10:00~19:30 (Last admission 18:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,'Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1089,1009,'en','Gyeongju World Automobile Museum','Gyeongju World Automobile Museum is a museum where visitors can observe the evolution of automobiles from the early days to modern times, representing human mechanical civilization. Opened in March 2017, it consists of three floors. Through various themed exhibitions and permanent displays, visitors can glimpse the history and cultural changes of automobiles. Additionally, it features an exhibition hall, video history hall, automobile cafe, and souvenir shop. Visitors can sit in a bucket seat used in racing cars and feel vibrations according to vehicle movements and road conditions when they turn the steering wheel. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby Bomun Tourist Complex and Cheomseongdae, allowing for combined tourism.','132-22 Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Bukgun-dong)','10:00~18:00','- Adults 9,900 KRW - Youth 8,000 KRW - Children 6,600 KRW ※ For more details, please refer to the website','2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:25:05',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(1090,191,'en','Masijoeun House','Masijoeun House is located in Nodong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in Hanok style, it features a charming exterior and a traditional atmosphere. Inside, there are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Stone Pot Rice. Other popular dishes include Buckwheat Jeonbyeong, Pork Ribs, Samgyeopsal, and Meat + Stone Pot Rice. The special sauce can be used to mix with rice or as a dipping sauce. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby famous tourist attractions include Cheomseongdae, National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it easy to explore together.','3 Taegong-ro 727beon-gil, Gyeongju (Noseo-dong)','11:00~22:00 (Last order 21:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Stone Pot Rice / Tteokgalbi Set / Ceramic Garlic Boiled Pork / Samgyeopsal, etc.','Available','Closed every Wednesday',NULL),(1091,1174,'en','Hongsi','Hongsi is a restaurant themed around traditional sauces, fermented foods, and persimmons. The owner personally researches and cooks without using any seasonings, resulting in a clean and light taste. It features a beautiful 700-pyeong garden and a European-style terrace for relaxation, where you can enjoy meals accompanied by live music in the summer. The signature menu is a set meal that includes five appetizers, 16 side dishes, a main course, tea, and dessert. The bulgogi set meal includes seven appetizers, 16 side dishes, bulgogi, tea, and dessert. In addition to the set meals, there are also a la carte options such as stir-fried octopus, bulgogi, cold pig\'s feet, and dolpatjeon.','5, Hwarang-ro 19beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Seonggeon-dong)','[Thursday to Tuesday] - 11:30~21:30 - Last order for lunch 14:30 - Preparation time 15:30~17:00 - Last order for dinner 20:30 [Wednesday] - 11:30~15:30 - Last order 14:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Set Meal / Bulgogi Set Meal / Stir-fried Octopus / Bulgogi / Cold Pig\'s Feet, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1092,1113,'en','Pizza Ok','Pizza Ok is a pizza specialty restaurant located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior, utilizing a traditional Korean house, creates a vintage atmosphere, while the interior is decorated as a clean and comfortable space. There are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for family gatherings or various meetings. The signature menu includes the Truffle & Pepperoni Half-and-Half Pizza topped with mushrooms, sirloin, poached egg, and truffle oil, along with various other dishes like Truffle Bismarck, Pepperoni, Margherita, and Shrimp Rose Cream Spaghetti. It is conveniently located near Gyeongju IC, with major tourist attractions such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village nearby.','1, Sonhyoja-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st Floor','11:00~20:40 (Preparation time 15:15~17:00) * No preparation time on weekends and public holidays',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Burrata Melanzane / Octopus Seafood Spaghetti / Pizza Ok Special Steak / Truffle French Fries, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1093,174,'en','Hanuga Mul-ae','Hanuga Mul-ae is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a hanok, it exudes an antique charm from the outside. The clean atmosphere of the interior is also noticeable. The signature menu is Hanwoo Mulhoe. Hanwoo Mulhoe is characterized by the harmony of icy broth and fresh Hanwoo beef. Other dishes include yukhoe bibimbap, yukhoe, tteok bulgogi, cheese bulgogi, and Hanwoo gukbap. It has a spacious parking lot, making it convenient for family gatherings or visits by car.','319 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~20:00 - Preparation time 15:00~17:00 - Last order 19:20',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hanwoo Mulhoe / Yukhoe bibimbap / Yukhoe / Cheese bulgogi / Tteok bulgogi, etc.','Available (Free)','Closed every Monday',NULL),(1094,1114,'en','Harubang Ttukbaegi','Harubang Ttukbaegi is located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Korean house, it exudes a vintage charm from its exterior. The interior also features a clean atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Momguk, and the Gosa-ri Yukgaejang is also very popular. Other offerings include Andong Mackerel, BBQ Set, and Seasoned BBQ Set. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC, with nearby attractions such as Seokguram, Bulguksa, and the Memory Lane.','101, Hadong Moan-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Jeju Momguk / Andong Mackerel / BBQ Set / Gosa-ri Yukgaejang, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1095,1038,'en','Haseo Port','Haseo Port is a fishing port located in Haseo-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is situated in Jinri Village, Haseo 4-ri, and is also known as Jinri Port or Yulpo Jinri Port. Near the port, there is Haseo Beach, which is a mix of pebbles and sand. Haseo Port is the starting point of the 1.7 km coastal walking path called Wave Sound Road, which leads to Eopcheon Port. Walking along this path, visitors can view the Yangnam Columnar Joint, designated as a natural monument, and the fan-shaped columnar joint at the Yangnam Columnar Joint Observatory.','61 Haseo-ri, Yangnam-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Open all year round',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13',NULL,NULL,'Open year-round',NULL),(1096,1178,'en','Hanwoo 114 Charcoal Grill','Hanwoo 114 Charcoal Grill is a meat restaurant located in Angang-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern exterior and clean atmosphere of the interior stand out. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu includes Hanwoo sirloin and Hanwoo rib meat, among various grilled Hanwoo options. After purchasing your preferred meat from the butcher shop, you can go to the restaurant, pay for the table setting, and grill it yourself. Other options include Yukhoe, Hanwoo Soup, Beef Gukbap, Mul Naengmyeon, Bibim Naengmyeon, and Somyeon. It is close to Gangdong IC, and nearby are the UNESCO World Heritage Site Yangdong Village and Oksan Seowon, making it easy to visit before or after your meal.','1535-2 Ahyeon-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Grilled Hanwoo / Hanwoo Soup / Beef Gukbap / Yukhoe, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1097,1159,'en','Haemaji Hoetown','Haemaji Hoetown is located in Daebon-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Operating for nearly 30 years, it features a clean exterior and a calm interior atmosphere. The interior can accommodate up to 100 people simultaneously and has group seating, making it suitable for various gatherings. The representative menu includes various sashimi such as sea bream and bass. Additionally, it offers mulhoe, sashimi rice, abalone porridge, grilled rockfish, and spicy rockfish soup. Haemaji course and special course are also available for tasting various seafood. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC and nearby Gyeongju Munmu Daewang Tomb and Najung Fine Sand Beach.','1514 Donghaean-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Haemaji Course / Special Course / Grilled Rockfish / Mulhoe, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1098,1140,'en','Haeam Hoesikdang','Haeam Hoesikdang is a sashimi restaurant located in Daebon-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been operated for over 40 years by the third generation and has been featured in the SBS current affairs program. The restaurant has a neat exterior and a calm indoor atmosphere, with group seating available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The view of the sea in front of Gampo can be enjoyed while dining. The signature menu includes assorted sashimi, and various seafood dishes such as sashimi rice, mulhoe, spicy soup, grilled abalone, and grilled rockfish.','12-48 Daemidgil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Monday / Wednesday] 10:30~17:30 [Thursday] 10:00~14:00 [Friday] 10:00~16:00 [Saturday / Sunday] 10:00~19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Assorted seafood sauce / Seafood sauce + rice set / Seafood sauce + rice bowl set / Abalone rice set, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday (However, if Tuesday is a public holiday, normal business hours apply)',NULL),(1099,1164,'en','Hyeongje Banjum','Hyeongje Banjum is located in Gampo-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It features a clean exterior and an old-fashioned atmosphere in its interior. It is known for being operated by a master chef. The signature menu item is the spicy Chinese bibimbap. Other offerings include Jajangmyeon, Hyeongje Jjamppong, Jjamppong Rice, Dumplings, Sweet and Sour Pork, Palbochae, and Kkanpungyuk. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC and nearby attractions include Gampo Port and the Songdaemal Lighthouse Light Experience Exhibition Hall.','94 Gampo-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:30~19:00 (Last order 18:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Chinese Bibimbap / Jajangmyeon / Hyeongje Jjamppong / Chinese Bibimbap, etc.','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1100,1128,'en','Tiger Kats','Tiger Kats is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior blends the elegance of a traditional Hanok with a modern atmosphere, and the clean interior is also eye-catching. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is the Tenderloin Kats Set. Other offerings include Sirloin Kats Set, Cheese Galbi Kats Set, Children\'s Kats Set, Ebi Curry Set, and Chashu Curry Set. The quality meat is carefully selected and fried to achieve a crispy exterior and moist interior. Additionally, you can enjoy a unique aroma and flavor of the pork cutlet with Andes salt, wasabi, and truffle oil, and have fun combining them according to your taste.','14, Sajeng-ro 57beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st Floor','- 11:00~21:00- Break time 15:00~17:00- Last order for lunch 14:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Tenderloin Kats Set / Sirloin Kats Set / Special Sirloin Kats Set / Cheese Galbi Kats Set, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1101,1124,'en','Hwangnam Milmyeon','Hwangnam Milmyeon is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The vintage atmosphere of the exterior and interior is striking. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature dishes are Hwangnam Perilla Milmyeon, characterized by a sweet and sour taste, and Hwangnam Yukhoe Milmyeon. The clean and refreshing Mul Myeon and Bibim Myeon are also popular menu items. Additionally, you can enjoy various dishes such as Jeju Black Pork Charcoal Grilled Meat and Spicy Raw Fish Salad. It is close to Gyeongju IC and surrounded by famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to visit.','12, Poseok-ro 1068beon-gil, Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam General Market, Room 75)','11:00~20:00 (Preparation time 15:30~16:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Hwangnam Perilla Milmyeon / Mul Myeon / Bibim Myeon / Hwangnam Yukhoe Milmyeon, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1102,1148,'en','Hwangpo Restaurant','Hwangpo Restaurant is located in Jeonchon-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and vintage atmosphere of the interior stand out. Inside, there are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu includes sashimi sets featuring various dishes, including raw fish. Additionally, you can enjoy braised hairtail, braised dorade, braised flounder, sashimi noodles, and mixed sashimi, with early closing in case of ingredient depletion. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC and nearby Gyeongju Munmu Daewang Tomb and Najung Goun Sand Beach.','2964 Gyeonggam-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Tuesday to Thursday 10:00~18:00 - Friday to Sunday 10:00~19:00 ※ Early closing when ingredients are exhausted',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 04:25:06','Sashimi set / Braised flounder / Braised hairtail / Sashimi noodles, etc.','Available Fee (Free)','Every Monday',NULL),(1103,1133,'en','Hulrimmok','Hulrimmok is a café located in Sajeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The traditional hanok exterior harmonizes with the sophisticated interior, and there are group seating areas suitable for various gatherings. Specializing in soufflés, it offers a variety of menus including plain soufflé, strawberry soufflé, tiramisu soufflé, strawberry tiramisu soufflé, and chocolate banana soufflé. Additionally, various coffee drinks such as Hulrimmok Coffee, Hulrimmok Latte, brewing coffee, and cold brew are also available. Seasonal menu items like milk bingsu and mango cheese bingsu can also be enjoyed. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to visit.','1061-9 Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Tiramisu Soufflé / Chocolate Banana Soufflé / Strawberry Soufflé / Hulrimmok Coffee, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1104,1175,'en','987 Pizza','987 Pizza is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been featured in various broadcasts, including SBS current affairs programs. The exterior is designed in Hanok style, exuding a vintage charm, while the interior is decorated in a sophisticated manner. The signature menu item is pepperoni pizza, and you can also enjoy various pizzas such as Hawaiian, jalapeño, and corn cheese. Additionally, fries and wing sticks are available. It is close to Gyeongju IC and surrounded by famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to visit.','26, Poseok-ro 1092beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Hwangnam-dong)','12:00~22:00 (Last order 21:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Pepperoni / Hawaiian / Jalapeño / Corn Cheese / Bulgogi, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1105,1129,'en','1894 Sarangchae','1894 Sarangchae is a Hanok cafe located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It utilizes a Hanok built in 1894, allowing visitors to experience its vintage charm, and the interior has a nostalgic atmosphere. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it a great place for various gatherings. The signature menu is the Snowflake Patbingsu, and the steamed buns with red bean filling are also popular. In addition, a variety of drinks and desserts such as Americano, vanilla ice cream, peach iced tea, and misutgaru can be enjoyed. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby famous tourist attractions include Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great spot to visit.','23, Poseok-ro 1068beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Weekdays]- 11:00~22:00 (Last order 21:00)[Weekends]- 10:00~22:00 (Last order 21:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Snowflake Patbingsu / Ginger Tea / Misutgaru / Steamed Red Bean Bun, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1106,1165,'en','Jeonghwa Songi Sundubu','Jeonghwa Songi Sundubu is located in Bukgundong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. This place has been in operation for over 30 years and has been featured in an SBS current affairs program. Built in a Hanok style, it exudes a vintage charm from its exterior. The clean atmosphere of the interior is also notable. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu item is the Songi Sundubu Jjigae, which is sold in limited quantities of 100 servings per day. Sundubu Jjigae and Clear Sundubu Jjigae are also very popular. Other offerings include Siraegi Soup, Sirloin Tofu Sweet and Sour Pork, Seafood Pancake, and Tofu Kimchi. It opens at 7 AM, making it perfect for breakfast on your travels. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex and Gyeongju Donggungwon.','5 Bukgun-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','07:00~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:13','2026-09-16 03:43:13','Songi Sundubu Jjigae / Sundubu Jjigae / Clear Sundubu Jjigae / Siraegi Soup, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1107,1118,'en','Jinmi Restaurant','Jinmi Restaurant is a traditional Korean cuisine restaurant located in Sajeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Featured on the MBC every1 entertainment program \'Delicious Map\', it offers a vintage atmosphere in a building constructed in Hanok style. The interior is decorated in a clean and tidy manner, with group seating available, making it suitable for family gatherings or various meetings. The signature menu item is the Bulgogi Wrap Rice Set, enjoyed with fresh wrap vegetables, along with various Korean dishes such as Seafood Pancake and Jeonbyeong. It is conveniently located near Gyeongju IC and close to major tourist attractions such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to enjoy both dining and sightseeing.','985 Poseok-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~20:00 (Last order 19:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Bulgogi Wrap Rice / Spicy Pork Wrap Rice / Seafood Soft Tofu / Seafood Pancake, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1108,1116,'en','Cheonnyeonae Hwangnam Branch','Cheonnyeonae Gyeongju Bread, Cheolbori Bread, and Cheolbori Rice Cake are specialty products located in Hwanglidangil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The building, constructed in a traditional Hanok style, exudes a vintage atmosphere, making it a popular spot for many visitors to purchase souvenirs during their trip to Gyeongju. The signature menu items are Cheolbori Bread and Cheolbori Rice Cake, made with 100% locally grown Cheolbori. Cheolbori is sown in mid-October each year and harvested in early June of the following year, characterized by its nutty flavor and chewy texture. It is a nutritious snack that embodies the regional characteristics of Gyeongju, which holds a thousand years of history and culture from the Silla Dynasty, and can be enjoyed by people of all ages, making it a popular choice for travel gifts or souvenirs.','67 Cheomseong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:00~20:00※ Limited quantity may sell out early, so please inquire by phone before visiting',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Cheolbori Rice Cake / Cheolbori Bread / Gyeongju Bread','Available (Free)','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1109,1166,'en','Cheongsan Hanwoo','Cheongsan Hanwoo is located in Wangsin-ri, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It has been featured in a KBS 2TV current affairs program. The clean exterior and old-fashioned atmosphere in its interior are notable. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu item is the rib meat served directly to customers. Other offerings include Salt Grilled Beef, Yukhoe, Beef Soup Rice, Cold Noodles, and Doenjang Jjigae. It is close to Gangdong IC and nearby attractions include the UNESCO World Heritage Site Gyeongju Yangdong Village and Oksan Seowon, making it easy to visit before or after meals.','938 Cheonggang-ro, Gangdong-myeon, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 10:30~21:00- Preparation time 14:00~16:00- Last order for lunch 14:00 / Last order for dinner 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Rib Meat / Salt Grilled Beef / Yukhoe / Beef Soup Rice, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1110,1127,'en','Cheong On Chae','Cheong On Chae is a Korean cuisine specialty restaurant located in Sajeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The Hanok exterior adds to its antique charm, and the clean atmosphere of the interior is also striking. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature dishes are Nurungji Soy Sauce Braised Short Ribs and Nurungji Spicy Braised Short Ribs, while Cheongdo Minari Yukhoe Bibimbap and Yukhoe Mulhoe are also popular. Additionally, you can enjoy a variety of dishes such as Cheese Potato Pancakes, Perilla Oil Buckwheat Noodles, and a plate of Yukhoe.','8-5, Poseok-ro 1079beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Monday~Thursday] - 11:00~20:30 (Preparation time 15:30~17:00) - Last order for lunch 15:00 / Last order for dinner 20:00 [Friday~Sunday] - 11:00~21:00 (Preparation time 15:30~17:00) - Last order for lunch 15:00 / Last order for dinner 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Nurungji Soy Sauce Braised Short Ribs / Cheongdo Minari Yukhoe Bibimbap / Perilla Oil Buckwheat Noodles / Cheese Potato Pancakes, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1111,1115,'en','Cafe Neung','Cafe Neung, located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, is built in a traditional Korean house, featuring a traditional exterior and a clean interior atmosphere. The signature menu is Vanilla Latte, and it offers a variety of coffee drinks including Iced Americano, Einspänner, Mocha Latte, Strawberry Milk, and Milk Tea. Desserts such as Pig Bar Cream Cheese Crumble are also available. It is close to Gyeongju IC and about a 15-minute walk from Gyeongju Intercity Bus Terminal, making it easily accessible. Nearby major tourist attractions include Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village.','3, Poseok-ro 1068beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:30~21:30 (Last order 21:00)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Vanilla Latte / Americano / Einspänner / Affogato / Pig Bar Cream Cheese Crumble, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1112,1117,'en','Taverna','Taverna is a French restaurant located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The building, remodeled from a Hanok, harmonizes a vintage exterior with modern interior design, allowing guests to enjoy meals in a special atmosphere that blends tradition and sophistication. The interior also features group seating, making it suitable for family gatherings or various meetings. Signature menu items include Crevettes en Fraîcheur, Brandade, and Foie Gras Terrine, showcasing authentic French cuisine with fresh ingredients and delicate cooking that delivers deep flavors. It is conveniently located near Gyeongju IC and close to major tourist attractions such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to enjoy both dining and sightseeing.','18 Cheomseong-ro 81beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:30~21:00- Last lunch order 14:30- Preparation time 15:00~17:00- Last dinner order 19:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Gyeongju Four Seasons Course / Soup Donong / Ratatouille / Magret de Canard, etc.','Not available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1113,1167,'en','Toham','Toham is located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a thatched house style, it exudes a vintage charm from its exterior. The interior also features a nostalgic atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu item is the Braised Hairtail Set, and the Braised Mackerel Set and Mountain Vegetable Set are also very popular. Other offerings include Pollack Jjigae, Mountain Vegetable Bibimbap, Pork Cutlet, Village Tofu Boiled Pork, and Assorted Grilled Fish. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex and Gyeongju Donggungwon.','159 Supmeori-gil (Bomun-dong), Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Braised Hairtail Set / Braised Mackerel Set / Assorted Grilled Fish / Mountain Vegetable Set, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1114,1130,'en','Poseokro Beef Short Rib Stew','Poseokro Beef Short Rib Stew is a Korean restaurant located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior built as a Hanok adds to its vintage charm, and the clean interior is also eye-catching. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Poseok Beef Short Rib Stew, and the Spicy Beef Short Rib Stew is also popular. Additionally, a variety of dishes such as Seafood Pancake, Chive Pancake, Pollock Roe Mayo Rice Ball, and Tuna Mayo Rice Ball can be enjoyed. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby famous tourist attractions include Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village.','22, Poseok-ro 1068beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','[Weekdays]- 10:30~21:00- Last order 20:30[Weekends]- 10:30~21:30- Preparation time 15:00~15:30- Last order 21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Poseok Beef Short Rib Stew / Spicy Beef Short Rib Stew / Seafood Pancake / King Rib Soup, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1115,1172,'en','From Sangrok','From Sangrok is a Hanok cafe located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern atmosphere of the exterior stands out, and the clean interior design is also impressive. The signature menu is cream puffs made fresh every morning. In addition, various beverages such as Americano, espresso, homemade strawberry latte, peach ade, matcha, and Earl Grey are available. The cafe operates as a no-kids zone, and pets are only allowed in the outdoor yard area. It is close to Gyeongju IC and famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to visit.','17-5, Poseok-ro 1068beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st Floor','11:00~21:00 (Last order 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Melting Almond / Shine Muscat Cream Puff / Gyeongju Fresh Strawberry Cream Puff / Custard Cream Puff, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1116,1171,'en','Stay 550','Stay 550 is a dessert cafe located on Hwanglidangil in Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The vintage exterior and exposed concrete interior are eye-catching. The signature menu item is strawberry cake, and a variety of high-quality fruit cakes are available. Additionally, there are various options including fruit bingsu and beverage menus. It is close to Gyeongju IC and surrounded by famous tourist attractions such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village.','56-1, Sajeong-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:30~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Strawberry Cake / Apple Mango Bingsu / Fresh Strawberry Juice / Americano, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1117,1160,'en','Spunk Coffee','Spunk Coffee is located in Hwang-o-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern exterior and clean interior create a striking atmosphere. The signature menu item is Americano. In addition, various food options such as Kale & Apple Salad, Baked Shrimp, and Chicken Layer are available. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and there are many famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju nearby, including Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village.','127 Imhae-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','08:00~17:00 (Last order 16:50)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Spunk Latte / Kale & Apple Salad / Bacon & Egg Sandwich / Spunk Layer, etc.','Available (Free)','Every Thursday',NULL),(1118,1168,'en','Seungjin Restaurant','Located in Gyeongju, Seungjin Restaurant is famous for its pork stir-fry with a slightly thick gochujang sauce. Originally a street food stall, it has expanded to its current form. It only serves pork stir-fry. The spicy broth topped with oyster mushrooms can be enjoyed with rice, and it\'s also great to have fried rice at the end.','22 Bihwa-dong-gil, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:30~21:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Pork Stir-fry / Fried Rice / Steamed Rice, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1119,1209,'en','Sigol Ssambap','Sigol Ssambap is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and nostalgic interior create a charming atmosphere. The signature menu is bulgogi ssambap, and the country-style ssambap is also very popular. Other offerings include yellow clay snail ssambap, soft tofu set meal, soybean paste stew set meal, pork cutlet, and galbitang. It opens early in the morning, making it a great spot for breakfast while traveling.','10 Gyerim-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- Monday to Friday 07:00~21:00- Saturday to Sunday 07:00~22:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Bulgogi ssambap / Country-style ssambap / Yellow clay snail ssambap / Soft tofu set meal / Soybean paste stew set meal / Pork cutlet, etc.','Available (Free)','Open year-round',NULL),(1120,1155,'en','Silla Noodle House','Silla Noodle House is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Hanok style, it exudes an antique charm from the outside. The clean and tidy interior is also noticeable. The signature menu features Silla Kalnakji, which combines stir-fried octopus and knife-cut noodles. Other offerings include Fresh Clam Knife-Cut Noodles, Potato Pancakes, Meat Dumplings, and Kimchi Dumplings. It is close to Gyeongju IC and surrounded by famous tourist attractions in Gyeongju, including Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyeongchon Hanok Village.','22-11, Cheomseong-ro 81beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~21:00 (Last order 20:20)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Silla Kalnakji / Potato Pancakes / Fresh Clam Knife-Cut Noodles / Meat King Dumplings, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1121,1208,'en','Sookbujangyi','Sookbujangyi is a Korean restaurant located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Hanok style, it exudes a vintage charm from the outside. The interior also features a nostalgic atmosphere. There are group seating arrangements available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu includes seasonal salad, soft tofu, potato pancakes, lotus root mushroom japchae, perilla seed mushroom soup, assorted fried dishes, lotus leaf rice, and soybean paste stew, all served as part of the lotus leaf rice set meal. Additionally, Sookbujangyi set meal, Seondeok table, and Wonhyo table are also available.','147-5 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~20:30- Preparation time 15:30~17:00- Last order 19:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Lotus leaf rice set / Sookbujangyi course / Guhjeolcho set / Lotus leaf rice set, etc.','Available (Free)','Every Wednesday / Lunar New Year and Chuseok',NULL),(1122,1207,'en','Arirang','Arirang is located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, North Gyeongsang Province. Built in a Hanok style, it exudes a vintage charm from its exterior. The interior also creates a nostalgic atmosphere. There is group seating available, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu consists of a chicken course meal featuring native chicken. Dishes such as chicken breast shabu-shabu, boiled chicken, and mung bean pancakes are served. It is close to Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include the Bomun Tourist Complex and Gyeongju Donggungwon.','197 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~20:00- Last order for lunch 14:00- Preparation time 15:00~17:00- Last order for dinner 19:00※ Operates by reservation, so please call before visiting',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Chicken Course','Available','Every Monday',NULL),(1123,1103,'en','AnGang Market','AnGang Market is located in Yangwol-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It is a medium-sized market established in 1923, and the market days are the 4th and 9th of every month. On market days, you can find fresh and clean agricultural products produced in AnGang and its surroundings, such as AnGang chamdan persimmons, peppers, sesame, garlic, and napa cabbage. Above all, you can purchase fresh seafood, salted fish, and various fish at reasonable prices. It is close to Gangdong IC, and nearby are the UNESCO World Heritage Site Gyeongju Yangdong Village and Historic Site No. 154 Oksan Seowon, making it easy to visit before or after meals.','1353-7 Yangwol-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','Varies by store',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14',NULL,'Available','Varies by store',NULL),(1124,259,'en','An-gang Halmae Goditang','An-gang Halmae Goditang is located in Hagok-ri, Angang-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior shows traces of time, giving it an emotional feel. The interior creates a clean atmosphere while being traditional. There are group seating arrangements inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. The representative menu is Goditang, which is boiled with freshwater snails, mugwort, and chives, offering a refreshing taste. Godibibimbap + soup and Godimuchim are also popular menu items. The side dishes that come with the food are also a delicacy, with over 10 types of side dishes available, including soybean leaves, pickled plums, and sea squirt. It opens early in the morning, making it perfect for a hearty breakfast on your travels.','2060 Hoguk-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','07:30~20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Goditang / Godibibimbap + soup / Godimuchim / Jeotgal, etc.','Available (Free)','Closed every Monday',NULL),(1125,1131,'en','Yangji Restaurant','Yangji Restaurant is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. It was featured in the SBS current affairs program. The clean exterior and vintage atmosphere of the interior are eye-catching. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is Bean Sprout Rice, which is mixed with rice, bean sprouts, carrots, green onions, enoki mushrooms, seaweed flakes, and seasoning. The green onion pancake, grilled to a golden brown with seafood such as squid, is also very popular.','30, Gyochon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 09:30~19:30- Break time 14:30~16:00- Last order 19:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Bean Sprout Bibimbap / Green Onion Pancake','Available','Every Wednesday / Lunar New Year’s Day',NULL),(1126,1134,'en','El Garden','El Garden is a café located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The modern exterior and sophisticated interior create a striking atmosphere. There are group seating areas inside, making it suitable for various gatherings. Outdoor seating is available for guests with pets. The signature menu item is fresh gold mango bingsu, and the snowflake bingsu is also very popular. Various desserts such as brown cheese croffle and plain croffle are offered. A variety of drinks made from freshly roasted beans, including Americano, are also available. It is close to Dong Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Seokguram, Bulguksa, and the nostalgic Dal-dong neighborhood. ※ Pets are allowed (please bring a leash and waste bags).','123 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:30~21:00 (Last order 21:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Carrot Rape Panini / Salad Pizza / Fresh Mango Bingsu / Mango Matcha Latte, etc.','Available','Every Tuesday',NULL),(1127,1135,'en','Yemion Hwanglidangil Branch','Yemion Hwanglidangil Branch is located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a hanok style, it exudes a vintage charm from the exterior. The clean and tidy interior is also notable. The signature menu items are savory beef pancakes made from thinly sliced Gyeongju Hanwoo and beef tartare bibimbap. Other offerings include beef tartare, cold bibim naengmyeon, and seasoned short rib bibimbap. Hwanglidangil is rich in food and attractions, with many cafes themed around hanok, and it is a great place to visit cultural heritage sites like Cheomseongdae and Daereungwon.','22-12 Cheomseong-ro 81beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do, 1st floor','- 11:00~21:00- Break time 15:30~17:00- Last order 20:30',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Beef Tartare Bibimbap / Cold Bibim Naengmyeon / Seasoned Short Rib Bibimbap / Short Rib Noodle Soup / Cockle Bibimbap, etc.','Available, use public parking lot','Open year-round ※ Closed days are announced on Instagram',NULL),(1128,1158,'en','Old Town Local Soft Tofu','Old Town Local Soft Tofu is a specialty tofu restaurant located in Bomun-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior, built in Hanok style, exudes a vintage charm. The interior creates a clean atmosphere and features group seating, making it suitable for various gatherings. The representative menu includes smoked duck tofu, and many people also visit for smoked pork belly tofu, whole smoked pork, and whole smoked duck. Meal options include local soft tofu stew, clear soft tofu stew, and mountain vegetable bibimbap. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby Bomun Tourist Complex and Donggung Palace.','132 Supmeori-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','09:30~20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Smoked Duck Tofu / Smoked Pork Belly Tofu / Whole Smoked Duck / Local Soft Tofu, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1129,1137,'en','Olive','Olive is a cafe located in Sajeong-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The building, constructed in a traditional Korean style, exudes a vintage atmosphere, and the neatly decorated interior space is also impressive. Inside, there are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is the vanilla cream latte, a drink topped with Olive\'s special cream that attracts many visitors. In addition, various desserts such as croissant sandwiches, fruit mix rolls, Dojima rolls, soufflé pancakes, fresh mango cake, and melon cake are available. In summer, you can enjoy traditional patbingsu and mango cheese bingsu, and there is a variety of drink options including Americano, cafe latte, vanilla latte, and orange grapefruit. Nearby, there are major tourist attractions in Gyeongju such as Cheomseongdae, the National Gyeongju Museum, and Gyeongju Gyochon Hanok Village, making it a great place to visit.','7-6, Sajeong-ro 57beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~21:00 (Last order 20:30)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Vanilla cream latte / croissant sandwich / fruit mix roll / affogato, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1130,1123,'en','Ujik','Ujik is a fusion Western restaurant located in Hwangnam-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Thanks to its hanok architecture, it gives off a vintage atmosphere from the outside, while the interior is decorated in a modern style, creating a comfortable ambiance. The signature menu is demiglace omelet served with homemade demiglace sauce. In addition, various menus such as mentaiko carbonara, shrimp oyster pasta, Neapolitan pasta, and assorted katsu are prepared.','8, Sajeong-ro 57beon-gil, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','- 11:00~21:00- Break time 15:30~17:00- Last order for lunch 14:30 / Last order for dinner 20:00',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Demiglace omelet / Mentaiko carbonara / Shrimp oyster pasta / Assorted katsu, etc.','Not available','Open year-round',NULL),(1131,1153,'en','Unsu Daetong','Unsu Daetong is located in Bukgung-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. Built in a traditional Hanok style, it exudes an antique charm from the outside. The clean and tidy interior is also noticeable. Inside, there are group seating arrangements, making it suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu features Hanwoo Jeon, the most tender part of beef. Other options include Flower Galbi, Marinated Galbi, and Anchangsal. Meal options include Hanwoo Tteokgalbi Set, Galbitang, Hanwoo Gomtang, and Hanwoo Gukbap. It is close to Gyeongju IC and nearby attractions include Bomun Tourist Complex and Donggungwon in Gyeongju.','132-5, Bomun-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','11:00~23:00 (Last order 21:40)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Hanwoo Jeon / Doenjang Sundubu / Hanwoo Galbi / Bibim Naengmyeon, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1132,1169,'en','Original Ganbaji Restaurant','Established in 1981, Original Ganbaji Restaurant is located in Yonggang-dong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The exterior shows signs of time, and the interior evokes memories of a street food stall. The signature dish is ganbaji, which is marinated pork grilled over charcoal. They also serve pork skin and soybean paste stew. It is close to Gyeongju IC and near the Bomun Tourist Complex and Donggung Palace.','2, 57 Beomeongang-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do (Yonggang-dong)','17:00~22:00 (Last order 21:15)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Ganbaji / Pork Skin / Soybean Paste Stew / Steamed Rice, etc.','Not available','Closed every Sunday',NULL),(1133,1119,'en','Nature Aegondeure','Nature Aegondeure is a traditional Korean cuisine restaurant located in Hadong, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The building, constructed in Hanok style, exudes a vintage charm, and the clean and tidy interior provides a comfortable dining space. The interior also features group seating, making it suitable for family gatherings or various meetings. The signature menu includes Gondeure Stone Pot Rice and Grilled Fish, served with a variety of side dishes, and the One-Person Set, which allows guests to enjoy Gondeure Stone Pot Rice and Stir-fried Pork together. Additionally, various traditional Korean meal sets such as the Premium Set, which includes Gondeure Stone Pot Rice and Braised Mackerel, are available. Guests can enjoy healthy Gondeure Rice and a carefully prepared Korean meal, making it popular among travelers. It is conveniently located near Dong Gyeongju IC, and nearby attractions include Bulguksa Temple, Seokguram Grotto, and the Memory of Dal-dong Village, making it a great place to visit.','147-6 Bobul-ro, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do','10:00~21:00 (Last order 20:20)',NULL,'2026-09-16 03:43:14','2026-09-16 03:43:14','Premium Set / One-Person Set / Genuine Set / Grilled Mackerel, etc.','Available','Open year-round',NULL),(1134,1138,'en','Jangteo Bapsang','Jangteo Bapsang is located in Jeonchon-ri, Gampo-eup, Gyeongju, Gyeongsangbuk-do. The clean exterior and luxurious atmosphere of the interior stand out. Inside, there are group seating arrangements suitable for various gatherings. The signature menu is the